135
00:31:21,290 --> 00:31:22,570
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Sorry sir, what's the last part?

136
00:31:22,710 --> 00:31:26,310
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Former AMLC. Former AMLC official, please tell us about that experience.

137
00:31:26,770 --> 00:31:42,130
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Objection, Your Honor. There's no basis yet. The witness has not testified that he was ever connected with the Anti-Money Laundering Council. We see that in the CV. But the witness has not identified the CV or attested to its truth, Your Honor.

138
00:31:42,390 --> 00:31:43,730
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Kindly reform, Attorney Mark.

139
00:31:45,110 --> 00:31:59,310
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright. We'll show you a copy of your own CV. Just so you can refer. It says in your CV that you are a former AMLC official. Can you please tell us more about that experience?

140
00:31:59,950 --> 00:32:13,490
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Okay, I entered the AMLC in 2015 as a financial investigator, proper designation bank officer 2. So I was assigned with the compliance and investigation group during that time.

141
00:32:13,500 --> 00:32:16,380
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: 2015 july 2015.

142
00:32:16,940 --> 00:32:21,220
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: All right. And what are your—what were your duties and responsibilities in relation to that role?

143
00:32:22,420 --> 00:32:43,940
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: uh well it's financial investigation we handle compliance matters financial investigation matters so any case referred to the council as part of the team that look into scrutinize check the data and produce reports that may be used by other

144
00:32:43,940 --> 00:32:49,310
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: agencies, law enforcement agencies and other agencies with investigative powers.

145
00:32:49,830 --> 00:32:58,810
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: You mentioned the term financial investigation. Can you describe your duties as far as you can and responsibilities as such as a financial investigator?

146
00:32:59,390 --> 00:33:29,010
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: We start first, Your Honor, with investigative sparks, investigative triggers. There are cases referred to us and these cases are then assigned. Ina-assign ito sa iba't ibang grupo within AMLC Secretariat. At kami yung gumagawa from scratch up until case build up until makapag-produce ng report, investigation or report that may be used.

147
00:33:30,530 --> 00:34:08,600
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Number one, tulungan ang ating mga law enforcement agencies sa pag-iimbestiga sa predicate crime. And number two, if meron ng predicate crime, mag-proceed yun sa pag-file ng kaso for money laundering. So, in a nutshell, doon humiikot yung aking duty previously with the AMLC and during that time kasi magkasama ang compliance and investigation. So, other than pag-iimbestiga, yung routine compliance checks sa mga ating covered persons ginagawa rin doon base sa aking function dati-dati sa sekretaryat.

148
00:34:09,820 --> 00:34:14,500
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: How would you describe or how extensive is your experience in financial investigation?

149
00:34:15,060 --> 00:34:30,660
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Well, from 2015 to 2018, during that time, very small pa lang ho ang sekretariat so we really multitask. Lahat ho ng pwedeng iba tong trabaho, hindi ho namin pwedeng hindian yan. So ginagawa ho namin lahat.

150
00:34:31,920 --> 00:34:37,460
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Matanong ko lang po very quickly, kaya po ba gawin in two weeks ang isang extensive financial investigation?

151
00:34:38,310 --> 00:34:49,090
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Two weeks? Kaya, pero mahirap po. If we would be very realistic, kaya, pero sobrang hirap po yan.

152
00:34:49,330 --> 00:35:06,890
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Okay. We'll leave it at that, no? Kasi yung ibang so-called expert, two weeks lang. Now, let's move on. By the way, dito po sa profile nyo, napansin ko rin po na there's this term AML, CFT, and CPF compliance. Can you explain to us what these are?

153
00:35:07,210 --> 00:35:44,630
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Okay. Ang anti-money laundering kasi ngayon hindi lang sa isa. Tatlo na sila. Mayroon ng terrorist financing at saka financing, rather, proliferation of weapons of mass destruction. So tatlo na yan. You cannot discuss money laundering without touching upon the topic on terrorism financing and proliferation of weapons of mass destruction. So magkakasama na yung tatlo na yan. Paggamit ng ating financial system, in order to mask yung illicit sources of money. So yan ho ang mundo. So it concerns financial crimes.

154
00:35:45,400 --> 00:35:52,320
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright. How about this, you have also a role on regulatory advisory. Can you share your experience in this?

155
00:35:52,940 --> 00:37:30,820
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Okay. When I left the public service po, ako ay pumunta sa private sector. I started a law firm with a friend and then later on, I branched out and started my own. 2021. That is AML Consulting PH. So aside from the private sector clients, I was also tapped by other government agencies as their AML consultant. Based on my competence and experience, tinulungan natin sila how to draft their own supervisory framework, how they will be governing their covered persons. So maganda ho kasi meron ang aking eksperyensya sa gobyerno dati na mix ko ho with my first-hand experience sa mga covered persons, private sector. So nakita ko ho kung saan nahihirapan ang ating private sector at napapaintindi ho natin sa kanila kung saan ang gagaling yung sa gobyerno. Bakit naghihigpit ang gobyerno? So sabi ko we have to be sa middle. We comply with the international standards but also we don't, for lack of better term, pahirapan itong ating private sector. So yung aking naging role, advisory lamang po, recommendatory. The ultimate decision maker are still kung sino yung head of the agency. So yan yung aking regulatory compliance work. We advise government agencies how to craft properly yung kanilang AML policy so that it is realistic. Hindi lang siya theoretical.

156
00:37:31,320 --> 00:37:31,980
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: All right.

157
00:37:32,100 --> 00:37:47,320
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: With the permission of Attorney Mark and Attorney Rainer, continuing authority is given to assisting counsels to approach the witness at any point in time. And no further authorization need be given by the court nor the presiding officer. You may continue, Attorney Mark.

158
00:37:47,320 --> 00:37:54,280
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Thank you, Your Honor. You also have experience as an accredited trainer for the AMLC. Please tell us more about that.

159
00:37:54,280 --> 00:39:02,420
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Again, I left the service in 2018. I had a one-year self-imposed bar na hindi ako nag-practice ng anything related to AML. So 2019, after one year, I applied for accreditation. I was one of the first three accredited trainers. So diyan ko sinimulan yung aking firm, training lamang. Hindi ko nga alam kung ito ay magpaprosper o hindi. So from time, yung aking mga nagiging estudyante, na niwala naman sila sa akin. So unti-unti dun ko na-build. Yung aking client base. They tapped me as their consultant. Kung ano yung tinuturo mo, sabi nila, tulungan mo kami how to craft our AML policies. So doon ho nag-expand yung aking practice. So dati-dati ho, mag-isa lang ako sa opisina. Ngayon ho, kahit papaano, meron na ho tayong mga team of lawyers, paralegals that do assist me in this kind of work. So from training, 2019, yan ho, hanggang ngayon ay tuloy-tuloy ko ho yung ginagawa. So covered persons, bangko, Real Estate, lahat ng tinatawag nating covered persons, we do provide training sa kanila.

160
00:39:03,370 --> 00:39:21,510
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright, you also mentioned that you have your own consulting firm and according to your profile, you are the founder and lead counsel of AML Consulting PH. Can you tell us when this was organized and can you tell us your duties and responsibilities for this organization?

161
00:39:22,070 --> 00:40:27,990
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Okay, yung AML Consulting PH, again, I started this 2021. Again, the focus po nito ay more, again, training, compliance work, and research. Our core, ano po namin sa training, again, later on, those that attended my sessions, they do tap yung ating hong opisina para kanila maging consultant kasi ito ay medyo technical. So they need assistance. Tinutulungan natin sila to craft their own MTPP, yung kanilang money laundering and terrorist financing prevention program, institutional risk assessment, post-registration compliance work. So ito, again, on the side lang kami, advisory. The ultimate decision maker remains the covered person. So ito ang ginagawa namin day in and day out. Sa dami ng ating covered persons, in my own way, nasa private sector, Masaya rin ako kasi natutulungan ko rin yung aking mga dating kasamahan sa AMLC. Tinuturuan natin ng tama, hindi tinuturuan ng mali yung mga covered persons.

162
00:40:28,650 --> 00:40:37,730
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright. You mentioned that you also work for the BIR or the Bureau of Internal Revenue. Can you share with us that experience as well?

163
00:40:38,030 --> 00:41:14,500
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Okay. Your Honor, noong 2009 to 2010, For at least one year, I worked with Revenue Region 6, BIR Manila, as a revenue officer. So, I was part of the assessment group. So, we review tax dockets na inaakyat po sa Revenue Region 6, Manila. So, pagre-review ng mga assessments, lahat po ng taxes, business taxes, income taxes, before... I-close yung case or pag may kulang pa, binabalik ko namin sa mga revenue district offices or sa RDOs.

164
00:41:15,690 --> 00:41:25,070
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright, you also mentioned governance commission for government-owned and controlled corporations. This is under the office of the President, correct?

165
00:41:25,330 --> 00:41:25,890
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor.

166
00:41:26,110 --> 00:41:33,770
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: And can you tell us your experience on this? What were your duties and experience, your responsibilities, as well as knowledge and trainings that you gained?

167
00:41:34,250 --> 00:41:35,890
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Okay, so for this one, Your Honor,

168
00:41:37,820 --> 00:41:58,360
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: 2012. I entered this commission as a financial analyst and then later on I was transferred to the transportation and infrastructure sector. So lahat ito, mga GOCCs na nandoon sa sector na iyon, in-evaluate po namin ang kanyang financials. Kailangan bang itong i-rationalize?

169
00:41:58,500 --> 00:42:19,180
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: i-close, i-dissolve yung mga korporasyon na ito? Kami yung gumagawa ng analysis and we give recommendations sa aming commissioners as to what are our findings and ano yung mga recommendations para matulungan yung ating gobyerno, lalo na sa mga GOCCs na hindi na based on their mandate.

170
00:42:19,420 --> 00:42:29,160
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: You were also an accredited trainer for the Philippine Amusement and Gaming Corporation or PAGCOR. Can you please tell us more about that?

171
00:42:29,600 --> 00:42:53,810
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: After getting my 2019 accreditation from the AMLC, nagkaroon ko ng accreditation process ang PAGCOR for the casino sector. So I was fortunate enough to be the first accredited AML trainer for the casino sector. So as far as I can remember, around 2022 or 2023.

172
00:42:54,500 --> 00:42:56,280
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: And what were your duties and responsibilities?

173
00:42:56,900 --> 00:43:21,920
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yung ating mga PAGCOR covered entities, casinos, land-based and internet-based casinos, they are required to undergo training. Again, we expect them to have these AML measures in place for the board and the frontliners to, again, properly implement it. They need proper training. So ito ang ating nagiging role. During that time, I think,

174
00:43:23,790 --> 00:43:38,330
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Marami ho kasi sila. So, in a way, it is being outsourced by PAGCOR to us through an accreditation process. So, I took the chance po of having this to complement my AMLC accreditation.

175
00:43:38,730 --> 00:43:50,830
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright. You also have experience as an independent consultant at the AML Research Center Asia Pacific or RCAP Incorporated. Please tell us more about your role in that organization.

176
00:43:51,470 --> 00:44:54,000
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Ito ang AML Research Center Asia-Pacific. This is an independent research firm. We registered this here in the Philippines. Hindi ako technically kasama sa grupo na ito. Ang purpose nito, kasi lumalaki na ang practice, is to detach it from AML consulting and have it dito sa research center na ito. More on collaborating. With other international bodies. Kasi over the years, I noticed na nare-recognize na rin ang Pilipinas pagdating sa AML matters. So nakakatawa nga po, mayroon na mga US-based fintech companies that do contact us asking for independent AML. Compliance Testing. So to delineate yung role domestic sa international, ito yung research center for this one and I am also designated here as a senior technical official po.

177
00:44:54,680 --> 00:45:04,520
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright, you mentioned yung independent consultant. Matanong ko lang sir, kapag sinabi po bang independent, do you weigh both sides or just focus on one side?

178
00:45:05,740 --> 00:45:26,340
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: I think you don't take sides po. That will destroy your independence. So your findings might go against the institution that engage you. So you're only answerable dun sa standards that you apply as a consultant.

179
00:45:26,720 --> 00:45:31,160
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Bakit po? Pag-focus po ba kayo sa one side, ano po bang effect dun sa independence niyo?

180
00:45:31,340 --> 00:45:33,540
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Well, again, there are biases.

181
00:45:33,540 --> 00:45:45,160
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: It obscures your overview from the start. So again, it derails your work. There is a bias.

182
00:45:45,360 --> 00:45:56,040
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: You also have experience as a former consultant for CEZA. Para lang po alam ng lahat ano po ba tong CEZA and what were your duties and responsibilities dito?

