00:49:00,490 --> 00:49:01,630
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: The point you decide to.

203
00:49:02,290 --> 00:49:03,750
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Very well, Your Honor. Can

204
00:49:03,750 --> 00:49:04,490
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: we just move on?

205
00:49:06,490 --> 00:49:31,110
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: To abbreviate the proceedings, Honorable Chel, that Attorney Rainer is qualified as an expert by the counsel for respondent, Attorney Mark, only means that he can give his opinion. Not that it's gospel truth, not that it's the truth, not that it's accurate, not that it's correct, but only to allow the witness to give his opinion if he's qualified as an expert.

206
00:49:33,500 --> 00:50:13,110
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: He will be testifying to giving his opinion on documents identified, AMLC documents identified, presented, offered, and allowed by this court. So, in the interest of abbreviating the proceedings, again, subject to cross, of course, as regards the depth of his expertise. It will only, qualifying attorney Rainer as an expert will merely Enable him to give his opinion. Not that it's correct, again, not that we agree with it, not that it's legal, not that it's accurate, but only to give his opinion. As opposed to an ordinary witness that's not allowed to give his opinion.

