222
00:52:18,430 --> 00:52:31,650
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright. Let's move on. Sorry for that interruption, Attorney Dela Fuente. You also worked for APECO. Can you tell us more about APECO and your duties and responsibilities with this organization?

223
00:52:32,050 --> 00:53:02,680
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: For APECO, your honor, Aurora Pacific Economic Zone Authority, same with CEZA. They have the same requirement during that time, crafting their supervisory framework, helping them how to perform their function, forming their own AML department. So, yan ang aking naging role sa kanila, setting up their AML group. So, I think it's for only one year or one and a half year lang po.

224
00:53:02,860 --> 00:53:14,580
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright. By the way, what other accountancy associations or institutions are you affiliated with? And what are your roles and positions in these associations or institutions, if any?

225
00:53:16,010 --> 00:53:42,690
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: As a CPA, we're part of the Philippine Institute of Certified Public Accountants. And from time to time, when I ventured into AML practice, they do invite me as their resource speaker or subject matter expert for AML. Kasi ang profession ng CPAs ngayon, covered na rin ng AMLA. So pagdating sa ganitong mga sessions, ako ang nagpa-facilitate.

226
00:53:43,290 --> 00:53:53,790
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright. What other law-related associations or institutions are you affiliated with and what are your roles and positions in such associations or institutions, if any?

227
00:53:54,090 --> 00:54:38,730
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Currently, Your Honor, sa IBP. I have yet to be invited by IBP for AML-related trainings. But other associations, yung ating mga covered persons. Sa mga banko, RBAP, Rural Bankers Association of the Philippines, they have invited me to speak before them for AML matters. Association po ng mga non-bank financial institutions, yung PAFERA, Philippine Association for Foreign Exchange Dealers and Remittance Agents. Sa real estate din ho, yung SHDA, Subdivision in Housing Development Association. So they do top me as their resource speaker pagdating sa mga ganitong AML matters.

228
00:54:39,330 --> 00:54:49,270
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright. Marami na po tayong na-discuss na roles niyo sa education and professional experience as well. But what awards and citations can you share with us, if any?

229
00:54:49,810 --> 00:55:20,990
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Well, individual awards, Your Honor. Wala ho. Kasi nung ako ay nasa gobyerno na Agency-based awards. But when I ventured into private sector, again, ito kung when they do invite me as their resource speaker, Arbap, Seda, local and international, those recognitions ang binavalyo ko po the most. So it's not the trophies but the recognition about my competence and experience that what matters to me po.

230
00:55:21,250 --> 00:55:29,750
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright, thank you for that. Meron pa po ba kayong any significant role or na hindi pa natin natalakay? Or any organization that you are part of?

231
00:55:29,890 --> 00:55:31,390
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: More or less, yun na po yun.

232
00:55:31,470 --> 00:56:26,790
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: More or less, Your Honor, yun na po. Lately, dun 2025 po, I was invited by an international organization, a non-profit organization, Traffic International, to help them in coming up with a paper. Using financial investigation in tackling illegal wildlife trade or environmental crimes. So it started with a research paper and then later on that research paper, naging libro po and we use it to train law enforcement agencies here in the Philippines and also the private sector to combat illegal wildlife trade. So nung hung nag-start siya 2024, 2025, we did a trading caravan and this year po. Meron kami noong April and next week meron kami noong November. So it will involve the public and private sector.

