649
03:46:11,870 --> 03:47:00,940
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: I think this was discussed before, Honorable Chel, and as pointed out too by one of the Senator judges, if not the Presiding Officer himself, on the phrase, participating in business, as opposed to merely having a conflict of interest. That the court took of record, took of note, that previous presidents, in fact not only President BBM, previous presidents wrote business interests in their salon without similar microscopic investigations being conducted against them, beginning for that matter. From former President Corazon Aquino, who I believe listed the most number of corporations that she was a part of at that time. So the court will allow it.

650
03:47:02,470 --> 03:47:11,670
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: If you know, Attorney Rainer, when you conduct your financial investigations, any comment on this portion, business interests and financial interests?

651
03:47:11,670 --> 03:47:43,180
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Well, in this case, Your Honor, as a financial investigator, I will only take note of this business interest. There's nothing adverse. With this disclosure. We'll take note of this information and if later on we stumbled upon another data that might elicit linking with these entities, business interests, then we'll use that. But as far as I can remember, this is a harmless information.

652
03:47:44,660 --> 03:47:50,260
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright, thank you. One more aspect on the SALN. Let us go through

