664
03:50:48,290 --> 03:51:13,550
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright, kasi yung pinag-uusapan natin dito, wala pa sa kalahati ng increase. But let me ask you about one more public official. Just to complete the picture, this is a SALN of then Vice President Lenny Robredo. Can you show the name? Maria Leonor Robredo. Can you go to that one portion lang? On the financial and business interests. Let's just see kung meron.

665
03:51:15,310 --> 03:51:16,730
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Meron din siya, Meralco.

666
03:51:18,900 --> 03:51:26,990
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Any comment on this? If you know lang, how you use these types of information in your financial investigation?

667
03:51:27,450 --> 03:51:40,250
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Again, a typical financial investigator would just take note of this information. It's harmless as it is. So later na lang po, if they stumble upon information regarding that, and then they will correlate it.

668
03:51:40,920 --> 03:52:36,500
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright, thank you. Let's move on. Let me direct your attention to page 21 of the so-called expert report. Paragraph 4. VP Sara and spouse have undeclared income from their business interests. It says here, and I read, can you flash that? It says there, a vice president is not allowed to have business interests. This prohibition is not only provided by ordinary law or government policy. The 1987 Constitution itself strictly prohibits the VP. From directly or indirectly participating in any business. Now, without assuming po that this so-called expert's interpretation is correct, how similar or different does the prohibition against the vice president to the prohibition against the president, members of the cabinet, and their deputies or assistants?

669
03:52:37,830 --> 03:52:42,670
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: May limited knowledge po of our constitutional law. It is uniformly applied.

670
03:52:43,070 --> 03:52:55,690
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Uniformly applied. And what special treatment po does the law have? In favor of the President, members of the Cabinet, and their deputies or assistants in relation to this provision. Kung meron man po.

671
03:52:56,890 --> 03:53:02,830
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Again, Your Honor, my personal appreciation of our constitutional law, it applies equally to all.

672
03:53:03,070 --> 03:53:13,990
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright. Now, one last point on SALN. Since we don't want to disclose any confidential information, Attorney De La Fuente, I'll give you a scenario and ask you several questions thereafter.

673
03:53:16,750 --> 03:53:42,350
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: I'll use a visual. So, there's a public official wife and he's married to a private citizen husband. And the public official wife has been in public office since 2007 up to the present, save for three years. Now, the public official wife filed SALNs for those 19 years, save for the three years. Parang ganito po yung finial na SALN.

674
03:53:44,950 --> 03:53:58,590
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: So, noong 2007, meron po siyang finial na 7 million. Around 7 million pesos. And then ang combined net worth nila, 19 years later, almost 20 years later, is 94 million.

675
03:54:01,170 --> 03:54:47,280
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Nakakasunod po kayo dun sa senaryo ko. So 94 million na po sila. So ang growth po in 19 years is around nandun. 86.9 million pesos. Now if you look at the pertinent ITRs of this couple, the grand total of combined income for which proper taxes were paid, was also around 86 million, 86.7. So ang difference po nila after 20 years is a measly 150,000 pesos. Kaya po, based sa senaryo po na ito as a financial investigator, what does it mean po that the lawful income for which proper taxes were paid matches or is proportionate with what is indicated in the SALN?

676
03:54:48,660 --> 03:55:22,570
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Given this hypothetical scenario, Your Honor, It weakens the argument that there is unexplained income, unexplained figures. Since the materiality of the difference. But again, ito ay base lamang dito sa hypothetical scenario na ito. But I would suggest a further inquiry, a further assessment in order for us exhaust everything. This will be a full-blown investigation.

677
03:55:23,050 --> 03:55:33,030
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Thank you po for that answer. Now let me direct your attention to the so-called expert's conclusion about unexplained wealth as contained in Table 39.

678
03:55:35,970 --> 03:56:13,640
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Meron pong ano dito, seven columns. Year. And then doon po sa fifth and sixth column, nakalagay po doon, and I'll read. Total computed undeclared income from Cali88 and Metro City. And yung sixth column po, total computed undeclared income from GenCorp. So huwag niyo na po masyadong pansinin yung mga figures to kasi conjectures lang naman yan. But let me first ask you, how should the personality of corporations be distinguished from the personality of the individuals affiliated with them?

679
03:56:14,120 --> 03:56:25,840
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Your Honor, I move to strike that portion of the question that refers to conjectures. That is an opinion on the part of the defense counsel and has no place in a direct examination question.

680
03:56:26,520 --> 03:56:43,440
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Let's just replace the opinion of the supposed expert with conjecture. Let that be reflected in the record. Witness may answer.

681
03:56:44,600 --> 03:56:59,200
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Ang question ko naman, Atty. Dela Fuente, in terms of the personality. So, how should the personality of corporations, kasi may binanggit dito na corporations, be distinguished from the personality of the individuals affiliated with them, if at all?

682
03:57:00,650 --> 03:57:08,750
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Under our revised corporation code, Your Honor, I think it's basic principle that there is a separate and distinct personality of the corporation over the shareholders.

683
03:57:09,450 --> 03:57:17,080
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: And how should the income of corporations be distinguished from the income of individuals affiliated to them, if at all?

684
03:57:17,080 --> 03:57:26,880
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: As a rule, Your Honor, we abide with the doctrine of separate juridical personalities, separate personalities. So it's separate from the individuals composing the corporation.

685
03:57:27,410 --> 03:57:59,330
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Okay, thank you. Let's go to another point, yung piercing the veil of corporate fiction po. Dito po kasi sa ginawang ng so-called expert ng prosecution, And I hope this is not become the gospel truth. But he imputed fraud and pierced the veil of corporate fiction. So my question is this, based on your knowledge as a financial investigation, who has the authority to pierce the veil of corporate fiction? If you know.

686
03:58:00,040 --> 03:58:22,480
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Under our revised corporation code, Your Honor, piercing the veil of corporate fiction lies with the court. There should be a judicial declaration first, judicial determination, and it should be made after due process. So there must be proper notice and hearing.

687
03:58:22,480 --> 03:58:43,410
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: All right. So court pala hindi yung so-called expert ang gumagawa ng piercing the corporate veil. Pero paano po kung yung so-called forensic expert lang yung gumawa and based on this alleged piercing the veil. He came up with figures in his report. My question is, what is the reliability of that kind of methodology?

688
03:58:44,850 --> 03:58:56,860
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Again, Your Honor, I did not read entirely the report as to its reliability. I cannot testify on that.

689
03:58:57,680 --> 03:58:59,000
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: In general?

690
03:58:59,240 --> 03:59:15,470
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: In general, well, it has an adverse effect on the... Reliability. It questions the assumptions made. It puts, na ano yan, nagkakaroon ng duda doon sa mga assumptions at computations made.

691
03:59:15,850 --> 03:59:27,510
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Okay, thank you po. Sorry, medyo tinetest ko na po yung corporate law knowledge nyo but naalala nyo po ba what are the proper grounds for very briefly lang po, grounds for piercing the corporate veil?

692
03:59:28,010 --> 03:59:43,920
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Normally, Your Honor, if it is to defeat public purpose, commission of fraud, Alter ego. The corporation is used as an alter ego or business conduit. So, those three are the grounds to pierce the veil.

693
03:59:44,160 --> 03:59:53,560
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: And one more question on this. How precise po ba should the determination be in terms of the grounds before you pierce the corporate veil?

694
03:59:54,100 --> 03:59:56,960
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Kailangan ho may court judicial determination.

695
03:59:57,760 --> 04:00:19,890
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Thank you po. Now, as a final... As a financial investigator, kung di naman pala tama yung piercing the corporate veil, and that is the premise of my question, what is the propriety of attributing gross revenue of a corporation or percentage thereof to any individual affiliated to it based on percentage of ownership, for example?

696
04:00:21,480 --> 04:00:25,600
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Well, gross revenues, Your Honor.

697
04:00:25,740 --> 04:00:30,730
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: or percentage thereof i-attribute dun sa individual affiliated to it kung wala namang proper piercing.

698
04:00:31,070 --> 04:00:36,720
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: It should be separated. Dapat po magkahiwalay pa rin yan. At hindi nilalump together.

699
04:00:37,100 --> 04:00:49,220
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright. So sa madaling salita po, kung wala pong proper piercing of the corporate veil, ano po yung dapat i-attribute na kita ng corporation doon sa affiliated na individual kung meron man?

700
04:00:50,320 --> 04:00:52,360
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Dapat po. Ito ay magkahiwalay pa rin.

701
04:00:52,590 --> 04:01:08,870
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Okay, thank you po. Now to be more vivid lang po, no? Kung wala pong proper piercing of the corporate veil ng Cale88, ano po yung dapat i-attribute na kita sa affiliated na individual tulad nila VP Sara at Atty. Mans?

702
04:01:09,640 --> 04:01:14,260
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yung dividendo kung maaari nilang matanggap, yun lamang po.

703
04:01:14,480 --> 04:01:19,430
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright. Kung walang proper piercing po ng Metro City, ganun din po?

704
04:01:20,520 --> 04:01:25,460
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Ganoon din po. Hindi po dapat i-attribute yun sa mga individuals. Separate pa rin po dapat siya.

705
04:01:25,500 --> 04:01:35,480
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: And then kung wala pong proper piercing of the corporate veil ng GenCorp, ano po yung mga dapat i-attribute na kita sa affiliated na individual na sina VP Sara at Atty. Mans? Kung meron man.

706
04:01:35,960 --> 04:01:39,340
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Kung meron man sila matanggap na dividendo o sweldo, yun lamang po.

707
04:01:39,520 --> 04:01:52,220
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright. Now, dito sa last column po ng so-called expert report. Which is quite inaccurate. May column and we will demonstrate that through this question. May total undeclared daw.

708
04:01:53,880 --> 04:02:23,810
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Pero kung mapapansin nyo, in-add lang naman. In-add lang naman yung assumed undeclaration per year from 2022 to 2025. Kaya po umabot ng 800 plus million. Now, my only question is this. Kung yung figures po kanina, kasi ito sabi niyo kanina eh, hindi naman attributable yan. If the figures used are inaccurate or not based on actual data, how reliable are the findings? Kung ganun po yung methodology na ginamit.

709
04:02:24,290 --> 04:02:35,590
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Objection, Your Honor, to the use of the phrase quite inaccurate. That's the lawyer testifying, not the witness. The witness has not said anything about any inaccuracies in the report of Atty. Cabrera.

710
04:02:36,210 --> 04:02:42,650
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Anyway, Your Honor, the question may be answered in general terms. My only question is how reliable are the findings?

711
04:02:42,970 --> 04:02:48,990
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Kindly reform, let that stay on the record. How reliable would the findings be if that is the methodology?

712
04:02:49,990 --> 04:02:52,050
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: For this, Your Honor, it would,

713
04:02:52,150 --> 04:02:52,730
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: again,

714
04:02:52,890 --> 04:03:04,450
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: depend on the discretion, the wisdom, application of wisdom ng ating Senate Impeachment Court. As to how, if this is reliable or not, I really leave it to the wisdom.

715
04:03:08,910 --> 04:03:17,190
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: I'll reform the question. If the figures are not based on actual data and then totaled, how reliable is the total?

716
04:03:18,730 --> 04:03:21,070
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Well, it weakens the reliability, Your Honor.

717
04:03:21,840 --> 04:04:22,640
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright, thank you. Let's proceed. Let me direct your attention to page 10 of the so-called expert report. Let me read that for you. To arrive at the calculated... Capital contribution of GenCorp. We confirm through inspection of official receipts the existence of five Jollibee branches in Centerpoint, Davao, Abriza Mall, Bolton, Davao, Gaysano Mall, and Times Square Plaza Corner, all bearing the name of GenCorp Industries, Inc. Refer to Annex C for the inspected receipts. I'll ask about the methodology used, attorney. It appears kasi na itong so-called expert na ito wanted to prove that certain branches of Jollibee belong to a corporation named GenCorp. So naisip niyang paraan ay kumain sa Jollibee branches at tingnan yung mga resibo. I'm not making this up. Let me illustrate. Kindly take a look at page 43 of the so-called expert report. Can you zoom in?

718
04:04:26,860 --> 04:04:38,240
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Sa resibo, nakalagay GenCorp Industries, tapos nakalagay yung branch. This was in Centerpoint. Centerpoint Plaza. Let's go to page 44 of the report.

719
04:04:40,320 --> 04:04:52,350
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Ito. So, yun ulit. GenCorp Industries, and then nilagay niyo yung branch. Bolton. Bolton Street. Okay. Page 45.

720
04:04:54,920 --> 04:05:04,910
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Yan. So, nakalagay ulit doon GenCorp. And then, nakalagay naman Abrizamol. Ito namang receipt na ito, walang duda galing Jollibee ito talaga. Kasi may

721
04:05:04,910 --> 04:05:07,730
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: marka pa ng gravy yung isang resibo.

722
04:05:07,910 --> 04:05:15,350
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Ayan. So, ito lang yata yung expert report na may gravy. But let's move on to page 46.

723
04:05:18,630 --> 04:05:29,200
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Davao City, yan. So, GenCorp ulit, Jollibee Corporation, Gaisano Mall. And then finally, for the fifth receipt, 47.

724
04:05:31,390 --> 04:05:51,260
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Jollibee, under GenCorp ulit, tapos ibang branch naman, Times Square. So, again, between this type of methodology, this is my only question from this so-called expert, and simply verifying information with the duly authorized representative of the corporation itself, which is, in this case, GenCorp, which is more reliable.

725
04:05:52,090 --> 04:06:37,870
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: If your honor, please. I'm sorry to interrupt the good counsel and the witness. But it would appear that this line of questioning is going beyond the offer of testimony of this witness. He was presented and his testimony was offered to prove fundamental anti-money laundering concepts. But now he is talking about a financial investigation into not money laundering but unexplained wealth. And he has no expertise insofar as that subject matter is concerned. He has neither been offered nor has he testified to having any credentials insofar as investigating unexplained wealth, salary and non-declarations, and participation in business interests are concerned.

726
04:06:38,610 --> 04:07:00,870
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: The chair will grant some latitude, counsel, and this can fall under in his general offer, the third or fourth offer if I'm not mistaken. And we'll allow the question. This, I guess... would be their part of their counter to your expert witness, Honorable Chel, and we'll allow it.

727
04:07:00,970 --> 04:07:01,490
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Thank you, Your Honor.

728
04:07:01,690 --> 04:07:02,770
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Attorney Mark, you may proceed.

729
04:07:03,010 --> 04:07:14,670
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Yung methodology lang po na ganun eh, between doing that, what I demonstrated, and verifying information with the corporations involved, which is more reliable in financial investigations?

730
04:07:15,850 --> 04:07:28,640
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Actually, Your Honor, napapakunot ako ng noo kanina dun sa placebo. I don't see the... Again, we don't do this sa financial investigation. It can be verified by official SEC documents.

731
04:07:30,470 --> 04:07:59,200
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: It is more in terms of reliability. It is more official. Again, right now, very ano na ho ang AI. Madaling mabago yung mga ganon. I'm not talking about that specific piece of, yung ating hong na-flash sa screen. But we have this reality, so the best evidence to obtain are those documents emanating from a government agency, certified true copies, etc.

732
04:07:59,680 --> 04:08:03,980
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Sorry, hindi ko lang po narinig yung unang part napapa... ano'ng sabi niyo, napapakunot?

733
04:08:06,200 --> 04:08:07,580
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor.

734
04:08:07,740 --> 04:09:57,240
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Okay. Let me direct your attention to pages 10 to 11 of the so-called expert report. Let me read. Desktop research from Jollibee's official website show an initial franchise cost to be at least 35 million to 55 billion per store. Conservatively, assigning a 35 million value to each of the five different branches, a total of at least 175 million capital should be invested. To operate these five branches, rent for the store venue, and working capital requirements for salaries of the manager and crew, as well as initial inventory costs should be, among others, be added. Nonetheless, for purposes of attributing the 20% capital of the respondent, we simply use the absolute minimum amount of 35 million. The equivalent of one of five stores. The capital investments should discuss above constitute equity investments that should form part of the couple's personal properties and should have been disclosed in the SALN. However, a review of the SALNs revealed no corresponding declarations of their equity in these assets. My question is this, we learned from GenCorp representative na hindi naman nagbayad ng 35 million each for each franchise kasi renewal of old franchises lang naman ang ginawa ng GenCorp. So in that case, what is the propriety of attributing 20% of an unverified value of 35 million and declaring it as unexplained wealth?

735
04:09:58,330 --> 04:10:28,820
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Again, Your Honor, I have no personal knowledge as to the methodology, how they Applied the techniques dito sa forensic examination report. But looking at this, it should have been complemented by other, not just desktop work or off-site work. There should be what natawag nating on-site. Meron hung iba pang investigation techniques that should have complemented this report nung ito pong naka-flash ngayon sa ating screen.

736
04:10:29,380 --> 04:10:35,540
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Thank you po. I'm glad you mentioned the term desktop research. What do you understand of the term desktop research?

737
04:10:36,120 --> 04:10:58,390
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: We also term it as off-site desk review lang po. Paper review. So, different po siya sa field work. Meron kayong on-site. Meron kayong walkthroughs. You interview, nakikita din nyo, nakakausap din nyo ang mga witnesses. You verify kung ano yung nakita nyo sa inyong desktop review with that on-site review.

738
04:10:58,800 --> 04:11:04,040
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright, what trainings or seminars po ba does one need to become an expert in desktop research?

739
04:11:05,230 --> 04:11:29,900
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Well, yan ho ay nabibigay naman ng mga financial investigation trainings, forensic accounting trainings. Ang kaibahan lang siguro nito ay yung pag-implement. Kasi you need to go out in the field to really observe the people and have a... Full experience how this investigation is being conducted.

740
04:11:30,160 --> 04:13:22,370
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Okay, thank you po. Move on na po tayo sa ibang part. Let me direct your attention to pages 19 and 7 of the so-called expert report. I'll read paragraph 3 for security bank account and then we just redacted it based on the ruling of the Honorable Court. We performed a fund flow analysis. and identified 5.3 million in fund transfers from, and let me highlight this, Deo Zambrano and Adam Anthony Cabe III, and 5 million representing proceeds from the maturity of an investment. Further, tracing indicated that the 5 million investment had initially been funded through cash deposits consisting of approximately 5,000 pieces of 1,000 banknotes. We have identified that these funds were used to purchase the 10.6 million insurance from FWD. I'll stop there. But in this scenario po kasi, just to give you a background, itong so-called expert identified two other individuals, si Zambrano at si Kabe, to have contributed to the purchase of an FWD insurance in the amount po of 10.6 million. And yet, on page 7, can we go there? We can see na yung whole amount po ng 10.6 million, tech please, was attributed by the so-called expert. Ayan po, let me direct your attention. Yung FWD insurance, inattribute po nung so-called expert, yung buo, sa mag-asawa kay VP Sara at Atty. Mans. So in relation to this scenario po, let me just first ask you muna. Who owns a property if several individuals contribute to its acquisition? If you can just recall po from civil law lang.

741
04:13:22,690 --> 04:13:25,010
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: The registered owner, your honor.

742
04:13:26,750 --> 04:13:38,360
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Kapag kamarami sila nag-contribute dun, what is the propriety po of attributing full ownership po dun sa isa lang na tao instead of all the co-owners?

743
04:13:38,860 --> 04:13:43,940
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: They are equally considered co-owners depending on their contribution.

744
04:13:45,180 --> 04:13:51,520
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright, so thank you po. So ano pong propriety pag isang co-owner lang kinonsider mo?

745
04:13:52,820 --> 04:13:53,540
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Mali po yan.

746
04:13:53,660 --> 04:14:27,820
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright, thank you po. On page 17 po of the report of the so-called expert, so we have here a table, table 23. And I just like to focus on, again, two things. Huwag niyo na pong pansinin yung figures. Nakalagay lang po dyan bank inflows and then income. I ask you this kasi meron po kayong background sa accounting. Pero let me just ask you first, how different po ba yung technical term na income dun sa term na bank inflows?

747
04:14:28,520 --> 04:14:39,440
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Magkaiba po yun, Your Honor. All, well, not all inflows are income but all income are considered inflows.

748
04:14:39,980 --> 04:14:55,490
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Okay, very clear po. But in the course of this trial, we also encountered the term return of capital. Return of capital. So how proper po or improper is it to consider po yung return of capital as income?

749
04:14:56,610 --> 04:15:01,890
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Magkaiba po yun, Your Honor. Balik lang po ito ng puhunan ng kapital. Hindi po siya kita.

750
04:15:03,500 --> 04:16:27,050
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Maraming salamat po. Now let's go back to page 37 of the so-called report. Again, hopefully, hindi naman ito paniwalaan as gospel truth ng marami. But again, we see here huge amounts attributed to VP Sara and her spouse Atty. Mans. And I won't go through these figures one by one, but just to highlight one last column. Dito po sa total computed amount, meron po ditong tatlong figures, 55 million, 74 million. 82 million. Hindi na po ako maglalabas ng calculator. Pero ang total amount po niyan is around 212 million, 629,718. Okay. When in fact, the GenCorp representative only said, and this is part of the court records, 2,142,369.14. So, around 100 times po off or 100 times mali yung so-called expert. Dito lang po sa column na to. My only question is this. In financial investigations, how important is it to meticulously go through the records one by one instead of considering summaries based on mere conjectures?

751
04:16:27,670 --> 04:16:34,850
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Objection, Your Honor, to the use of the phrase mali. I'm an expert. That again is a conclusion on the part of the lawyer.

752
04:16:34,850 --> 04:16:42,930
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Let's convert it to divergent or different from. If that's okay, Attorney Mark. 100 times different or divergent from.

753
04:16:43,430 --> 04:16:45,630
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Yes, divergent from.

754
04:16:45,650 --> 04:16:45,890
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: We're

755
04:16:45,890 --> 04:16:58,800
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: fine with that, Your Honor. So, that's the only question in financial investigations. How important is it to meticulously go through the records one by one instead of considering summaries based on mere conjectures?

756
04:16:59,420 --> 04:17:13,080
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Very important, Your Honor. Attention to detail is very important. Again, if there is a material deviation from the computation, it casts doubt dun sa computation.

757
04:17:13,600 --> 04:17:17,500
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: And how would you characterize a report po that uses conjectures?

758
04:17:18,480 --> 04:17:33,590
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Well, we cannot base, especially if it concerns financial investigation, hindi ho lang base sa conjectures. Dapat ho, ito ay May facts. Ito ay base sa mga actual na nangyari.

759
04:17:34,140 --> 04:17:41,680
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright. Salamat po. And para lang po madaling maintindihan para rin po sa mga publiko, ano po ba yung conjecture sa Filipino? If you know.

760
04:17:42,790 --> 04:17:45,530
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Sa akin kong paghalang, ito ay mga haka-haka.

761
04:17:46,880 --> 04:18:02,130
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Okay. So based on haka-haka. Alright. Now, by the way, in your years in AMLC, in relation to financial investigation, para po diretso na, how much do you value findings? From so-called experts that are based on conjectures.

762
04:18:03,150 --> 04:18:39,740
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Well, sa AMLC po na trabaho, magagaling ho yung mga tao natin sa AMLC. They're the top-tier government agency insofar as doing financial investigation. So, I don't see the need of outsourcing this information. Sa batas ho, sa kanila lang nakalagak ang mandato na yan. At nakita ko kasi first hand din gaano ka professional, ka dedicated ito mga tao natin sa sekretaryat. So why give it, why outsource it to another person when you have one agency, it is exclusively reserved to that agency, that function.

763
04:18:40,280 --> 04:18:58,030
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Maraming salamat po. Isa pa pong tanong dito, how much the, pero parang na-at-sagot yun na rin po, pero diretso yun ko na lang. How much does the AMLC rely? On third-party forensic analysts vis-a-vis its own financial investigators.

764
04:18:58,570 --> 04:19:10,930
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Hindi po sila nagre-rely. The AMLC is not bound to admit, rebut, or even suspend its activities pending the review of these private documents.

765
04:19:11,630 --> 04:19:25,170
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright po. And between the prosecution and the defense, I'm not just talking about this case, but in general. Between the prosecution and the defense, who has the burden of proving that an allegation is not based on conjectures?

766
04:19:25,780 --> 04:19:27,200
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: The prosecution.

767
04:19:27,720 --> 04:19:49,690
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: One last point on this. Kung sa raw records po, such as CTRs and STRs from AMLC, may double entries. May double entries. Pero may report po ng isang so-called financial expert na nagsasabi na walang double entries. What holds more value? Records ba ng AMLC o yung report ng so-called expert?

768
04:19:50,410 --> 04:19:54,390
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: The records of the AMLC po, no, should prevail.

769
04:19:54,810 --> 04:20:05,670
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright, maraming salamat po. Let's move on. What is the function of lifestyle checks of public officials in financial investigation?

770
04:20:06,750 --> 04:20:30,290
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Well, again, Your Honor, no, the purpose is to check if, again, the... The finances of that particular official is already beyond what is expected from him or her given the income and the declared business interests. So it checks if there's a disparity. Meron kong pagkakaiba. Ito sa in-expect at ito sa actual.

771
04:20:31,200 --> 04:21:09,970
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Now let me direct your attention to Article 11 entitled Accountability of Public Officers. Article 11, Accountability of Public Officers. Section 1, Public Office is a Public Trust. Public officers and employees must at all times be accountable to the people, serve them with utmost responsibility, integrity, loyalty, and efficiency, act with patriotism and justice, and lead modest lives. Let me first ask you po, in relation to financial investigation of public officials, what is your view on public office as a public trust?

772
04:21:10,510 --> 04:21:23,170
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: That is again the foundation of our government. Cannot have a government without the people behind it supporting it. And support is again predicated on trust.

773
04:21:24,430 --> 04:21:31,950
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright. And based on the provision that we just read, very briefly lang po, what does the command to lead modest lives entail?

774
04:21:33,620 --> 04:21:47,420
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Well, it must, again, they must be public officials, must lead modest lives. So again, not... Extravagant lifestyle. Do not adopt extravagant lifestyle but lead.

775
04:21:50,100 --> 04:21:54,740
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Have a lifestyle that is again what is expected from these public officials.

776
04:21:55,320 --> 04:22:04,420
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Ito quite personal na po, but you may or may not answer. But as a people, what should their attitude be towards public officers who do not lead modest lives?

777
04:22:06,590 --> 04:22:15,730
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Well, it degrades public trust. If it's, again, outside what is expected from these officials.

778
04:22:16,190 --> 04:22:20,390
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright, I'll just use a more vivid scenario just to drive this point. Say hypothetical.

779
04:22:22,110 --> 04:22:51,630
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: There's a public officer who claims to be anti-poverty and he owns this type of vehicle. This is a 2026 Mercedes-Benz G-Wagon, all-electric, obsidian black metallic. and the starting price of this vehicle is around 13.5 million pesos. Grabe talaga. So, what does this scenario say about leading a modest life? In your opinion?

780
04:22:52,790 --> 04:22:54,630
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: I'd rather not answer that.

781
04:22:54,810 --> 04:23:16,520
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Not answer? Okay. So, for example, this public officer accuses another of unexplained wealth and ostentatious lifestyle. My question is, in that scenario po, Again, hypothetical only. What does this say about the integrity of the accusation made by this kind of accuser? Kung ganyan yung public officer na nag-accusa.

782
04:23:17,050 --> 04:23:21,540
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Same your honor, same answer. I'd rather not delve upon this.

783
04:23:21,740 --> 04:23:23,400
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright, thank you. Let's just move on.

784
04:23:25,240 --> 04:23:37,000
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: When you conduct financial investigation on a public official, what is the propriety of upholding that person's rights?

785
04:23:38,350 --> 04:24:02,810
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Well, very important po yan. Along the course of the financial investigation, intact po ang rights ng ating subject. So, insofar as going into bank inquiry order, bank inquiry, even up to the civil forfeiture and filing of the money laundering case, meron po laging legal remedy ang ating subject, ang ating respondent.

786
04:24:04,860 --> 04:24:59,790
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Let me draw your attention to Article 11, Section 2. Section 2. The President, the Vice President, the members of the Supreme Court, the members of the Constitutional Commissions, and the Ombudsman may be removed from office on impeachment for and conviction of culpable violation of the Constitution, treason, bribery, graft and corruption, other high crimes, or betrayal of public trust. All other public officers and employees may be removed from office as provided by law, but not by impeachment. Sorry, please bear with me, Atty. Dela Fuente. I just have to go through this portion kasi meron pong financial investigation conducted in this impeachment. My question is, how will you describe the nature of the list of impeachable officers found in this section? If you can recall lang from your constitutional law.

787
04:25:01,150 --> 04:25:02,990
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: This is an exclusive list, Your Honor.

788
04:25:04,420 --> 04:25:10,560
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Exclusive. And how will you describe the nature of the grounds of impeachment in terms of seriousness?

789
04:25:11,940 --> 04:25:23,040
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Well, very serious po ito. On top of the hierarchy sila as to the degree of the offense.

790
04:25:23,620 --> 04:25:42,290
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright, thank you. And conviction in impeachment carries, alam naman po natin lahat to, the penalties of removal from position. and perpetual disqualification to hold public office. Now, how would you describe or characterize these penalties in terms of gravity or seriousness?

791
04:25:42,940 --> 04:25:57,620
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Well, very serious, Your Honor. Other than removal from office, absolute disqualification from holding further government offices. It leaves a stigma on the official.

792
04:25:58,920 --> 04:26:34,590
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Okay. We learned from mga amici curiae that the Court invited that the provisions of the Constitution kagaya po neto must not be read in isolation but in conjunction with each other. So let me relate the effects of the impeachment with another article under the Constitution, Article 5 on Suffrage. Let me read Section 1. Suffrage may be exercised by all citizens of the Philippines, not otherwise disqualified by law. For at least 18 years of age, have resided in the Philippines for at least one year in the place.

793
04:26:34,810 --> 04:26:41,210
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: With the permission of Attorney Mark, yes, what is the pleasure of Senator Judge Raffy Tulfo?

794
04:26:41,290 --> 04:27:26,000
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Is he a super witness, omni-witness? Ano bang klaseng witness ng pine-present ng defense? Pati ba naman pati amici curiae, pakialaman niya, Supreme Court, pakialaman niya, o Ombudsman, DOJ. Who is he? Who is this guy? I'm really very, very curious about the qualification of this gentleman para lahat na lang ng topic, kayang-kaya niyang sagutin mula sa kanyang handler, or excuse me, sa Defense. I don't think he's capable of answering those questions kasi hindi niya territory yun eh, Mr. Presiding Officer. Parang nakakaantok na, parang hindi kapani-paniwala. Parang binobola lang tayo nito. Nakangiti nga siya. Smile means yes. Anyway, Mr. Presiding Officer, siguro medyo put him in a short leash.

795
04:27:28,460 --> 04:28:18,590
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Atty. Mark, Along these lines of questions, how many more do you have? I think I get the point and drift of Senator Judge Raffy. He seems to be an expert in all already. But these are basic concepts and interpretations of the law, which the court can and will do on its own, given that we can and have taken judicial notice, especially of the constitutional and other legal provisions. Especially given that he is not presented nor was he qualified as a constitutional expert but merely expressing his opinion as a lawyer. Similar to both parties and those are lawyers in this impeachment court. So either wind up with this line of questioning or move on to your next point, Attorney Mark.

796
04:28:18,820 --> 04:28:21,980
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Mr. Presiding Officer, if I may, Mr. Presiding Officer.

797
04:28:22,960 --> 04:28:24,720
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Yes, what is the pleasure of Senator Judge...

798
04:28:24,720 --> 04:31:59,160
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Yes, Mr. Presiding Officer. I wanted to share the sentiment of my seatmate, Senator Raffy Tulfo because we have been giving a lot of leeway to the respondent's line of questioning but I was looking at the subpoena issued to the witness and it says here The witness, Attorney De La Fuente, will testify on fundamental legal concepts relating to the Anti-Money Laundering Act as amended. Identify documents relevant to his testimony and such other relevant matters. The issuance of a subpoena duces tecum and ad testificandum is requested directing the witness to appear and give his testimony. Using his curriculum vitae and other documents relevant to his qualifications and testimony. I'm just wondering, Mr. Presiding Officer, if the witness here will only talk about and be our resource person with regards to what was written in the subpoena. Because if you listen carefully to... What we have been hearing, number one, bagamat maaari po siyang magbigay ng expert opinion sa kanyang larangan bilang eksperto sa anti-money laundering, Hindi naman usap. Siguro pwedeng magdeklara na mali o invalid ang findings ng AMLA. At nasa Korte po yung pagpapasya kung gaano kabigat yung ebidensyang inilalahad po dito. Ikalawa, ginawang pangulaw, matagal na diniscuss kanina yung bank secrecy law. And malinaw naman po doon sa Section 2 na ang isang impeachment proceedings ay exemption sa bank secrecy. And in the November 5 order of this court, pinayagan po na ang AMLA records na may sumiti pursuant doon sa lawful subpoena subject to confidentiality safeguards. At panghuli ginong Pangulo, Mr. Presiding Officer, yung expertise po kasi ng witness sa anti-money laundering, bagamat may iba siguro na hindi mag-agree na siya isang eksperto, ako na ho, I give him the benefit of the doubt, Pero ang maaari niya pong ipaliwanag ang AMLA at banking practices pero na-ba-bother po ako, ginong Pangulo, at naa-alarma na hindi po siya ang DOJ, hindi po siya ang ombudsman, lalo na hindi po siya ang parte ng korte para magbigay po ng binding legal conclusions o mag-desisyon kung meron nga pong criminal liability. Mr. Presiding Officer, my only question is, dapat ba doon lang po umiikot yung kanyang pagiging isang testigo doon sa inisyo na subpoena? Or ang dahilan po ba kung bakit siya naririto ay para i-refute yung pong sinasabing financial expert ng prosecution? Because if that's the case, I have no problem with that, Mr. Presiding Officer.

799
04:32:00,630 --> 04:32:13,270
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Atty. Mark, kindly respond to the query. Noted, Senator Judge Villanueva, kindly respond to the query of the Presiding Officer. How long will your questions be along these lines?

800
04:32:14,230 --> 04:32:46,190
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Just a couple of pages worth of questions, Your Honor. Anyway, just to respond also for the guidance of the Senator Judges, part of our offer is for... The witness to testify on other relevant matters and we deem that these are all relevant matters. Considering your honor, my prior question that how important is upholding The rights of the person being financially investigated apply as well. So, just a couple more questions. Again, Your Honor, we ask for leeway considering...

801
04:32:46,190 --> 04:32:50,970
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: We have been giving... You must acknowledge that we have been giving leeway.

802
04:32:51,070 --> 04:33:01,110
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: And we very much appreciate, Your Honor, the leeway that has been given to us. But just to answer the question of the presiding officer, there's a couple pages worth of questions, Ron.

803
04:33:01,620 --> 04:33:03,540
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Just one follow-up question on that.

804
04:33:03,560 --> 04:33:05,300
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Kindly turn on the mic of Senator Judge Villanueva.

805
04:33:05,420 --> 04:33:11,690
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Just one follow-up question on that. Did you give the witness a copy of the forensic report?

806
04:33:13,340 --> 04:33:14,200
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: No, your honor.

807
04:33:14,850 --> 04:33:30,570
Sen. Joel Villanueva: No, because I was wondering, Mr. Presiding Officer, a while ago, if I heard it right from the witness, that he himself did not even get a chance to actually read the forensic report. So he doesn't have any copy of that.

808
04:33:31,560 --> 04:33:42,210
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: That's accurate, your honor. That's why... Part of our questioning is to confront actual portions of that report and asking him of his general comments there.

809
04:33:42,230 --> 04:33:53,450
Sen. Joel Villanueva: I'm just wondering because if he is to refute the report, then he should have seen the report, should have read the report. I'm just wondering. Thank you, Mr. President.

810
04:33:53,670 --> 04:34:02,940
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: With all due respect, Your Honor, we just wanted to do it in open court. We didn't want to have any prior correspondence with the subpoenaed witness.

811
04:34:03,140 --> 04:34:22,960
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Because that's the thing that I'm going to do later on when we get the chance to ask questions. We will be asking him about the forensic report because we feel that he is the best person to refute the forensic report. Now, if he cannot answer these questions, then... For me, it's going to be useless.

812
04:34:23,320 --> 04:34:30,800
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: We are okay with that, Your Honor, with that methodology. It's really up to, we submit to the court's wisdom on how they want to confront this witness later.

813
04:34:30,800 --> 04:34:42,520
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Okay, thank you. Thank you for that clarification. How the senator judges will ask or make interjections and how the senator judges in the court will appreciate the testimony of this witness. Yes, what is the pleasure of Senator Judge Raffy Tulfo?

814
04:34:42,780 --> 04:36:05,840
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Thank you, Mr. President. Dudugtuhan ko lang ang sinabi kanina ni Senator Villanueva. Kung i-refute niya ang forensic expert witness and yet hindi pala siya nabigyan ng kopya ng mga dokumento present ng expert witness. So hindi dapat siya pwedeng mag-refute o kumontra dahil in the first place wala siyang idea kung ano yung mga nakasaad doon sa sinabi ng testigo yung forensic expert witness. At pinasenta rito, maliban na lamang sa on the spot, pinagtatanong ng defense. So dapat, beforehand, he was given a copy of those documents para makapag-aralan niya, para makapagawa siya ng research, para in that case, magiging intelligent, he will be well informed, and he can give intelligent assessment doon sa pag-refute. Sa mga sinabi nung forensic witness, sa ngayon kasi wala eh. Wala siyang kaalam-alam, Mr. Presiding Officer. Wala talaga. Zero. Nagtakangaw kanina, pati ba naman yung, ano ba to? G-Wagon, mag-witness sa G-Wagon, ano ba to? Salesman na rin. I mean, baka mamaya eh.

815
04:36:05,840 --> 04:36:12,820
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: The court reminds the gallery to kindly not react or avoid reacting to statements made by anyone in this chamber.

816
04:36:12,980 --> 04:36:37,740
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: I mean, sorry, parang gina - Maybe it's not your fault. I'm not gonna fault you on this. Maybe ang problema sa defense, sobrang bilib sila sa iyo, pero hindi mo siguro kayang panindigan yung kasobrang kabiliban nila sa iyo na kung ano na lang pinapasok at sinusubo sa iyo na hindi mo kayang panindigan, hindi mo kayang sasagot. Nagmumakatuloy ikaw na parang alam mo na, hindi mo kagagawa niyong kundi kagagawa ng defense. Maraming salamat po, Mr. President Officer.

817
04:36:38,860 --> 04:36:43,280
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Yes, Duly noted, Senator Judge Raffy, what is the pleasure of Senator Judge Bam?

818
04:36:44,760 --> 04:36:47,980
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: On this note, Mr. President Officer, Mr. Witness,

819
04:36:50,200 --> 04:36:54,520
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: Any documents provided to you before appearing here?

820
04:36:55,520 --> 04:36:56,160
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: None, Your Honor.

821
04:36:57,460 --> 04:37:16,130
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: So, none of the AMLA records that we subpoenaed were shown to you? Yung mga bank statements, insurance, placements, GIS ng mga kumpanya, were any of these shown to you?

822
04:37:16,470 --> 04:37:17,350
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: None, Your Honor.

823
04:37:17,690 --> 04:37:24,670
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: None? Okay, so I take it the defense is asking you about the report in terms of concepts.

824
04:37:25,610 --> 04:37:40,210
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: And on the basis, Your Honor, of actual portions. Because it's a 50-page report, Your Honor, so we just wanted to focus on several portions of that report by confronting him in open court of those portions and then asking him about concepts.

825
04:37:40,230 --> 04:38:33,650
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: Okay, so it's really concepts and general ideas about... Amla, and Financial Investigations. Okay? Kasi, Mr. Witness, and again, di mo naman itong kasalanan, but many times, we have witnesses here, pag tinatanong na namin, ang sagot sa amin, di ho namin alam. So, gusto namin ng mga witness na pwede kaming saguting diretso talaga. Because we just want to find out, we just want to find out the truth, we want to know your opinion. but on specific matters also. So, anyway, you're here and later on may cross, later on magtatanong kami, pero ang ayaw naming marinig is yung sunod-sunod na hindi ko po alam, hindi ko po nabasa, hindi ko po, di ba? Kasi ang nangyayari parang wala rin tayong narating na totoong opinion o totoong pananaw dito sa mga bagay-bagay. Thank you, thank you, Mr. President.

826
04:38:33,890 --> 04:38:38,470
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: What is the pleasure of Senator Judge Erwin, the remarks of the Hon. Aquino are generally noted.

827
04:38:40,780 --> 04:40:15,200
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Mr. Presiding Officer, quick manifestation lamang po. Kung wala pong nakakita ng mga dokumento itong testigo po na ito, lahat po na sinasabi niya kanina pa, kanina pang umaga, may aabutin na tayo ng alas 6 ng gabi, lahat po ito ay theoretical and cannot be rebutted, documented as documented financial intelligence, Mr. Presiding Officer. Kahit na nanggaling pa siya dyan sa AMLC, etc. na yung kanyang expertise. Kung hindi naman niya po nakita pala ay mga dokumento, STRs, CTRs. What good is it? Para anong titistigo niya? E puro ito theory sa kanyang paningin, sa kanyang paniniwala. I think the defense. I know that you can do better than that. Siguro this coming days, get a witness. Now, who can really stand up? I'm just telling you now to prepare. Get somebody who can really stand up, who can really answer questions from the senator judges. Because mamaya ito, papawisan ito, baka hindi na makasagot ito. I mean, medyo mahina po, I'm sorry ha, mahina po yung the witnesses that you're presenting here these past few days. I cannot dictate that, but I'm just saying, that's my opinion there. Against somebody who can really ika nga na professional, na who can rebut yung mga sanasabi ng prosecution, makakasagot po. Maraming salamat po.

828
04:40:15,200 --> 04:40:18,080
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: We respect the opinion. We know the manifestations of the Senator.

829
04:40:18,180 --> 04:40:20,860
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Yes, what is the pleasure of Senator Judge Risa Hontiveros?

830
04:40:24,550 --> 04:40:34,640
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: If I may, Mr. Presiding Officer, just a quick follow-up question to the questions raised right now by the colleague Senator Judges. If I may.

831
04:40:34,720 --> 04:40:35,060
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Yes.

832
04:40:35,420 --> 04:40:36,940
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Salamat po, Mr. Presiding Officer.

833
04:40:37,000 --> 04:40:37,520
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: You may proceed.

834
04:40:37,940 --> 04:40:50,700
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Atty. Dela Fuente, kasasabi niyo na lamang po ngayon na hindi niyo po nabasa ang forensic report na earlier inihain sa korteng ito ni Atty. Cabrera. Tama po?

835
04:40:50,980 --> 04:40:51,680
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Correct, Your Honor.

836
04:40:52,160 --> 04:41:11,790
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Pero at least nabasa niyo po ba o nasimulan man lang iscan, natignan niyo po ba yung mga iba't ibang records na sinupinas, sinumite sa korteng ito na pinagbasehan? Atty. Cabrera sa kanyang inihaing forensics report sa amin.

837
04:41:11,850 --> 04:41:17,350
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Your Honor, hindi po kasi ito ay confidential. Wala akong authority to look into those documents.

838
04:41:18,110 --> 04:41:39,930
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: So, ibig sabihin, with all due respect po, sa ngayon, wala po kayo sa solid na posisyon na suriin. Yung kalidad or katotohanan or solidong basehan kahit po sa general principles nung forensic report na iyon ni Atty. Cabrera.

839
04:41:40,070 --> 04:41:57,310
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Meron po, Your Honor. As flashed on the screen, I echo what the law says. So base lang po sa batas, maaari ko na akong sagutin kung ano yung nasa... Na ito ba ay lawful or hindi? Yun po ang ginagawa ko ngayon.

840
04:41:57,410 --> 04:42:30,460
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Alright. So lastly, follow up sa ngayon, Atty. De La Fuente. Kasunod ng mga prinsipyo ngayon na kung bibigyan niyo po ng benefit of the doubt si Atty. Cabrera noon na nagsisikap siyang sumunod din sa mga batayang prinsipyo ng inyong propesyon, dahil kayo po ay peer, kayo po ay colleague kay Atty. Cabrera, Masasabi niyo po ba na may misrepresentation kay Atty. Cabrera na tawagin siyang supposed expert sa field ninyo?

841
04:42:30,460 --> 04:43:17,300
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Well, I have a high respect for, respect for Atty. Cabrera. His professional and personal opinions po ay nirerespeto natin siya. But pagdating sa batas, again, we have to abide kung ano yung tama ba, nasa tamang proseso po ba, ang kanyang methodologies po ba ay tama. So ang ginagawa ko lang po, binabangga ang kanyang ginawa doon sa kung ano ang meron sa batas. Kung ito po ba ay mag-a-align. Yun ang aking role dito. Kaya nga sabi ko, I don't need to, ito sa sarili ko, to read the full report even before going here. Because kahit i-flash yan ngayon pa lang, makikita niyo na po, aligned po ba ito sa mga provisions ng AMLA? or hindi.

842
04:43:17,500 --> 04:43:49,970
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Sa huli po, at least, salamat naman sa pinahayag niyong pagrespeto bilang peer ninyo kay Atty. Cabrera and I'm willing to guess kung itinanong namin sa kanya noon, sasabihin din niya sa kahit sinong colleague. So at the very least po, and in closing dito sa interjection ko, dahil tinanggap po ng Korte na isa sa mga expert witnesses sa trial na ito si Atty. Cabrera, at the very least, nire-respeto niyo po ba? Yung ganyang pagtanggap ng Korte kay Atty. Cabrera bilang isa sa mga expert witnesses sa trial na ito.

843
04:43:49,990 --> 04:43:50,370
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes,

844
04:43:50,370 --> 04:43:50,530
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Your Honor.

845
04:43:50,750 --> 04:43:54,130
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Maraming salamat po, Atty. De La Fuente. Salamat, Mr. Presiding Officer.

846
04:43:54,410 --> 04:43:56,450
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Senator Judge Imee, what is your pleasure, ma'am?

847
04:43:58,770 --> 04:44:24,990
Sen. Imee Marcos: Yes, maraming salamat sa ating presiding judge. At nakikinig po ako sa aking mga kasamahan dito sa Senado. Subalit, ipapaalala ko lang sa lahat na si Lady Justice o yung babaeng justisya ay bulag na katakipang mata. Kasi hindi kinakailangan na basahin ang bawat dokumento, alamin ang mga personalidad, dahil pantay-pantay ang timbang sa batas. Yun lang po.

848
04:44:26,220 --> 04:44:29,840
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Senator Judge Camille? What is your pleasure, ma'am?

849
04:44:34,280 --> 04:45:29,860
Sen. Camille Villar: Yes, hello, good afternoon po. Just a quick manifestation. I think we've been listening to this witness and I have to say that while he probably hasn't seen the documents that were given by the AMLC, I distinctly remember even the supposed expert witness ng prosecution, si Atty. Cabrera, meron po siyang mga figures dun sa kanyang report of the alleged unexplained wealth that was based on, and it was in the forensic report, that was based on research on the internet. There were also certain facts that he put that also he had very little or no basis for saying. And I think we respected that and accepted that.

850
04:45:32,860 --> 04:46:27,080
Sen. Camille Villar: Personally, I would like to hear the thoughts and opinions of our witness, especially regarding theories because I think while some of his answers to the questions that are being asked by both the defense and the prosecution is of his expert opinion, I think they are of universal principles. Some accounting principles are also universal. So he can answer that even without seeing the specific documents. And I think we listened to the expert witness, to the forensic witness, the financial forensic witness of the prosecution. I think we should also give due time to the expert witness of the defense.

851
04:46:30,220 --> 04:46:35,350
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Chair notes. Kala ko pupunta ka sa kantin eh.

852
04:46:35,960 --> 04:47:48,000
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Yes. Just one quick manifestation, Mr. Presiding Officer. Number one, let me again put on record that we have been listening attentively to the respondent's line of questioning despite the fact that it's beyond the issuance of the subpoena and the boundaries set forth by the court inasmuch as the process is concerned. We have no problems with that, Mr. President. In fact, I wanted to palawigin nga, Mr. President, Mr. Presiding Officer, yung ginagawa ng depensa kung siya ay isang forensic expert, kung siya ay magre-refute noong forensic report. I'm more than willing to listen. In fact, kayo na po nagsabi, Mr. President, at inamin na po ng defense lawyer na nagbibigay tayo ng leeway sa kanila. And we have been, we should be continuously giving leeway to be able to understand clearly. But ang hindi po kasi maganda kung unlimited yung magiging

853
04:47:50,600 --> 04:48:47,330
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Scope ng pagiging testigo ng isang witness. And again, we respect the witness. We feel that he is indeed an expert sa issue ng money laundering activities. And again, Mr. Presiding Officer, we're willing to listen to him as long as nandun pa rin sa tamang jurisdiction. At yun nga pong aking masidhing pagnanais ay Matanong po siya mamaya dun sa forensic report para nang sa ganoon makita po natin yung kabilang side, yung kabilang face. Noong pong nangyaring pag-testigo, noong pong forensic expert ng prosecution. Now, if he is not the forensic expert ng defense, I am more than willing to listen in the coming days kung meron pong forensic expert ang defense to refute yung mga binanggit naman ni Atty. Cabrera. Maraming salamat, Mr. Presiding Officer. Thank you.

854
04:48:47,550 --> 04:48:53,270
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Yes, Senator Judge Raffy. Kindly turn on the mic of Senator Judge Raffy.

855
04:48:53,710 --> 04:49:11,680
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Kasi... Kanina pa tayo dito at parang nagiging super witness na siya, ika nga sabi kanina. Now, very simple question lang dito kay Mr. Witness. Kanina, if you remember, I asked you kung ikaw ba ay nakapagkompleto na ng isang kaso while you were in AMLC. You said yes?

856
04:49:11,740 --> 04:49:11,980
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes.

857
04:49:12,320 --> 04:49:13,780
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: You sure? You're under oath?

858
04:49:14,080 --> 04:49:14,460
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, sir.

859
04:49:14,520 --> 04:49:16,160
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Okay, and ano yung kaso ngayon?

860
04:49:16,620 --> 04:49:22,140
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Hindi ko po siya dahil... As part of the confidentiality, hindi ko po masabi.

861
04:49:22,140 --> 04:49:31,560
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: What if I would present to you an evidence later on na wala kang naikompletong kaso at wala ka pang naifile na kaso whatsoever while you were in AMLC? What if I can present that evidence?

862
04:49:31,560 --> 04:49:34,560
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Personally, Your Honor, it's the agency who files, hindi ko ako yung personal.

863
04:49:34,680 --> 04:49:44,260
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Kasi sabi mo kanina nung tinanong kita, kanina-kanina pa, na ikaw pa yung nakapag-investigate, nakapagbuo na ng isang kaso. What if I can show you proof later on na wala talaga, so pwede ka makontempt?

864
04:49:45,940 --> 04:49:48,360
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: As far as I can remember, Your Honor, I signed.

865
04:49:48,740 --> 04:49:49,520
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: You signed?

866
04:49:49,880 --> 04:49:51,040
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, sir.

867
04:49:51,340 --> 04:50:15,390
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Pwede ma-refute yan later on. So doon pa nga lang, Mr. Presiding Officer, nagkaka-problema na eh. Sinasabi niya na meron na siyang nabuo na kaso hanggang sa na-efile, when in fact, ang pagkakaalam ko, wala. Wala pa talaga. And he's just claiming it, and like I said, later on, pwede akong kukuha ng ebidensya na wala pa siyang nabuo ng kaso at baka makontemplan ito. Thank you, Mr. Presiding Officer.

868
04:50:16,650 --> 04:50:41,470
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: We note, The manifestations made by all of the senator judges. However, the court cannot dictate nor impinge upon how either party will present their evidence in chief, much less dictate their strategy in choosing their respective witnesses. I urge our colleagues to...

869
04:50:43,720 --> 04:51:30,250
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Exercise more leeway and patience with the presentation being made by the counsel for the respondent. Senator Imee is correct. Habang sinisimbolo ng babaeng sumisimbolo sa ustisya na nakatakip ang mata niya, hindi po nakatakip yung kanyang mga tenga. Ibig sabihin, huwag tayong magbasa base sa panlabas na kanyuan. Makinig at pakinggan din natin kung anong sinasabi, hindi lamang ng mga testigo, pero ganyan din, ng magkabilang panig. I ask for the indulgence of our colleagues and ask Attorney Mark II to take note of the manifestations made and be sensitive to them to a certain extent in continuing with this direct examination with this witness. You may proceed, Attorney Mark.

870
04:51:31,460 --> 04:52:05,630
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Thank you, Your Honor. Okay, so I'll just abbreviate some of the portions, Your Honor. In respect of what the Senator Judges have manifested. So, we're talking about financial investigation about public officials as well. My question is, in an impeachment process, how does the Bill of Rights apply insofar as that impeachable officials' rights when financial investigations are being conducted against that person?

871
04:52:06,220 --> 04:52:15,800
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: During the course of the financial investigation, Your Honor, Bill of Rights, the rights of the accused are still intact. In fact, meron ho siyang mga legal remedies along the way.

872
04:52:17,410 --> 04:52:25,190
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: And how does due process, which is part of the Bill of Rights, apply in financial investigations of an impeachable official, if at all?

873
04:52:25,800 --> 04:52:35,780
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Again, it is still intact. Meron ho legal remedies, right of the accused to answer, opportunity to present evidence in his or her defense.

874
04:52:37,500 --> 04:53:27,050
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright, I'll just abbreviate other portions of the Bill of Rights, but let me direct your attention to Article 14, Section 3 of the International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights to which the Philippines is a signatory. And I'll just end with this point, Your Honor, for this portion. In the determination of any criminal charge against him, everyone shall be entitled to the following minimum guarantees in full equality. A. To be informed promptly and in detail in a language which he understands of the nature and cause of the charge against him. My question is in line with that provision that we just read. What is the value of informing the person that you're investigating promptly and completely of the charges against him?

875
04:53:27,720 --> 04:53:42,630
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Again, this is financial investigation, Your Honor. Again, the right of the accused. To confront the evidences presented and also answer with the proper court. Yun po ay importante pa rin.

876
04:53:42,790 --> 04:56:47,140
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright, thank you. Sige, move on na po tayo. Dito po sa impeachment na to, Atty. De La Fuente, yung conviction or acquittal ni VP Sara, she was voted in 2022 by 32,208,417 na Pilipino. Nakasalalay po ito sa boto ng ating mga mahal na senador ngayon, 24 of them. And ang pagboto and conviction ay nakabase na lamang sa isang article of impeachment. Yun po yung unexplained wealth, alleged unexplained wealth. These constitute the formal charges against the impeachable officer. Just to eliminate doubt, balikan lang po natin yung article na yun. Again, yung tatlo kasing article na withdraw na. Kapag binalikan natin itong Article 2, attorney de la Fuente, says here, Respondent Vice President Sara Z. Duterte committed culpable violation of the Constitution and betrayed public trust when she, letter A, amassed unexplained wealth manifestly disproportionate to her lawful income and earnings during her incumbency as a public official. Letter B, failed to fully and truthfully disclose all her and her spouse's assets, liabilities, and net worth in her statement of assets, liabilities, and net worth, or SALN, including in her SALN for the years 2022, 2023, and 2024. And Letter C, failed to divest and instead willfully continued all her business interests during her tenure as Vice President. For the years 2022, 2023, 2024, and 2025. So as regards letter A, so we don't mislead the public, we just want to be more precise. This is what the articles of impeachment charge or is part of their charge. And I'll read. From 2007 to 2024, the net worth of respondent and her spouse rose from 7 million to 88 million. or a total increase of around 80 million. However, as shown earlier, the lawful income of respondent and her spouse for the same period only amounts to roughly 30 million. The difference between their lawful income of 30 million and the increase in their net worth of around 80 million, resulting in a disparity of approximately 50 million, clearly constitutes unexplained wealth. So yun po yung charge. Financial investigator po kayo. Base lang po sa bahaging ito po ng charges, may approximation po na 50 million na unexplained wealth daw po. Okay, according to that charge. Ano pong masasabi niyo po sa kalidad na paratang na ito bilang basihan ng pag-convict or pag-acquit kay VP Sara?

877
04:56:47,910 --> 04:57:01,130
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Objection, Your Honor. Given that the witness has admitted that he has not read the entire report, and that he has not been given access to any of the documents in this case, he would not be competent to render an opinion on that.

878
04:57:01,330 --> 04:57:03,270
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Yeah, but this is not the report. This is the articles

879
04:57:03,270 --> 04:57:08,210
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: of impeachment. If he knows, if you know, Attorney Rainer, kindly respond.

880
04:57:08,570 --> 04:57:17,090
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Your Honor, for this one, I leave it to the discretion of our Honorable Impeachment Court and I leave it to the wisdom of our Impeachment Court.

881
04:57:18,220 --> 04:57:22,580
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright, I'll move on to a new allegation or part of the allegation.

882
04:57:24,520 --> 04:59:31,110
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Let me direct your attention to pages 13 to 14 of the articles of impeachment. Former Senator Antonio Trillanes IV disclosed that a significant portion of this wealth was sourced from illegal activities, including funds linked to illegal drug operations and associations with drug syndicates, and identified specific transactions and individuals connected to the drug trade. These disclosures are corroborated by the findings of the AMLC, which flag billions of pesos in transactions involving respondent and her spouse, reflecting patterns consistent with money laundering and predicate offenses. Notably, a certain name identified in the AMLC records corresponds with those publicly disclosed by Trillanes. Taken together, these facts establish a pattern of criminal enrichment and demonstrate that respondent's wealth is manifestly unlawful, grossly disproportionate to legitimate income, and constitutes ill-gotten wealth. Clear grounds for impeachment. Alright, I'll just go straight to the point, Atty. De La Fuente. Those are the charges, but number one, former Senator Trillanes was not presented. No illegal activity was ever identified. No drug operations with drug syndicates were discussed. No discussion about money laundering and the amount laundered. And no discussion also about any predicate crime. And yet the paragraph ends with, and I quote, Taken together, these facts establish a pattern of criminal enrichment and demonstrates that respondent's wealth is manifestly unlawful, grossly disproportionate to illegal. Legitimate income and constitutes ill-gotten wealth. Clear grounds for impeachment. My only question is this. As a seasoned financial investigator, how clear or viable are these charges of unexplained wealth against the Vice President?

883
04:59:31,550 --> 04:59:43,010
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: As to viability, as to the viability of the charges, again, Your Honor, I leave it to the Court to decide if these charges would warrant

884
04:59:44,980 --> 04:59:48,120
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Decision on conviction or acquittal. So, it's really up to the court.

885
04:59:48,360 --> 05:01:25,760
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright. Punta naman po tayo dun sa letter B or yung nondisclosure in the SALN. Last couple of pages, Your Honor, if I may be allowed to just finish. Contrary to her declarations in the SALN, Respondent and her spouse owned and acquired billions of pesos which were deposited from 2007 to 2024 in their bank accounts. These funds deposited in their bank accounts were not declared in Respondent's SALNs, including in her SALNs covering the years 2022, 2023, and 2024. Despite the billions of pesos deposited in respondent and her spouse's bank accounts from 2007 to 2024, these deposits were not declared as cash on hand, cash in bank, or other personal assets in respondent's SALNs, including in her SALNs for 2020 to 2023 and 2024. Again, ganun lang po yung allegation na nakalagay sa articles of impeachment. And I quote, owned and acquired billions of pesos. which were deposited from 2007 to 2024 in their bank accounts. And then these funds deposited in their bank accounts were not declared in respondent SALNs, including in their SALNs covering the years 2020 to 2024. Again, my only question as a financial investigation, ano ang effect? Maybe you can answer not in lieu of the facts of this case, but what is the effect if the accusation of financial wrongdoing is vague?

886
05:01:27,520 --> 05:01:28,560
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Again, Your Honor, the last

887
05:01:28,560 --> 05:01:34,740
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: part. What is the effect of a vague accusation of financial wrongdoing as a financial investigator?

888
05:01:35,720 --> 05:01:41,520
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Objection, Your Honor. There's nothing vague about the quoted portion that is a conclusion on the part of the...

889
05:01:41,520 --> 05:01:49,140
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Kindly reform your question, Attorney Mark. Just ask him directly what his opinion is of the allegation you read in the articles. If you can.

890
05:01:50,730 --> 05:02:08,360
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Opinion on this, Your Honor. Again, the question... If there's ambiguity or vagueness, well, that would weaken. But again, I defer to the wisdom of the Honorable Impeachment Court how they appreciate these observations.

891
05:02:09,820 --> 05:02:12,100
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: We respect that. Okay.

892
05:02:18,310 --> 05:02:18,870
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Okay.

893
05:02:19,230 --> 05:02:29,670
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Your Honor, I'm very sorry to interrupt. Before we continue, could we have a very brief CR break? It's a one or two minute break. I think the witness also may need to...

894
05:02:30,180 --> 05:02:31,880
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Do you need to go, Atty. Rainer?

895
05:02:32,480 --> 05:02:33,080
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor.

896
05:02:34,790 --> 05:02:38,630
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Chair declares a three-minute bathroom break.

897
05:02:39,070 --> 05:02:40,550
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Thank you, Your Honor. Thank you, Your Honor.

898
05:08:37,580 --> 05:08:46,630
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Thank you, Your Honor. I'm winding up, Your Honor. We decided to obviate certain portions.

899
05:08:46,970 --> 05:08:48,030
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Kindly proceed, Atty. Morris.

900
05:08:48,210 --> 05:09:27,360
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Thank you, Your Honor. Alright, let me direct your attention to Article 3, Section 3 of the 1987 Constitution. It says here, The privacy of communication and correspondence shall be inviolable except upon lawful order of the court or when public safety or order requires otherwise as prescribed by law. Any evidence obtained in violation of this or the preceding section shall be inadmissible for any purpose in any proceeding. In line with this provision and your experience also as a financial investigator, kindly explain the concept of fishing expedition. If you know. or if you can recall.

901
05:09:28,800 --> 05:10:25,510
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Well, on fishing expedition, Your Honor, this is again initiated under that constitutional provision. It protects the individual from any arbitrary state intrusion, ensuring that privacy of communication and also information relating to the individual is being safeguarded. So pinaprotectahan po ng ating Constitution. Ang panghihimasok, walang habas na panghihimasok sa informasyon na ito provided na kung ito man ay in relation sa ongoing investigation o sa isang kaso, dapat sundin pa rin ang mga safeguards provided ng batas. Hindi ho ito unlimited authority to disclose and... Discloses information.

902
05:10:26,110 --> 05:10:34,530
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright, and what is the effect of fishing expedition in terms of documents used as evidence in an impeachment trial, if at all?

903
05:10:35,030 --> 05:10:41,170
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: So ito ay considered na fruits of a poisonous tree. These are inadmissible as evidence.

904
05:10:41,790 --> 05:10:56,080
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright, thank you po. I'm about to conclude. Yung term na ill-gotten wealth actually appears once in the Constitution. Let me direct your attention to Article 18, Section 26.

905
05:10:57,600 --> 05:11:34,470
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Let me read. The authority to issue sequestration or freeze orders under Proclamation No. 3 dated March 25, 1986 in relation to the recovery of ill-gotten wealth shall remain operative for not more than 18 months after the ratification of this Constitution. However, in the national interest as certified by the President, the Congress may extend such period. My only question about this article is this. If you know, based on the history of our 1987 Constitution, kaninong ilgaten wealth po ba yung tinutukoy ng probisyong ito?

906
05:11:37,020 --> 05:11:52,180
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: For this specific provision, there's no specific individual, official, or entity mentioned po dito sa Section 26 in Article... At any rate,

907
05:11:52,260 --> 05:12:02,780
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: how important po ba is it to look back on the history of our Constitution as we undertake the impeachment process today? If you can just give your opinion on that.

908
05:12:03,500 --> 05:12:14,560
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Napaka-importante ho. Our history would dictate our future. So we have to look back kung ano man ang sarkomstansyang nakapaligid nung naisulat ho ang batas na ito.

909
05:12:15,610 --> 05:12:26,800
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright. Last set of figures before I end. Let me show you VP Sara's recent ratings in the 2028 Presidential Preference Surveys. So I'll just show you three surveys.

910
05:12:30,890 --> 05:13:52,070
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: So Sara Duterte leads 2028 Presidential Preference in Pulse Asia. So there's the rating. And then next survey, Sara Duterte maintains commanding lead in 2028 Presidential Preferences. And then there's the one with, I think this is OCTA, Current Presidential Voting Preference. And I'm about to end. We all know that impeachment carries the penalty of disqualification to hold any office under the Republic of the Philippines. This is my second to the last question and it is quite a personal one. Since iisa na lang naman po yung charge against VP Sara. Again, you can answer based on the factual milieu of what you know from this case or based on your opinion. What is the seriousness po? What is the seriousness of financial wrongdoing that warrants a conviction in an impeachment case? Your Honor, again, let me repeat the question, considering also, granting that these surveys, that VP Sara, the, well, the choice of the people based on these surveys, what is the seriousness of financial wrongdoing that warrants VP Sara's conviction?

911
05:13:53,960 --> 05:13:56,900
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Seriousness of financial wrongdoing that warrants...

912
05:13:56,930 --> 05:14:03,160
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Conviction in this impeachment case. Gusto niyo po bang tagalogin para mas may time kayo?

913
05:14:03,680 --> 05:14:04,540
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Sige nga po.

914
05:14:04,740 --> 05:14:19,020
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Gano po ba kagrabe or ano po ba yung bigat ng financial wrongdoing that will warrant yung conviction ng isang tao sa isang impeachment proceeding?

915
05:14:19,750 --> 05:14:42,320
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Dapat ito ay may absolute certainty po tayo. Given we are impeaching a high-ranking official, the findings should be based on facts, not conjectures. At dapat ito, yung magiging desisyon ng ating impeachment court must

916
05:14:42,320 --> 05:14:44,900
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: uphold the rule of law.

917
05:14:45,810 --> 05:14:57,350
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: So ang ating magiging desisyon, it should... Encapsulate yung prinsipyo na our law should protect the innocent as aggressively as it pursues the guilty.

918
05:14:58,020 --> 05:15:30,650
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Thank you. One last question, Your Honor. And I'll end with a preamble. The preamble states we, the sovereign Filipino people, imploring the aid of Almighty God. And then the lawyers would know the rest of the preamble. But my question is this, and it's again quite a personal question. You are a lecturer. You mentioned that you have students and you have an influence on the next generation. How important is it to implore the aid of Almighty God in such a time as this when the ongoing impeachment has greatly divided our beloved country?

919
05:15:31,630 --> 05:15:53,780
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Again, very important, Your Honor. There are things that are beyond our explanation, beyond our comprehension. So it's really important that all of our decisions should be guided. by the Divine. And again, we have to be aware that whatever our decision will be, will have long-lasting effects sa ating bansa.

920
05:15:54,160 --> 05:16:50,510
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Thank you. Your Honor, just no more questions, just a manifestation, Your Honor. Again, we respect the sentiments, Your Honor, of our senator judges. But again, and this is coming from a personal standpoint, and I know I'm not authorized to speak on behalf of this witness, Your Honor, but as a colleague in the profession, We have an oath, Your Honor, and we're just doing our job, trying to do our job in the best possible way, Your Honor. We do not want to impede on any rights of other peoples, as well as the rights of the prosecution to make their own case. But, Your Honor, our goal in this whole exercise is really to ferret out the truth and provide two sides of the coin, Your Honor. And we hope, Your Honor, that this will be well taken as well by the Senate Impeachment Court. Thank you, Your Honor.

921
05:16:50,690 --> 05:17:07,870
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: We note the manifestation of Attorney Mark as stated by the Presiding Officer earlier. Liyue has been given and patience has been extended not only by the Presiding Officer but by members of the Impeachment Court as well. Attorney, Honorable Chel Cross.

922
05:17:08,270 --> 05:17:10,490
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: With the permission of the Honorable Court.

923
05:17:10,910 --> 05:17:11,890
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: You may proceed, sir.

924
05:17:12,780 --> 05:17:14,640
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Good afternoon, Mr. Witness.

925
05:17:14,960 --> 05:17:16,180
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Good afternoon, Your Honor.

926
05:17:16,920 --> 05:17:23,560
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: You started out in the Anti-Money Laundering Council in July of 2015.

927
05:17:23,820 --> 05:17:25,760
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: July of 2015, Your Honor. Correct.

928
05:17:26,000 --> 05:17:35,670
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: And you were part of the Compliance and Investigation Group only until August of 2017. Is that correct?

929
05:17:36,450 --> 05:17:40,430
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: 2018. Yes, Your Honor. But I'm still part of the Secretariat after.

930
05:17:41,100 --> 05:17:55,520
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: August 2017. Let's be clear about that. You were only a financial investigator for a period of 24 months. July 2015 up to August 2017. 25 months. Is that correct?

931
05:17:56,540 --> 05:17:57,480
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Roughly, Your Honor.

932
05:17:58,330 --> 05:18:15,780
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Yes. You were only a financial investigator for 25 months at the AMLA. You started in July of 2015. and ended as a financial investigator in August of 2017. Isn't that correct?

933
05:18:16,260 --> 05:18:17,040
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor.

934
05:18:17,180 --> 05:18:37,340
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: In fact, in August of 2017, you were taken out of the compliance and investigation group and reassigned to the technical services staff under the office of the Executive Director. No longer doing any form of investigation. Isn't that true?

935
05:18:38,770 --> 05:18:40,790
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: The first part of the statement is...

936
05:18:40,790 --> 05:18:50,410
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: My answer, my question is very simple. Sir, you're a lawyer, you're a CPA. You can answer it by yes or no. Your defense counsel can ask you to explain later if they want to.

937
05:18:51,370 --> 05:18:52,830
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: The question again, Your Honor?

938
05:18:53,690 --> 05:19:13,920
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: You were only a... After you were assigned from the... or taken out of the compliance and investigation group and transferred to the TSS... or Technical Services Staff under the Office of the Executive Director. Your work was really more on information campaign awareness, right?

939
05:19:14,140 --> 05:19:23,730
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Your Honor, before the witness answers, can we just ask for leeway so that the witness will be allowed to answer freely without interruption?

940
05:19:23,890 --> 05:19:32,970
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: He's on cross, counsel. You can address whatever issues he needs to clarify on redirect. Witness, will please answer the question.

941
05:19:33,310 --> 05:19:33,830
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: The answer is

942
05:19:33,830 --> 05:19:34,010
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: yes,

943
05:19:34,070 --> 05:19:35,530
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: but can I explain, Your Honor?

944
05:19:35,670 --> 05:19:38,310
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Later, if your lawyer wants to ask you to explain.

945
05:19:38,370 --> 05:19:40,250
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Can he be allowed at this time, Your Honor?

946
05:19:40,350 --> 05:19:50,870
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Counsel, the Honorable Diokno already got his answer. Again, without prejudice to you asking him to explain and redirect, we will not prohibit him.

947
05:19:52,040 --> 05:20:01,400
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: The Technical Services Staff under the Office of the Executive Director is a totally different office from the Compliance and Investigation Group, correct?

948
05:20:01,950 --> 05:20:02,590
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, your honor.

949
05:20:02,750 --> 05:20:11,690
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: In fact, the technical services staff serves as staff to the office of the executive director. It has no investigative functions at all.

950
05:20:11,830 --> 05:20:12,430
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, your honor.

951
05:20:12,740 --> 05:20:30,120
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: In other words, your only background or expertise, quote-unquote, claimed expertise as a financial investigator is the 25 months you served as an FI under the compliance and investigation group. Is that correct?

952
05:20:31,210 --> 05:20:32,830
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: May I explain, Your Honor?

953
05:20:32,950 --> 05:20:37,530
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: You may answer my question. Perhaps later you may explain if your lawyer wants to ask you.

954
05:20:37,710 --> 05:20:38,170
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor.

955
05:20:38,760 --> 05:20:45,160
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Now, you started out, what was your position, Sir? BSP ranking?

956
05:20:45,460 --> 05:20:46,440
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Bank Officer 2.

957
05:20:46,460 --> 05:20:51,900
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: And Bank Officer 2. So that is not a senior management position, am I correct?

958
05:20:52,400 --> 05:20:54,300
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor. Yes. That's entry level.

959
05:20:54,900 --> 05:21:00,590
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Entry level. And you were never promoted from bank officer too?

960
05:21:00,830 --> 05:21:01,290
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: No, Your Honor.

961
05:21:01,430 --> 05:21:20,220
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: So your expertise or your claimed expertise as a financial expert in financial investigation only comes from the 25 months you were an entry-level investigator for the AMLC. Is that correct?

962
05:21:20,640 --> 05:21:21,400
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor.

963
05:21:23,900 --> 05:21:33,560
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: You would agree with me that a financial investigation under the AMLA involves investigation of money laundering and its predicate crimes. Tama po ba iyon?

964
05:21:33,860 --> 05:21:36,580
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Money laundering, Your Honor, not the predicate crime.

965
05:21:36,860 --> 05:22:00,850
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Ah, money laundering. Thank you. I stand corrected. So iba po ang trabaho ng isang financial investigator kung ang iniinvestigahan niya ay unexplained wealth, non-declaration ng SALN, At participation in business. Wala pong kinalaman ang financial investigator ng AMLA doon sa mga bagay na iyon, hindi po ba?

966
05:22:01,090 --> 05:22:04,750
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes po. Yun po kasi ay predicate crime, iba pong ahensya.

967
05:22:05,290 --> 05:22:24,560
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Tama po iyon. Now, as a member of the TSS, yung pong technical services staff under the office of the executive director, Ang naging trabaho niyo ay capacity building at information awareness campaign. Di po ba?

968
05:22:24,820 --> 05:22:26,060
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Isa po sa mga trabaho.

969
05:22:26,400 --> 05:22:46,770
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: So your employers felt that you would be more appropriate to serve AMLA no longer as a financial investigator. I'm not yet finished, Your Honor, please. But rather, you would best... Provide services to AMLA as a member of the TSS.

970
05:22:47,270 --> 05:22:52,130
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Objection, Your Honor. The witness will not be competent to answer that question. It's also argumentative.

971
05:22:52,350 --> 05:22:56,730
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: If he knows, counsel. It's not argumentative, but if he knows.

972
05:22:57,310 --> 05:23:04,450
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Iniwan ko po yan sa discretion ng aming leadership during that time. So ako ko kasi kung ano man ang iba tong trabaho, kagawin ko natin yan.

973
05:23:05,570 --> 05:23:16,590
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Alright. Noong dalawang taon na kayo ay isang AMLA financial investigator, how long... On the average, would it take for you to complete one investigation?

974
05:23:17,950 --> 05:23:23,210
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Depende ho kung simple or complex cases. Depende ho ito.

975
05:23:24,350 --> 05:23:33,170
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Let's talk about complex cases. Sorry to interrupt you. Mga more or less, gaano katagal po yung isang investigation na gano'n?

976
05:23:35,680 --> 05:23:49,640
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Para ho makapag-come up ng isang financial investigation report, normally, three weeks to one month, or even, but it won't go beyond two months.

977
05:23:51,280 --> 05:24:07,780
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: So, in other words, your only experience actual on the ground during those 25 months was the assigned cases given to you, which according to you, complex, could take several months. Is that correct?

978
05:24:08,480 --> 05:24:11,900
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: For complex, but it's mixed with other cases, Your Honor.

979
05:24:12,040 --> 05:24:30,270
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: So let's say from July 2015 up to August of 2017, if every complex investigation took several months, you would not have been able to complete more than 20 or 30 of those. Would that be a fair statement?

980
05:24:30,630 --> 05:24:35,220
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: If the witness knows, Your Honor.

981
05:24:35,400 --> 05:24:37,980
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: I would have to overrule, counsel. Witness may answer.

982
05:24:38,320 --> 05:24:39,700
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: The question again, Your Honor.

983
05:24:41,170 --> 05:25:04,530
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Sabi po ninyo kanina na yung mga komplikadong mga investigasyon ay umaabot minsan ng ilang buwan. Considering po na kayo ay dalawang taon lamang naging financial investigator ng AMLA, yung mga natapos nyong complex na financial investigation, hindi po maaaring lumampas ng mga dalawampu o tatlumpung kaso.

984
05:25:05,830 --> 05:25:21,640
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Maaaring lumampas kasi during that time, Lean Manpower ang AMLC. So we are really multitasking. Kaya humabalik ako doon sa kanina inyong nabanggit. Ako ay nasa TSS. But the cases that I was initially assigned, I still continue handling them.

985
05:25:23,270 --> 05:25:32,650
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: At yun lang po ang masasabi niyong experience ninyo sa pag-iinvestiga ng mga pinansyal na bagay na nasa AMLC kayo.

986
05:25:32,770 --> 05:25:34,090
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: As an answer, Your Honor.

987
05:25:34,350 --> 05:25:35,310
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Move on, counsel.

988
05:25:36,220 --> 05:25:46,350
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Ngayon, You only became an accredited AMLA trainer, you said earlier, after you left already the Anti-Money Laundering Council.

989
05:25:46,790 --> 05:25:47,810
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: 2019, Your Honor.

990
05:25:48,030 --> 05:26:02,230
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: In fact, you are testifying here today based on your short stint as a financial investigator and also on your knowledge of general principles of anti-money laundering. Is that not correct?

991
05:26:02,810 --> 05:26:03,590
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor.

992
05:26:03,960 --> 05:26:13,760
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Wala po kayong... Nakita o nabasa ng kabuuan na forensic report ni Atty. Cabrera. You did not read the entire report.

993
05:26:14,340 --> 05:26:16,740
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Hindi po, Your Honor. Sa mga news lang po.

994
05:26:17,020 --> 05:26:23,420
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: You did not look at any of the bank records that Atty. Cabrera examined.

995
05:26:24,220 --> 05:26:26,360
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Hindi po dahil confidential po ito.

996
05:26:26,640 --> 05:26:35,520
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: You did not have a look at any of the records produced by the Bureau of Internal Revenue to this Court. Hindi niyo rin po naalam yun.

997
05:26:35,640 --> 05:26:37,960
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Same answer, Your Honor. Confidential po kasi ito.

998
05:26:37,960 --> 05:26:47,580
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Hindi niyo rin po nakita yung records ng SEC o Securities and Exchange Commission na binigay po nila dito sa hukumang ito.

999
05:26:47,900 --> 05:26:48,980
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Ah, hindi po, Your Honor.

1000
05:26:49,280 --> 05:26:58,660
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Pati po yung mga records na binigay ng insurance companies, lahat po ng ebidensya na nandito sa loob nitong hukumang ito, wala kayong binasa.

1001
05:26:59,390 --> 05:27:03,050
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Hindi po dahil hindi po ako yung intended end user.

1002
05:27:03,730 --> 05:27:13,910
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: So, any opinions that you may give have no basis in any factual evidence provided in this court.

1003
05:27:13,910 --> 05:27:21,810
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Objection, Your Honor. That's misleading. It already calls for a conclusion of law that only this honorable court has the function to do.

1004
05:27:21,910 --> 05:27:25,610
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Kindly reform. I know where you're getting at, Honorable Chel. Kindly reform.

1005
05:27:27,490 --> 05:27:47,050
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: You have stated, you have made a variety of opinions about The report of Atty. Cabrera about methodologies that were employed. But you have no personal knowledge of what exactly was done by Atty. Cabrera in preparing his report. Is that right?

1006
05:27:47,350 --> 05:27:47,890
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Correct, Your Honor.

1007
05:27:49,460 --> 05:27:57,100
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: So ano ngayon ang bigat ng inyong opinion kung wala naman pala kayong alam tungkol sa mga ginawa ni Atty. Cabrera?

1008
05:27:57,320 --> 05:28:04,040
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Objection, Your Honor. Question is argumentative, Your Honor. And already, again, calls for a conclusion of fact and law.

1009
05:28:06,760 --> 05:28:10,480
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: He said ano-anong ayan ang halbigat or halaga.

1010
05:28:10,740 --> 05:28:15,500
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: No, I heard a question. If you know, Attorney Rainer, if you wish to answer and if you know.

1011
05:28:15,700 --> 05:28:47,350
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor. Ang akin lang hung saligan ay ang ating amla, ang ating batas. So I can answer based on the law. I echo, I mirror what the law says. So hindi ko daw kailangan... Ako personally ayokong basahin yung report because coming here... and awala rin akong akses sa report. Coming here, reading that report, I will develop biases. I will be swayed doong report na iyon. So ang akin lang kung sinasandalan dito ay kung ano ang nasa batas.

1012
05:28:48,710 --> 05:29:01,230
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Now, your knowledge of AMLA operations is limited, your personal knowledge of AMLA operations is limited to your brief stint as a financial investigator of AMLA. Isn't that correct?

1013
05:29:01,940 --> 05:29:03,840
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Brief but meaningful. Yes, Your Honor.

1014
05:29:04,140 --> 05:29:15,620
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: And as far as any current policies, practices, procedures of the AMLA, wala po kayong personal knowledge doon mula nung kayo'y umalis noong 2018.

1015
05:29:16,380 --> 05:29:20,920
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Internal policies, none. But those that would affect covered persons, yes.

1016
05:29:22,780 --> 05:29:29,900
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Yung kaalaman ninyo about the anti-money laundering concepts ay...

1017
05:29:31,590 --> 05:29:45,300
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Na-acquire ninyo after you left. Well, let me reform. What you know about the anti-money laundering concepts is the same as what any other lawyer who reads the law would know. Isn't that right?

1018
05:29:46,100 --> 05:30:02,340
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, I respect po. Na-develop po ito nung ako'y nasa loob pa at nung ako'y lumabas na. Mas lalo na-develop because aside from getting the insights sa public sector, nakita ko rin ho, I was able to harmonize, marry kung ano ba yung meron sa private sector.

1019
05:30:02,960 --> 05:30:18,500
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Nabasa ko po yung inyong curriculum vitae. Tama po ba na wala naman ako nakita doon na meron kayong special knowledge, experience, training, or education in investigating cases of unexplained wealth. Tama po ba yan?

1020
05:30:18,700 --> 05:30:43,820
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Meron po, Your Honor. I think this was trainings conducted by USAID, anti-corruption, and then meron din po sa international. ILEA, International Law Enforcement Academy in Thailand. So meron siyang financial investigation po, session 7. So I was able to, I was sent by the office to go there and participate, represent the office po namin.

1021
05:30:44,080 --> 05:30:52,580
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: But as you mentioned earlier, your work is for the AMLA, involved financial investigation of money laundering. Tama po?

1022
05:30:52,960 --> 05:30:53,700
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Correct, Your Honor.

1023
05:30:53,920 --> 05:31:12,460
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Yes. Now, I noticed as well from your background that you, while you did serve in other agencies... Let me go through this one by one. Yung una niyong trabaho ay sa BIR, hindi po ba?

1024
05:31:12,580 --> 05:31:13,020
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Correct po.

1025
05:31:13,220 --> 05:31:17,460
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Earlier on direct, you said you served there at least one year. Is that correct?

1026
05:31:17,460 --> 05:31:19,320
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor. Working student po ako doon.

1027
05:31:19,320 --> 05:31:25,180
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: But it would appear that you were only working there for 11 months.

1028
05:31:25,600 --> 05:31:26,820
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Short of one year.

1029
05:31:27,500 --> 05:31:31,480
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Short of one year. Short of

1030
05:31:31,480 --> 05:31:31,920
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: one month.

1031
05:31:32,300 --> 05:31:43,580
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: One year short of one month with the BIR. Your second job was with Punong Bayan and Aralio. How many months did you work at Punong Bayan and Aralio?

1032
05:31:43,660 --> 05:31:45,100
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Just for two months, Your Honor.

1033
05:31:45,420 --> 05:31:56,640
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Two months. And your third job was with the GCG, Governance Commission for GLCCs. How many months did you serve in that office?

1034
05:31:57,260 --> 05:32:03,720
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Two years, Your Honor. Before, I think, almost a few months after two years.

1035
05:32:04,740 --> 05:32:11,480
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: My records indicate that you started in April 2012 and ended in January 2014. Would that be accurate?

1036
05:32:11,480 --> 05:32:12,500
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Around that time, yes, Your Honor.

1037
05:32:12,620 --> 05:32:14,820
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: So that's not two years. That's 21 months.

1038
05:32:16,930 --> 05:32:17,630
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Roughly, yeah.

1039
05:32:18,030 --> 05:32:23,610
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: And your next job was at the Commission on Elections where you served there for 17 months.

1040
05:32:23,870 --> 05:32:24,350
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor.

1041
05:32:24,350 --> 05:32:26,990
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: January 2014 to June 2015.

1042
05:32:27,710 --> 05:32:28,570
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor.

1043
05:32:29,210 --> 05:32:37,570
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: And that is the summa total of your qualifications as a financial expert that you are peddling before this court?

1044
05:32:37,890 --> 05:32:55,210
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: No, Your Honor. That is the history of my government and private employment. Insofar as financial investigation, that would start with AMLC up to until now that I'm into private practice. It continues up to the present.

1045
05:32:55,670 --> 05:33:15,210
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Now, you said you worked for Punong Bayan and Aralio for two months. So this did not give you any opportunity to learn how to conduct forensic audits, how to conduct compliance and due diligence, and other auditing services that are usually offered by these kinds of firms. Isn't that right?

1046
05:33:15,310 --> 05:33:30,690
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: I was assigned at the tax division. I am a senior tax associate. So the engagements that we handle are tax assessments. and also due diligence review. Yeah, we did that.

1047
05:33:30,990 --> 05:33:34,150
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: So wala po kayong ginawa o sinagawang forensic audits?

1048
05:33:34,490 --> 05:33:36,710
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Wala po. Iba pong grupo ang audit.

1049
05:33:37,840 --> 05:34:00,050
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Alright. Now, let me move on to, well, first of all, insofar as your work as a financial investigator, ever since you left the Anti-Money Laundering Council, Wala na po kayong contact sa mga nasa opisina ng AMLA?

1050
05:34:00,230 --> 05:34:18,930
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Wala po. After leaving the service 2018, I started my own, well, with a friend po, we started a law office. So I imposed a one year, wala po talaga, that's for one year, no AML related work. That's a, kumbaga, delikadesa na rin po namin.

1051
05:34:20,680 --> 05:34:36,310
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Thank you. You were asked about Section 8-A of Republic Act 9160. May I know, how many times was the Anti-Money Laundering Law amended?

1052
05:34:36,730 --> 05:34:37,350
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Seven times.

1053
05:34:37,830 --> 05:34:43,530
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Now, when was the Section 8A put in to the Anti-Money Laundering Law?

1054
05:34:43,630 --> 05:34:46,690
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: That's 2021 by virtue of Republic Act 11521.

1055
05:34:47,190 --> 05:34:49,070
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: So wala na po kayo sa AMLA noon?

1056
05:34:49,810 --> 05:34:50,710
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor.

1057
05:34:51,310 --> 05:35:04,080
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: And am I correct in reading that law, that particular section? That there is an exception for the orders of the Court of Competent Jurisdiction.

1058
05:35:04,320 --> 05:35:07,040
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor. That's on paragraph 2.

1059
05:35:08,230 --> 05:35:15,890
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: And since the Impeachment Court is a creation of this Constitution, the Impeachment Court is a Court of Competent Jurisdiction. Is that not right?

1060
05:35:15,950 --> 05:35:16,330
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor.

1061
05:35:17,030 --> 05:35:38,700
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Now, once that exception applies and now information is subpoenaed by the Impeachment Court, From the Anti-Money Laundering Council. At binigay na po ng Anti-Money Laundering Council yan sa court. That is now within the custody of the court. Is that not right?

1062
05:35:39,040 --> 05:35:39,800
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: The last part?

1063
05:35:39,960 --> 05:35:46,400
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Once that information is submitted to the court, that information is now in the custody of the court.

1064
05:35:46,480 --> 05:35:46,900
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Correct, Your Honor.

1065
05:35:47,100 --> 05:35:56,520
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: And it is the court that then will decide on whether what conditions that can be imposed in terms of using that

1066
05:35:58,000 --> 05:36:04,780
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor, subject to the same paragraph of Section 8-A.

1067
05:36:04,780 --> 05:36:13,520
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Yes, and in fact it's not only the impeachment court that issues subpoenas to the AMLA, even the Sandiganbayan does, am I correct?

1068
05:36:13,520 --> 05:36:14,380
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor.

1069
05:36:14,380 --> 05:36:22,940
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: And once the AMLA submits the information to the Sandiganbayan, that can now be included in the decision of the Sandiganbayan.

1070
05:36:22,940 --> 05:36:24,100
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Correct, Your Honor.

1071
05:36:24,400 --> 05:36:36,720
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Even up to the Supreme Court, that can be mentioned, right? So, wala na pong espasyo sa confidentiality yan. Basta compelled by court order ang information. Di po ba?

1072
05:36:37,180 --> 05:36:49,580
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Correct, Your Honor. Nakalagay ko kasi doon. Merong mga procedures that must be implemented for the protection, handling, and storage of access over such information.

1073
05:36:52,420 --> 05:36:54,020
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: I'm sorry, please continue.

1074
05:36:54,760 --> 05:37:03,060
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yung confidentiality na yan, hindi nahuhubad kapag yan ay napunta na sa Korte. It travels with the information.

1075
05:37:04,200 --> 05:37:18,740
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: I have to... I wonder about that because I've read and I'm... Have you ever read any Supreme Court decisions that came from an appeal from the Sandigan Bayan that discuss what was presented by AMLA?

1076
05:37:19,720 --> 05:37:20,820
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Sorry, Your Honor.

1077
05:37:22,530 --> 05:37:37,980
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Is it not a fact that once the AMLA reports are submitted to the Sandigan Bayan, as you said, they can be incorporated in the decision and therefore accessible to the public?

1078
05:37:38,820 --> 05:37:48,600
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Your Honor, the witness won't be competent to answer without the good counsel confronting him with the documents.

1079
05:37:49,140 --> 05:37:54,000
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: If he knows of a case, he was presented as an AMLC expert.

1080
05:37:54,800 --> 05:38:02,350
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Correct me if I'm wrong, Your Honor. Can the decision cite portions of the report?

1081
05:38:02,550 --> 05:38:22,960
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Is that a question? You are familiar with the cases of Ligot, among others. And you will confirm that in the decision of the Supreme Court, Mention there was made of what was presented by the Anti-Money Laundering Council, if not in the legal case, in similar cases of unexplained wealth. Okay.

1082
05:38:23,000 --> 05:38:23,660
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor.

1083
05:38:23,920 --> 05:38:35,000
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: So in that respect, ay hindi na po confidential yung galing sa AMLA kasi mismo ang Supreme Court na naglabas ng mga nilalaman ng AMLA documents.

1084
05:38:36,480 --> 05:38:50,220
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: If my memory serves me right, Your Honor, these are findings already. Process information. What... is prohibited is the raw data, intelligence report data, which is subject to verification.

1085
05:38:50,740 --> 05:38:59,560
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: So now you're making these finer distinctions that you did not make earlier. Ang sinasabi po ninyo ngayon, yung raw data lang po ang confidential.

1086
05:39:00,400 --> 05:39:05,260
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Including the investigation report, Your Honor, not just the raw data, which is a derivative.

1087
05:39:05,260 --> 05:39:12,500
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Pero yung investigation report nga po ay sinasight mismo ng Supreme Court. So paano siya magiging confidential kung ganon?

1088
05:39:12,860 --> 05:39:19,140
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Objection, Your Honor. Counsel is already arguing with the witness, Your Honor. Anyway, the witness already gave his answer.

1089
05:39:20,160 --> 05:39:21,980
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Move on to your next point, Attorney Chell.

1090
05:39:22,660 --> 05:39:31,700
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Now, earlier on your direct examination, you testified that there's no such thing as sensitivity analysis.

1091
05:39:32,620 --> 05:39:33,580
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Sa batas.

1092
05:39:33,700 --> 05:39:34,560
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Sa batas.

1093
05:39:34,700 --> 05:39:35,160
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Wala po.

1094
05:39:35,480 --> 05:39:39,860
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Ngayon, kayo po ay certified public accountant, hindi po ba?

1095
05:39:40,120 --> 05:39:41,020
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor.

1096
05:39:42,640 --> 05:39:50,460
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Am I correct in saying that that concept of sensitivity analysis is recognized in the field of accountancy?

1097
05:39:50,680 --> 05:39:51,300
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor.

1098
05:39:51,920 --> 05:39:57,560
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: So, nagagamit po yan ng mga accountants sa kanilang pag-iinvestiga, hindi po ba?

1099
05:39:57,760 --> 05:39:58,220
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor.

1100
05:39:58,680 --> 05:40:09,000
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: And there's nothing wrong with a forensic expert applying a sensitivity analysis test in his or her examination. Would that be correct?

1101
05:40:09,260 --> 05:40:09,780
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor.

1102
05:40:10,460 --> 05:40:25,120
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Now, In connection with that sensitivity analysis, meron din kayong kanina nabanggit na piercing the corporate veil can only be done by the court. Did I get you right?

1103
05:40:26,420 --> 05:40:32,420
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor. I base it on my limited knowledge of our revised corporation code.

1104
05:40:32,840 --> 05:40:51,200
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Limited knowledge of the revised corporation code. Ibig niyo bang sabihin na sa pag-analyze ng isang accountant, Odikaya, financial investigator. Hindi niya pwedeng tingnan kung sino ang totoong may-ari ng isang kumpanya?

1105
05:40:51,880 --> 05:40:55,780
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Objection, Your Honor. Misleading and already assumed sa fact that it has not been established.

1106
05:40:57,320 --> 05:41:01,060
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: It's not misleading, Your Honor. It's based on the testimony of the witness given.

1107
05:41:01,060 --> 05:41:10,580
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Misleading, Your Honor, because that's not even the concept that is contemplated by the piercing, the veil of corporate fiction, Doctor.

1108
05:41:11,120 --> 05:41:20,400
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Actually, court would like to hear the witness answer. Court has its own questions with respect to his theory in that regard at the proper time. If you know, Attorney Rainer?

1109
05:41:20,840 --> 05:41:22,320
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: May I ask again?

1110
05:41:22,320 --> 05:41:23,900
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Can you repeat the question, Honorable Chel?

1111
05:41:25,680 --> 05:41:47,700
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Let me just rephrase it. Kanina po, sinabi ninyo na ang korte lang ang pwedeng mag-pierce ng corporate veil. Ang tanong ko po, ibig nyo bang sabihin na hindi maaaring i-apply yung doctrine na yan ng isang CPA o forensic investigator?

1112
05:41:48,200 --> 05:41:50,320
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Sa kanya hong analysis, maaari.

1113
05:41:51,500 --> 05:42:03,000
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: So, wala naman pong palang pagkakamali ang ginawa ng forensic experts sa impeachment court na ito sa pag-apply ng piercing the corporate veil sa kasong ito.

1114
05:42:03,080 --> 05:42:16,100
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Objection, Your Honor. That's already misleading. Considering, Your Honor, that the good counsel already added his own interpretation to what the forensic analyst allegedly did.

1115
05:42:16,380 --> 05:42:24,710
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: No, Atty. Mark, the witness answered that it is possible, it can be used. Witness may answer. It came from his own answer.

1116
05:42:24,910 --> 05:42:34,570
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: The question again, Your Honor, kung tama ba? Yes, Your Honor, tama naman. Maaari niyang gawin yun. At ano po niyong pangalawang tanong?

1117
05:42:34,570 --> 05:42:45,520
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Wala pong ginawang pagkakamali si Atty. Cabrera nung in-apply po niya yung doctrine of piercing the corporate veil. Sa kanyang analysis sa kasong ito?

1118
05:42:45,640 --> 05:42:53,060
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Sa kanyang professional report. Wala naman po. Walang nagbabawal sa kanya na gamitin iyon.

1119
05:42:54,850 --> 05:42:56,490
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Thank you. Thank you for that.

1120
05:43:07,150 --> 05:43:16,010
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Earlier, you said that you have quote-unquote limited knowledge of constitutional law. Kayo na mismo po na nag-amin yan, di ba?

1121
05:43:16,550 --> 05:43:20,050
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor. I was subpoenaed for AML matters.

1122
05:43:20,740 --> 05:43:44,490
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: So your opinions about What is found in the Constitution are really, don't really have much... Paano po kami makakapaniwala sa sinasabi ninyo sa mga nabanggit ninyong constitutional law opinions kung mismo kayo nagsabi na limited po ang inyong kaalaman tungkol sa saligang batas?

1123
05:43:44,550 --> 05:43:54,720
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Objection, Your Honor. The witness is already incompetent to answer that question considering that he cannot delve on the minds of... His own listeners, Your Honor.

1124
05:43:54,900 --> 05:43:57,340
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: I will withdraw the question, Your Honor.

1125
05:43:57,600 --> 05:44:00,000
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you. You may proceed, Atty. Arnabuchel.

1126
05:44:03,670 --> 05:44:21,670
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Now, earlier as well, you said that you were asked about legitimate income and you answered to the effect that legitimate income would include income derived from one's profession or business activities. Did I hear you right?

1127
05:44:22,400 --> 05:44:24,240
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Correct, Your Honor. Correct, Your Honor.

1128
05:44:24,940 --> 05:44:48,710
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: But if a certain official of the Executive Department is expressly prohibited by the Constitution from receiving any emoluments other than what they receive from their salary, ay hindi na rin po legitimate income yung kita mula sa profesyon. Kasi pinagbabawal mismo ng Constitution eh.

1129
05:44:51,010 --> 05:44:58,730
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: To the impeachment court to decide whether they would consider this as legitimate or illegitimate given the facts surrounding the case.

1130
05:44:59,150 --> 05:45:14,670
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: But you would agree with me that under Section 13, Article 7 of the Constitution, the Vice President is not allowed to receive any emoluments other than her salary as Vice President. You would agree with that legal statement?

1131
05:45:15,070 --> 05:45:26,560
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Objection, Your Honor. Again, already calls for a conclusion of law. And that's precisely the question that the court needs to resolve in this impeachment case.

1132
05:45:26,800 --> 05:45:30,940
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: I think the Honorable Chel is quoting the constitutional provision itself. Would that be correct?

1133
05:45:31,160 --> 05:45:31,940
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Yes, Your Honor.

1134
05:45:32,600 --> 05:45:38,920
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: But he's asking already for an interpretation of such provision, Your Honor, that favors their position, Your Honor.

1135
05:45:39,120 --> 05:45:45,500
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: He also did that, Atty. Mark, but the witness simply answered he defers to the court. He may do so again now.

1136
05:45:45,880 --> 05:45:46,900
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: We will submit, Your Honor.

1137
05:45:48,460 --> 05:45:50,120
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Yes, Atty. Rainer, if you know.

1138
05:45:50,580 --> 05:45:52,780
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: If it is what is written in the Constitution, yes, Your Honor.

1139
05:45:53,990 --> 05:46:07,910
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: So, would your answer now change about what is legitimate income, considering that for the Vice President, income from a profession is not allowed while the Vice President is sitting as such?

1140
05:46:08,700 --> 05:46:11,820
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Again, I leave it to the discretion of the Honorable Court, Your Honor.

1141
05:46:13,170 --> 05:46:34,270
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Now, question. Earlier, you were shown snippets of the report of Attorney Cabrera. You have already testified that you didn't read the whole report. Wouldn't you agree that context means a lot in terms of evaluating the veracity of a financial report?

1142
05:46:34,610 --> 05:46:38,970
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Objection. Question is vague, Your Honor. Context means a lot. What does that mean?

1143
05:46:40,760 --> 05:46:42,960
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: I think the witness is intelligent enough

1144
05:46:42,960 --> 05:46:44,740
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: to be able to understand the question.

1145
05:46:45,900 --> 05:46:47,380
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Witness may answer if you know.

1146
05:46:47,580 --> 05:47:02,930
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: As much as I want to read. Your Honor, I have no access over this information. I did my research, reading the news, watching some of the audio clips, and that's it.

1147
05:47:04,010 --> 05:47:16,010
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Let's turn this around. Let's say that I were going to evaluate your investigation report. Kayo po ba ay nakapagsubmit hindi po ba ng investigation report sa Anti-Money Laundering Council?

1148
05:47:16,030 --> 05:47:16,370
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor.

1149
05:47:16,850 --> 05:47:28,770
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Pero sa pag-husga ko, sa pag-evaluate ko ng inyong report, hindi ko muna babasahin yung kabuuan. Hahanap lang ako ng ilan ng mga portion doon. Don't you think that would be unfair to you?

1150
05:47:29,250 --> 05:47:32,270
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Objection, Your Honor. It's a speculative question, Your Honor.

1151
05:47:32,820 --> 05:47:36,020
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: I think the witness is capable of answering that, Your Honor.

1152
05:47:36,080 --> 05:48:02,480
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Allow me, Counsel. Atty. Rainer, ang pinupunto lamang naman po ni Hon. Diokno, importante ang konteksto. Ibig sabihin, yung kabuuan... Report para maunawaan yung parte nito at yung mga conclusion nito. Sangahin po ba kayo sa statement na yun na mahalaga ang konteksto at medyo may pagkukulang kapag hindi nyo nakita yung kabuhang report sa pagbibigay ng komentaryo kaugnay sa parte o bahagi lamang ng report?

1153
05:48:02,960 --> 05:48:14,720
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Correct, Your Honor. Pero ang pagbabahagi ho ng aking opinion sa report ay base lamang ibabanggahos kung ano mang provided ng batas. So I am not countering his or her conclusions.

1154
05:48:22,660 --> 05:48:42,980
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: As to the acceptability or not, again, we respect the professional, personal opinion of the forensic accountant who did that. But it should have been done within the bounds of law. Yun lang ang aking role. I do not question. Nasa sa ating impeachment court na huyon kung kanila bang tatanggapin o hindi.

1155
05:48:43,680 --> 05:48:46,360
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: You cannot

1156
05:48:46,360 --> 05:48:52,020
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: cite any specific action done by Atty. Cabrera that violates the law.

1157
05:48:52,810 --> 05:49:00,800
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Based on the circumstances, again, it's up to the impeachment court.

1158
05:49:00,860 --> 05:49:10,400
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Sir, my question is very simple. Meron pa ba kayong maipapakita ng mismong paglabag ng batas doon sa report ni Atty. Cabrera?

1159
05:49:13,280 --> 05:49:18,300
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Your Honor, again, the witness was not able to peruse the actual report, Your Honor.

1160
05:49:18,560 --> 05:49:47,500
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: As to the portion shown to you, Atty. Rainer, as to the portion shown to you, you testified, you made observations earlier, you expressed your opinion earlier. The question of Atty. The Honorable Chel is quite clear. On the portion shown to you and methodology used as described by the counsel when he was asking questions, were any laws, did Atty. Cabrera in his methodology and their presentation violate any laws. In your opinion?

1161
05:49:48,350 --> 05:49:59,870
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: At Section 8 of RA 9160 as amended. On confidentiality. On confidentiality to a private individual.

1162
05:50:00,310 --> 05:50:08,070
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Ito yung pagbibigay ng prosecution o ng komite sa kanya ng kopya para pag-aralan, suriin, at pagbasihan ng report. That's the violation.

1163
05:50:08,470 --> 05:50:17,950
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Pero ito ay, again, depende na ho sa aggrieved party. If he or she will... Pursue that case. So again, nandun na po tayo nakadepende. And

1164
05:50:17,950 --> 05:50:22,850
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: that is the only legal provision that you can cite? Nothing else?

1165
05:50:24,320 --> 05:50:35,920
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: That's the only legal provision on confidentiality, Your Honor. Section 8-A, in relation to that, we have the penal provision on Section 14-D.

1166
05:50:36,300 --> 05:50:38,460
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Yes, so those two related provisions.

1167
05:50:38,800 --> 05:50:39,160
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor.

1168
05:50:39,380 --> 05:50:59,710
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Now, considering that the impeachment court itself has allowed Presentation of the Anti-Money Laundering Council Records and also allowed the testimony of Attorney Cabrera. Is it your opinion that that provision is still being violated by the Impeachment Court?

1169
05:50:59,810 --> 05:51:30,500
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Objection, Your Honor. Question is misleading. What the witness answered was that it was a violation of 8A because the AMLC documents or materials were provided by the prosecution. A third party. Now the counsel is implying your honor that the court authorized such disclosure but the court will never admit your honor that it issued any order authorizing the release of those AMLC documents to attorney Cabrera.

1170
05:51:31,080 --> 05:51:46,470
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Share confirms that and I believe the prosecution admitted that they gave a copy to attorney Cabrera much much earlier based on the documents received by the Committee on Justice, by virtue of a subpoena issued by the Committee on Justice. Move along, counsel.

1171
05:51:46,730 --> 05:52:10,420
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Thank you, Your Honor. Earlier, you questioned the report's reliance or, according to you, use of official receipts from Jollibee Corporation. Ayun pong pinakita sa inyong mga resibo. Those are considered as official receipts from the branches involved, right?

1172
05:52:11,020 --> 05:52:11,500
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, sir.

1173
05:52:11,550 --> 05:52:16,370
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: So in other words, those documents have evidentiary weight.

1174
05:52:17,590 --> 05:52:20,990
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Depende ho yan sa ating impeachment court if they will take it.

1175
05:52:21,350 --> 05:52:31,270
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: In fact, if a corporation issues a receipt and states that it is their corporation that is issuing the receipt, that is in the nature of an admission by the corporation, is it not?

1176
05:52:31,270 --> 05:52:37,420
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Objection, Your Honor. It already calls for conclusions of facts and law, and the witness will not be able to testify on those.

1177
05:52:37,420 --> 05:52:42,100
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Your Honor, the witness is a lawyer and a CPA. I believe if he knows, he can provide an answer. But

1178
05:52:42,100 --> 05:52:44,260
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: it was not covered in his testimony.

1179
05:52:44,460 --> 05:52:47,480
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: I am entitled to question him on this point on cross-law.

1180
05:52:47,480 --> 05:52:52,200
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: We're giving him enough leeway, counsel. Witness may answer if he knows on the receipts.

1181
05:52:52,420 --> 05:52:55,100
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Ano po, Lee, yung specific question, Your Honor?

1182
05:52:55,980 --> 05:53:03,360
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Yung pong mga official receipt na ini-issue ng isang kumpanya ay meron pong evidentiary weight yun, di ba?

1183
05:53:04,320 --> 05:53:13,360
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: It's not the best evidence obtainable, po. There are... Better evidences po sa ating official certified true copies.

1184
05:53:13,760 --> 05:53:29,540
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Well, thank you for that. That really wasn't my question. My question is very simple. When a company issues an official receipt and states that it was that company that issued the receipt, mapikat po na ebidensya yun, hindi po ba?

1185
05:53:29,720 --> 05:53:40,110
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Objection. As an answer, Your Honor, the witness already distinguished Your Honor. The evidentiary weight of such document vis-a-vis other official documents.

1186
05:53:40,110 --> 05:53:41,820
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Move on, counsel. We get the point.

1187
05:53:41,820 --> 05:53:58,660
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Thank you, Your Honor. I just have a few more questions on cross-examination, but if I may be given just a minute or two to confer with my colleagues, there may be other points that I will raise, if I may, Your Honor.

1188
05:53:58,660 --> 05:54:00,840
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Without calling a recess, you may do so, counsel.

1189
05:54:11,540 --> 05:54:13,980
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: We will entertain some interjections then.

1190
05:54:16,210 --> 05:54:17,350
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: From one or two,

1191
05:54:25,120 --> 05:54:27,980
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Senator Judge Sotto, former Senate President is recognized.

1192
05:54:31,080 --> 05:54:33,400
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: You may proceed with the interjection, sir. You have two minutes.

1193
05:54:39,680 --> 05:54:44,220
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: Actually, I have one or two questions, only Mr. Presiding Officer. Thank you.

1194
05:54:47,060 --> 05:54:54,250
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: Mr. Witness, Attorney Dela Fuente, when did you author that AML handbook?

1195
05:54:55,580 --> 05:55:03,620
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: July of 2025, Your Honor. It was published, but initial works here started in 2024.

1196
05:55:05,870 --> 05:55:12,790
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: You worked with the AMLC from 2015 to 2018 only, correct?

1197
05:55:13,110 --> 05:55:13,710
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor.

1198
05:55:16,940 --> 05:55:19,980
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: Where were you in January 2021?

1199
05:55:22,090 --> 05:55:30,180
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: January pandemic work, Your Honor, or the actual place?

1200
05:55:30,400 --> 05:55:32,580
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: What work? What was your work then?

1201
05:55:33,040 --> 05:55:36,080
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: I was a partner at Gialogo de la Fuente and Associates.

1202
05:55:36,220 --> 05:55:37,700
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: No longer with AMLC.

1203
05:55:38,020 --> 05:55:38,720
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor.

1204
05:55:38,940 --> 05:55:42,580
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: Yes. We amended the law in January 2021.

1205
05:55:42,920 --> 05:55:43,520
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Ah, yes, Your Honor.

1206
05:55:43,760 --> 05:55:44,160
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: Thank you.

1207
05:55:46,490 --> 05:55:53,420
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Honorable Chel, are you ready? Senator Judge Lacson, what is your pleasure, sir? Okay. Honorable Chel, you're ready?

1208
05:55:58,350 --> 05:56:01,430
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Not yet? Senator Judge Lacson, what is your pleasure, sir?

1209
05:56:04,430 --> 05:56:35,540
Sen. Panfilo “Ping” M. Lacson: Thank you, sir. Presiding Officer. I had actually... Interjected on the issue involving the claim of the same defense counsel about weaponizing AMLC, the AMLC, for political persecution and harassment, when then Executive Director Buenaventura was our witness. Since Atty. Vinluan brought it up again, pinapull out ko na po yung TSN para mas accurate.

1210
05:56:35,740 --> 05:56:37,560
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: I remember, Honorable Lacson.

1211
05:56:38,310 --> 05:56:50,610
Sen. Panfilo “Ping” M. Lacson: And ang tanong ko po sa witness, familiar pa kayo sa history or provenance ng Section 16 ng AMLA? Kung saan ang galing yung Section 16?

1212
05:56:51,030 --> 05:56:52,370
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Attorney Rainer, kindly respond.

1213
05:56:52,630 --> 05:56:54,170
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Not that familiar,

1214
05:56:54,370 --> 05:56:54,630
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Your Honor.

1215
05:56:54,930 --> 05:57:19,020
Sen. Panfilo “Ping” M. Lacson: But I'll tell you, no? Historical. Yeah. Ang nag-introduce niyan, Senator Sotto, Sotto Amendment. Actually, yung kasama niya nag-introduce dito, patay na rin pareho. Si late Joker Arroyo, Senator Arroyo, and Senator Ople, as well as Senator Angara. Siya na lang po ang naiwan.

1216
05:57:21,300 --> 05:58:04,980
Sen. Panfilo “Ping” M. Lacson: Well, I can say na, following yung interjection ni Senators Sotto and Ople, pwede natin madeduce natin na yung present provision of Section 16 on prohibitions against political harassment of the money laundering law including the AMLC on the prohibition against political persecution and harassment was really for the protection not only of trade and commerce but also of a candidate sa eleksyon. Diyan po nagsimula yan. So general lang yung paragraph 1, actually yung 2 yung specific, yun nga inintroduce ni Senator Sotto at that time.

1217
05:58:07,180 --> 05:59:13,610
Sen. Panfilo “Ping” M. Lacson: Kaya nasa amin yung trade and commerce kasi yun yung mga contributors eh. Baka maharas. So hindi pwedeng i-interpret na in a general sense like an impeachment trial na i-apply yung political persecution. Kasi po ako noong 2001 hanggang 2000 when I ended my term in 2013, subject po ako ng political persecution. Money laundering din. Sinasabi nung dating administration ay stashed sa mga foreign banks hundreds of millions of US dollars. Yun ang political persecution. Hindi ko ginamit yung prohibition kasi hindi applicable. Kasi nga applicability ng Section 16, papunta lamang doon sa election period para huwag maharas yung kandidato. I would just like to reiterate that kasi laging nabibring up yung political harassment. Asaka persecution dito sa impeachment trial. Hindi po yung intent and purpose of that provision. Yun lamang po, Mr. Presiding Officer.

1218
05:59:13,830 --> 05:59:20,570
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you, Senator Judge Lacson. Honorable Chell, you may proceed with your cross and wind up.

1219
05:59:21,140 --> 05:59:38,730
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Thank you. Thank you, Your Honor. Earlier, Mr. Witness, good afternoon. You testified that you felt that two weeks was medyo mahirap para magpapagsagawa ng isang financial... Investigation. Tama po ba yan?

1220
05:59:39,290 --> 05:59:41,810
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Challenging po yan. Mahira po.

1221
05:59:42,170 --> 06:00:00,830
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: But that is on the assumption that the person involved only had two weeks. If that person had several months to begin their examination and as records came in, continued to examine the documents, walang pong issue ang two weeks. Tama po ba?

1222
06:00:01,350 --> 06:00:01,910
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor.

1223
06:00:02,130 --> 06:00:12,560
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Thank you. Now, let me just wind up. I just want to summarize several points that you have mentioned.

1224
06:00:15,220 --> 06:00:25,100
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: You're not saying to this Court that the AMLA records, that the records submitted by AMLA are inaccurate or untruthful. Wala namang kayong sinasabing ganun.

1225
06:00:25,140 --> 06:00:25,920
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Wala po iyon.

1226
06:00:26,080 --> 06:00:29,220
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: You're not saying that the records submitted by the BIR

1227
06:00:31,230 --> 06:00:37,330
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: SEC, and other government agencies are tampered or fabricated. Hindi mo rin sinasabi yun.

1228
06:00:37,450 --> 06:00:38,030
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: None, Your Honor.

1229
06:00:38,330 --> 06:00:45,550
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Hindi niyo rin sinasabi na hindi totoo yung mga bank records na sinabmit ng mga bank o sa hukumang ito.

1230
06:00:46,230 --> 06:00:47,050
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: None, Your Honor.

1231
06:00:47,330 --> 06:01:00,820
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Hindi niyo rin sinasabi, aside from yung mga nabanggit niyo, mga snippets ng report ni Atty. Cabrera, Meron pang ibang mga questionable parts ng report niya dahil hindi mo naman nabasa yung kabuuan.

1232
06:01:01,120 --> 06:01:03,340
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Kung ano lang po yung napakita sa akin, Your Honor.

1233
06:01:04,580 --> 06:01:14,920
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Hindi niyo rin sinasabi na, in fact, kanina pinupurin niyo yung qualifications ni Atty. Cabrera bilang forensic expert. So you're not questioning his qualifications.

1234
06:01:15,420 --> 06:01:18,240
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: I still respect him as a fellow professional.

1235
06:01:18,660 --> 06:01:38,420
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: No question. Kasi baka po magka hindi kayo maintindihan o hindi malinaw sa publiko. Kayo po ba, sinasabi ba ninyo na pag walang money laundering, wala rin unexplained wealth? Ano po? Pag walang money laundering, walang unexplained wealth?

1236
06:01:39,000 --> 06:01:48,070
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Baliktad po. Money laundering is a derivative offense. So, it has to depend on a... Wala kong ilo-launder kung walang krimeng nangyari.

1237
06:01:48,290 --> 06:02:27,770
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: So, kahit na wala kayong mahanap na ebidensya ng money laundering, pero... Mapatunayan yung requirements ng unexplained wealth sa ilalim ng Republic Act 3019 Section 8 ay pwede pa rin po magka-finding ng unexplained wealth. So tama po yung sinabi ko. Even if there is no case or finding of money laundering, a case for unexplained wealth can still prosper If the evidence is there to prove unexplained well.

1238
06:02:27,790 --> 06:02:28,230
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor.

1239
06:02:28,450 --> 06:02:30,390
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Thank you. Ngayon,

1240
06:02:32,340 --> 06:02:38,840
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: nakausap niyo si Defense Counsel bago po kayo na upo dito?

1241
06:02:39,120 --> 06:02:40,700
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Unfortunately, hindi po.

1242
06:02:42,480 --> 06:02:53,110
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: So, hindi po niya naipaliwanag sa inyo kung ano talaga yung nasa loob ng Article 2 ng Articles of Impeachment?

1243
06:02:53,390 --> 06:02:54,570
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Hindi po, Your Honor.

1244
06:02:54,860 --> 06:02:58,720
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: At hindi nyo rin nabasa bago ngayon yung laman.

1245
06:02:58,720 --> 06:03:01,780
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Sa balita po, nabasa po yung laman ng article.

1246
06:03:01,800 --> 06:03:02,700
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: I'm sorry, hindi ko.

1247
06:03:02,880 --> 06:03:03,840
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Sa balita po, Your Honor.

1248
06:03:04,140 --> 06:03:09,350
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Ah, sa balita. Pero yung mismong dokumento na Article 2, you have not read?

1249
06:03:09,550 --> 06:03:09,870
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Not.

1250
06:03:10,810 --> 06:03:29,380
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Now, that may perhaps be the difficulty in your testimony. Kasi po, ang batayan ng Article 2, kung babasahin po ninyo yung laman, Ay hindi naman po Republic Act 9160.

1251
06:03:30,080 --> 06:03:31,500
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Objection, Your Honor. Sorry to interrupt.

1252
06:03:31,640 --> 06:03:32,640
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: I have no question yet.

1253
06:03:32,640 --> 06:03:57,370
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: I understand that. But Your Honor, Good Counsel already used the terms difficulty. So in other words, again, Your Honor, with all due respect, it's not the prosecution's function to interpret the... or give probative value to the testimony of the witness. It is the function of the court. He can just ask questions, Your Honor, to test his credibility.

1254
06:03:57,930 --> 06:04:08,610
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: I haven't heard a question yet, Attorney Mark. Kindly restate your question, Honorable Chell. I don't believe you've asked a question yet.

1255
06:04:08,790 --> 06:04:22,260
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Not yet, Your Honor. Since you did not get to read Article 2 of the Articles of Impeachment, you do not know that This article is based on Republic Act 3019.

1256
06:04:22,680 --> 06:04:32,860
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Based on the news, Your Honor, and the research that I did before coming in here, yes, I know that it's based on that Republic Act.

1257
06:04:32,860 --> 06:04:44,360
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: So you confirm that this article on unexplained wealth is based, one of the laws is Republic Act 3019, anti-graphic corrupt practices law. You confirm that?

1258
06:04:44,660 --> 06:04:45,040
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor.

1259
06:04:45,120 --> 06:04:54,170
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: You confirm as well that Law is in relation to the provisions of Republic Act 1379 on civil forfeiture.

1260
06:04:55,820 --> 06:04:56,800
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor.

1261
06:04:56,960 --> 06:05:05,920
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: You also confirm that Article 2 is based on Republic Act 6713, your code of conduct of public officials and employees.

1262
06:05:06,540 --> 06:05:07,360
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor.

1263
06:05:07,480 --> 06:05:37,000
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: And most especially, you confirm that the allegations of unexplained wealth, amassing of wealth manifestly disproportional to the lawful income of the respondent, the allegations of participation in business that is prohibited by law, as well as the non-declaration of salary. These are all based on the Constitution of our country.

1264
06:05:37,440 --> 06:05:38,200
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, sir.

1265
06:05:39,060 --> 06:05:40,580
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Thank you. No

1266
06:05:45,320 --> 06:05:46,140
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: more questions, Your Honor.

1267
06:05:46,380 --> 06:05:47,140
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Redirect, Your Honor.

1268
06:05:47,300 --> 06:05:48,520
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Redirect, Attorney Mark.

1269
06:05:49,580 --> 06:06:14,430
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Good afternoon. Kunti na lang po, Attorney De La Fuente. During cross-examination, you were questioned about your limited time with the AMLC or particularly the AMLC Secretariat. However, you also characterized your stint with the AMLC as brief and meaningful. Can you explain that? Bakit yung po nasabi yan?

1270
06:06:15,050 --> 06:06:57,430
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yung aking competence and experience, it's not counted by the quantity of years that I have been with the Secretariat. So it's not on the quantity but the quality of work. Kung mahaba nga akong oras ninyo, pero for lack of better term, pabanjing-banjing ka lang, wala rin yung, it's not meaningful experience. Now, when I left the Council na Secretariat noong 2018, if hindi maganda ang aking record, probably they won't accredit me 2019. Other than that, I also got another accreditation from PAGCOR. Again, if hindi naging maganda ang aking record, ang aking trabaho, I won't be able to get those approvals.

1271
06:06:57,870 --> 06:07:03,830
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Art, you mentioned yung accreditation na yun from AMLA. This is already beyond your stint sa AMLC?

1272
06:07:05,010 --> 06:07:08,910
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor. That's 2019, a year after I left the service.

1273
06:07:09,250 --> 06:07:20,460
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Correct. But yet, you described... Another function which is an accredited trainer of the AMLC. Paano po ba ito? Can you describe your functions kahit nawala na po kayo sa AMLC?

1274
06:07:20,780 --> 06:07:40,760
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Well, napaka-importante kasi, no, that we make the public, especially the covered persons, aware of their obligations, no, AML obligations. Sa dami ho ng ating covered persons, hindi ho yan na-accommodate lahat ng ating AMLC Secretariat. So they accredit private

1275
06:07:42,320 --> 06:08:10,700
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Individuals and also institutional training providers. They subject to vetting process. Ini-screen ho yan. Do you have the proper experience, competence? So meron din hong tine-check. Nagkaroon ng demo lectures. If we follow the syllabus of the AMLC. So hindi ho siya basta-basta pinoprovide. Meron hong proseso bago kabigyan ng accreditation.

1276
06:08:11,230 --> 06:08:22,870
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Thank you for that clarification. So, in terms of training of or training with AMLC people, how would you characterize your work kahit na wala na po kayo sa AMLC?

1277
06:08:24,310 --> 06:08:30,850
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: I still do maintain good relationship with them. But again, hiwalay ko ang personal sa professional.

1278
06:08:31,390 --> 06:08:35,850
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright. And then you also mentioned that you have extensive...

1279
06:08:37,370 --> 06:08:46,450
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Experience in financial investigation despite your limited time with the AMLC. Paano niyo po nasabi na extensive yung naging experience niyo?

1280
06:08:46,910 --> 06:08:53,770
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Lahat ho ng klase ng trabaho ng isang financial investigator na daanan na ho. In fact, that's the reason why I left the service.

1281
06:08:55,390 --> 06:09:15,660
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Natatakot na ho ang aking pamilya dahil sa risk. So, when I reached that point, I think I already contributed enough. For the service, that's the time for me to think about my family and also my personal career. That's why I left the service and also tried to establish my own law office.

1282
06:09:16,020 --> 06:09:48,700
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Thank you po for that clarification. On cross, you also mentioned about yung Section 8A ng AMLA. And again, we don't have any question with the authority of this court. In fact, yung questions po on direct. Really pertained on the proceedings or processes before the House Committee on Justice. If you can just distinguish po ba, paano po ba naiiba yung proceedings ng impeachment court na ito sa ibang mga proceedings na hindi naman po court?

1283
06:09:49,480 --> 06:10:15,730
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Well, normally, when we go to the financial investigation part, marami po munang pinagdadaanan yan. Council approval, and then you file a petition with the Court of Appeals for freeze order. and Bank Inquiry. So marami kong pinagdadaan ng proseso yan. Dito sa ating impeachment court, again, the court is free to adopt its own rules and request subpoenaed documents from agencies such as AMLOC po.

1284
06:10:15,970 --> 06:10:37,170
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright, thank you po. Now, you also mentioned that subpoenaed documents, no? I understand that may mga subpoenaed documents yung court. But again, just to clarify, what is the propriety of disclosing even subpoenaed documents to a third party? If you can just answer.

1285
06:10:38,620 --> 06:11:01,840
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Again, that would contravene the second paragraph. It is authorized disclosure but re-disseminating, re-forwarding that information without observing the proper guidelines is I think a violation. Section 8-A.

1286
06:11:03,080 --> 06:11:17,280
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Okay. Na-mention din po yung maraming question on cross yung kay Atty. Cabrera. Yung disclosure po kay Atty. Cabrera, what is the propriety of that without the proper court order? If you just can answer.

1287
06:11:17,520 --> 06:11:36,940
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Again, sorry. I have no personal knowledge as to how it was submitted to him, how it was shared to him. Ako po ay nakabase lang sa batas. At plainly, nasa ating Section 2, Section 8-A, na dapat ho may sinunod na proper protocols.

1288
06:11:38,060 --> 06:12:03,680
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Thank you po. You were also asked about piercing the corporate veil. Sinabi nyo on direct na it is the court that has the authority to do that pero on cross sinabi nyo naman din na if I can recall that wala namang problema kung gawin nyo ng forensic act. How do you reconcile those two concepts?

1289
06:12:04,360 --> 06:12:05,380
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Again, Your Honor, sorry.

1290
06:12:05,680 --> 06:12:18,080
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Kasi sinabi niyo po on direct na it is the court that has the authority to pierce. Pero on cross, tinatanong kayo si Atty. Cabrera kasi nag-pierce din siya ng corporate. So how do you reconcile po?

1291
06:12:18,400 --> 06:12:54,490
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Well, the so-called piercing made by the forensic is only for analysis. It's not, again, dalabaho ang... Financial intelligence, which is analytical, at saka financial investigation. In my own humble opinion, what he did is, on the first part, analytical. It's not yet evidence gathering that would trigger yung mga compulsive or coercive processes. So, in that case, that is only for case build-up. Fact-finding lang ho yun. Hindi pa siya ebidensya.

1292
06:12:58,960 --> 06:13:17,840
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: You were also confronted with the fact that you did not access yung mga actual CTRs and STRs para hindi niyo po, and you said na hindi niyo po mako-confront yung report ni Atty. Cabrera on this. Ano nga po ulit yung reason why you did not access these reports?

1293
06:13:18,300 --> 06:13:39,000
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Well, the only reason, Your Honor, is that, well, that's confidential. I do what I preach. If I'm saying that this is confidential, I also observe that. Even if maganda sana makita ko, but I am not the intended end user of the documents. So why would I bother looking into those documents?

1294
06:13:39,910 --> 06:13:54,110
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Thank you po. You were also confronted about the idea, yung money laundering versus yung unlawful activity case. Can you just explain to us ano nga po ba yung pagkakaiba nito?

1295
06:13:55,870 --> 06:14:17,090
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Money laundering is a derivative offense. It has to depend on the prior unlawful activity. Hindi nakadepende ang pagpapafile ng unlawful activity kung mayroong money laundering. Baliktad, dapat nakadepende ang money laundering sa existence ng unlawful activity.

1296
06:14:17,780 --> 06:14:21,480
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: And yung unlawful activity na po yun, yun po yung source?

1297
06:14:23,880 --> 06:14:27,080
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Sino po yung may responsibility to prove that?

1298
06:14:27,770 --> 06:14:35,410
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: In our current proceedings, it is the Honorable Impeachment Court who will be determining if there is an unlawful activity or not.

1299
06:14:35,790 --> 06:14:37,770
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Okay. Based on the allegations?

1300
06:14:38,070 --> 06:14:38,870
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Based on the allegations.

1301
06:14:41,490 --> 06:14:53,370
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: And sino po ba yung may responsibility to gather or collate the necessary evidence to prove that unlawful activity? Kung meron pong mga...

1302
06:14:55,010 --> 06:14:56,510
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Allegations on money laundering.

1303
06:14:56,650 --> 06:15:17,650
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Your Honor, please. This line of questioning is very misleading. The presiding officer himself has stated categorically that the respondent is not being charged with money laundering and yet the defense counsel is making it appear that it is the impeachment court that will make a decision about unlawful activities. Wala po sa issue dito pa yan.

1304
06:15:17,850 --> 06:15:18,850
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: If he knows, Your Honor.

1305
06:15:19,180 --> 06:15:32,560
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: For the information of the witness, it is not part of the charges against the Vice President, given your admission that you have not yet read the actual articles of impeachment. It is not. With that in mind, kindly answer the question of Attorney Mark.

1306
06:15:32,560 --> 06:15:35,200
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Can you repeat the question?

1307
06:15:35,200 --> 06:16:00,680
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Because you were, you were explaining the logical sequence between a Logical sequence involving predicate crime or unlawful activity and money laundering. My question is very simple. Who has the burden of gathering evidence for unlawful activity or predicate crime to support any money laundering?

1308
06:16:00,880 --> 06:16:02,080
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: In this case, the prosecution.

1309
06:16:05,100 --> 06:16:14,920
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: If your honor, please, I move to strike the answer of the witness considering that the presiding officer himself already informed this witness that money laundering is not...

1310
06:16:15,340 --> 06:16:18,140
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: It is not one of the charges, Atty. Raynor.

1311
06:16:18,160 --> 06:16:19,080
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes.

1312
06:16:19,080 --> 06:16:20,060
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Asked and answered, Your Honor.

1313
06:16:20,420 --> 06:16:24,600
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: It's not up for the prosecution, Atty. Raynor.

1314
06:16:27,130 --> 06:16:36,250
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: With the knowledge that it's not part of the articles of impeachment that the Vice President is supposed to answer to or respond to, that's your answer? It's up for the prosecution?

1315
06:16:37,030 --> 06:16:43,710
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: I think the question is who has the burden of proving the unlawful activity?

1316
06:16:44,480 --> 06:16:54,180
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Yes, Your Honor. In that sequence, only based on that scenario that there is an unlawful activity or predicate crime and then there's a money laundering aspect as well.

1317
06:16:54,700 --> 06:17:02,660
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: I would object then, Your Honor. The question is irrelevant in the material since the respondent is not being charged with any money laundering offense.

1318
06:17:03,020 --> 06:17:10,800
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: No, I'll allow it because it presupposes a predicate crime, which the counsel for the prosecutors also asked. Witness may answer.

1319
06:17:13,450 --> 06:17:20,120
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Kindly answer, Attorney Reg. Who has the burden of proving? What was your question, Attorney Mark?

1320
06:17:22,380 --> 06:17:31,320
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Who has the burden of proving that particular aspect on unlawful activity? The unlawful activity. The predicate crime, yes.

1321
06:17:32,130 --> 06:17:38,420
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: The prosecution, your honor. Yes. Burden of proving the existence of the unlawful activity.

1322
06:17:38,940 --> 06:17:44,160
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: And again, just for clarity, what is the burden of proof in these types of accusations or allegations?

1323
06:17:45,160 --> 06:17:57,450
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Well, in impeachment. Or normally, if the normal case is, Your Honor, well, I'll prove beyond reasonable doubt. This is a criminal case.

1324
06:17:58,600 --> 06:17:59,960
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: That will be all, Your Honor.

1325
06:18:00,220 --> 06:18:02,280
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Rick Ross, Honorable Chell.

1326
06:18:02,580 --> 06:18:04,300
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: With the permission of the...

1327
06:18:04,300 --> 06:18:04,980
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: You may proceed, sir.

1328
06:18:06,690 --> 06:18:11,850
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Don't you think that your statement about the quality of your work is self-serving?

1329
06:18:13,810 --> 06:18:14,290
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Well...

1330
06:18:14,290 --> 06:18:15,390
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Objection, Your Honor.

1331
06:18:15,450 --> 06:18:16,430
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: I know myself, Your Honor.

1332
06:18:18,460 --> 06:18:19,840
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Question is argumentative, Your Honor.

1333
06:18:20,000 --> 06:18:22,040
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: It is argumentative, Honorable Chad.

1334
06:18:22,080 --> 06:18:36,490
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: I will move on. In other words, Mr. Witness, your own evaluation of your work, you have concluded that you have high quality work. That's why you said your stint in the AMLC has been brief and meaningful.

1335
06:18:37,510 --> 06:18:38,910
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Objection, Your Honor. Same objection.

1336
06:18:39,790 --> 06:18:43,870
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: It was phrased properly, Counsel. Witness, may answer?

1337
06:18:46,750 --> 06:19:20,980
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: I did not mention the... Word high quality. I just mentioned quality. So it's based on perception. So I see myself, well, during my time, I think the cases that I handled, they showcased it when we had meetings with law enforcement agencies. Yung mga kasong hinawakan ko, yun yung mga pinapakita namin with our counterparts to show how it is done. So that recognition from my superiors, I think, is... An affirmation of the quality of work that I did.

1338
06:19:22,100 --> 06:19:34,270
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: I'll go back to that in a minute. I just have one other question, sir. Yung nabanggit niyo ang burden of proof, proof beyond reasonable doubt, applicable lang po yan sa mga criminal cases, hindi po ba? Yes, po?

1339
06:19:34,830 --> 06:19:42,670
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor. That's the, yun po yung nilatagganin ang question sa akin. Kaya I also, that's the normal burden of proof po.

1340
06:19:43,210 --> 06:20:03,260
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Going back to your statement of having a brief but meaningful stint at AMLA and that you have quality work, tama po ba ako na nung kayo ay naging financial investigator sa AMLA, meron din ibang posisyon na financial analyst? Tama po ba yan?

1341
06:20:03,460 --> 06:20:04,900
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes po, iba pong grupo yan.

1342
06:20:05,100 --> 06:20:11,240
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: So ang trabaho ng financial investigator ay mag-investiga ng money laundering cases.

1343
06:20:11,520 --> 06:20:12,160
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Tama po.

1344
06:20:13,750 --> 06:20:16,870
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Ano po ang trabaho ng financial analyst?

1345
06:20:17,210 --> 06:20:24,790
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Ang financial analyst po, they receive, they analyze, and disseminate financial intelligence. So magkaiba po ang intelligence sa investigation.

1346
06:20:25,290 --> 06:20:41,480
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: So tama po ba ang statement na it is the financial analyst who examine and analyze CTRs and STRs, covered transactions and suspicious transactions, not the... Financial Investigator.

1347
06:20:41,760 --> 06:20:42,320
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Correct, Your Honor.

1348
06:20:42,700 --> 06:20:44,000
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: No more questions, Your Honor.

1349
06:20:44,600 --> 06:20:46,020
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you, Honorable Chel.

1350
06:20:46,020 --> 06:20:47,240
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Just a short manifestation, Your Honor.

1351
06:20:47,500 --> 06:20:49,840
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Yes, what is the manifestation of Atty. Vinluan?

1352
06:20:50,260 --> 06:21:04,820
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Considering, Your Honor, that there have been a lengthy debate on the credentials also, we just want to express, Your Honor, our gratitude to the witness for attending and for taking the time off from his family and just testifying today. That will be all.

1353
06:21:04,940 --> 06:21:07,580
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Of course, but you're not yet done, Attorney Rainer.

1354
06:21:08,720 --> 06:21:19,090
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: We still have some interjections from Senator Judges. Senator Judge Raffy Tulfo is recognized. First interjection. You have two minutes, sir. You may proceed when you're ready. Thereafter, Senator Judge Erwin.

1355
06:21:27,330 --> 06:21:39,940
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: For the record, they're exchanging positions. Senator Judge Pangilinan, first. After Senator Judge Raffy. Senator Judge Raffy, you may proceed, sir. You have two minutes.

1356
06:21:41,920 --> 06:21:57,750
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Mr. Expert Witness, the way you are being painted by the defense like you're omniscient. Omniscient, like Omni-witness, like you know everything. Sobrang bilib sila sa'yo, which ako naman may bilib din sa'yo kasi magaling ka na sumagot agad-agad. Tanong ko lang, ano po yung plantilya nyo?

1357
06:21:58,050 --> 06:22:01,150
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Bank Officer 2 position po nung akwita sa AMLA.

1358
06:22:01,210 --> 06:22:03,250
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Correct. Hindi pa entry-level position niya?

1359
06:22:03,310 --> 06:22:03,610
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes po.

1360
06:22:03,950 --> 06:22:09,190
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Good. At meron pa ng Bank Officer 3, Attorney 3, Attorney 4. And yet hindi ka na-promote?

1361
06:22:09,860 --> 06:22:10,520
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Hindi po.

1362
06:22:10,520 --> 06:22:10,960
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Sa 3 or 4?

1363
06:22:11,220 --> 06:22:13,120
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes po. For that brief statement.

1364
06:22:14,560 --> 06:22:16,760
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Why were you not promoted? Ba't hindi ka na-promote?

1365
06:22:17,150 --> 06:22:36,740
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: I leave it to the discretion po of my superiors, but if I may continue, Your Honor, before leaving, I was offered a higher position. Now, out of delicadesa, I don't want to make it look like I am bargaining for that position. So I still stick with my decision to leave the service. So, yun po.

1366
06:22:37,280 --> 06:22:43,460
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Actually, after ng bank officer 2, nalipat ka sa office of the executive director, ata, as training staff.

1367
06:22:44,140 --> 06:22:47,870
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Ako po ay... Hineram, kasi may... Pero hindi

1368
06:22:47,870 --> 06:22:48,850
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: promotion yun, tama?

1369
06:22:49,030 --> 06:22:49,930
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Hindi po, hindi po siya promotion.

1370
06:22:50,230 --> 06:22:53,370
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: So, inoperang ka ng promotion, pero tinanggihan mo?

1371
06:22:53,650 --> 06:22:54,450
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Nung ako ay palis na po.

1372
06:22:54,450 --> 06:22:55,810
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Pero tinanggap mo yung last training staff?

1373
06:22:56,610 --> 06:23:00,510
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Kasi po, I have to follow kung ano po ang discretion ng aming executive director.

1374
06:23:00,910 --> 06:23:11,490
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Yeah, so anyway, entry-level position yung plantilya mo when you were sa AMLAC. Now, kanina natanong ko sa'yo kung meron ka na natapos na kaso.

1375
06:23:12,110 --> 06:23:12,770
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor.

1376
06:23:13,050 --> 06:23:16,210
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Sa AMLAC as financial investigator, ilan?

1377
06:23:17,070 --> 06:23:19,710
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Marami po. There are notable cases.

1378
06:23:20,050 --> 06:23:24,630
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Approximately ilan? 20, 50, 60? For that 36,

1379
06:23:24,950 --> 06:23:37,430
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: almost 36 months, almost close to, lahat-lahat po ah. Around almost 80 to 90 cases. Kasi I would assume for each month, marami po nire-refer sa aming kaso.

1380
06:23:37,670 --> 06:23:41,170
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Is that so? So kayo bang elite investigator o cosigner lang kayo?

1381
06:23:41,570 --> 06:23:42,350
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Ano po, sir?

1382
06:23:42,410 --> 06:23:54,670
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Co-signer lang kayo doon sa dokumento na isasumite sa Sandigan Bayan. Co-signer. Kasi alim ka doon, di ba? Magpipirma doon sa report.

1383
06:23:55,230 --> 06:23:57,330
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Marami po kami nagpipirma. So we also sign.

1384
06:23:57,330 --> 06:23:58,050
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Marami ka pipirma.

1385
06:23:58,170 --> 06:23:58,570
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Correct.

1386
06:23:58,750 --> 06:24:00,070
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: So ang tawag sa iyo, co-signer.

1387
06:24:01,030 --> 06:24:03,270
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: If that's the definition you're...

1388
06:24:03,270 --> 06:24:20,660
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Well, yan ang definition ng AMLAC. Sa katulad sa iyo, na hindi ikaw ang lead investigator, you were just part, kumbaga pro forma lang. Kailangan ka mag-sign dahil kasama ka sa team. So hindi ka talaga ang pinaka-main investigator, hindi talaga nag-initiate sa'yo yung pagbuo ng kaso.

1389
06:24:20,760 --> 06:24:21,380
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Meron po.

1390
06:24:21,680 --> 06:24:31,380
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Kaya nga, mga kasama mo. Kasi otherwise, ikaw yung pinaka-main. Ikaw ay kasama lamang doon as co-signer. Hindi ako co-signer po pala.

1391
06:24:31,460 --> 06:24:44,420
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Hindi po. Ako po yung main investigator. May mga kaso po na main investigator or kapag kukompleks ang kaso, Team ho kayo. Para if not available yung isa, mayroon ho magte-testify na isa pa.

1392
06:24:45,130 --> 06:24:55,170
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Kaya nga. But in some cases, lumilitaw na co-signer ka. Hindi ka talaga... Kung meron man yung sinasabi mo na ikaw ay lead investigator, ilan yun?

1393
06:24:56,400 --> 06:25:00,100
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Hindi ko na ho mag... Hindi ho ako nag-inventory... And

1394
06:25:00,100 --> 06:25:08,460
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: mapapanindigan mo yun kung magbibigna certification ng AMLAC na kinokontra po yung sinasabi mo ngayon? Kung re-request ng impeachment court.

1395
06:25:09,110 --> 06:25:10,770
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor. Yes, Your Honor.

1396
06:25:11,520 --> 06:25:59,290
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Okay. And then two points na lang. Kasi sabi mo, inamin mo na first time mo lang makita yung report na pinakita sa screen na sinumite ni Attorney Cabrera, yung isang expert ng prosecution, forensic. Now first time mo lang makita, and yet, kinukontra mo, nire-refute mo yung nasa report without even studied it first, without having it reviewed. And then agad-agad nakakapagbigay ka na agad ng expert opinion mo. Okay, sige. Thank you po. Mr. Presiding Officer.

1397
06:25:59,970 --> 06:26:04,330
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Kindly wrap it up. Senator Judge Raffy, witness will please answer.

1398
06:26:04,790 --> 06:26:08,210
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Yeah, so, di ba? Nag-guess mo yung point ko?

1399
06:26:08,430 --> 06:26:17,430
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor. So, yun po, no? Kahit ho maigsi ang aking naging stint, sa isang tingin ko pa lang po kanina, alam ko na po kung ano yung mga problema.

1400
06:26:17,450 --> 06:26:31,030
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Wow! So sa isang tingin mo pa lang, parang kang supercomputer. Nakikita mo agad, parang kang ChatGPT. Isang kita lang, alam mo na agad kung saan ang mali doon. Without even studying it, without even reading it, without even analyzing it.

1401
06:26:31,310 --> 06:26:32,850
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Hindi ho, I'm not saying na mali yun.

1402
06:26:32,850 --> 06:26:34,110
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Hindi, kasabi mo sa isang kita lang.

1403
06:26:34,350 --> 06:26:38,100
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yung mga problema. Sa kanyang report.

1404
06:26:38,440 --> 06:26:49,480
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: So how can you tell that there's a problem with the report? In fact, you haven't even looked at it for 10 minutes at least. Dito pinakita lang sa'yo, parang seconds lang eh. And then agad-agad, you were able to form an opinion and judgment.

1405
06:26:49,600 --> 06:26:55,020
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Binangga ko na kasi ito, your honor, sa aming normal financial investigation process.

1406
06:26:55,020 --> 06:27:06,180
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Exactly, but still, you have to have at least reviewed the report for let's say 10 minutes, 15 minutes siguro, enough na. Pero kanina, seconds lang ata, wala pang isang minuto. Agad-agad, nakapagbigay ka ng opinion mo.

1407
06:27:06,600 --> 06:27:11,460
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: At saka yung po aking opinion kanina ay binangga ko kung ano yung meron sa batas.

1408
06:27:11,540 --> 06:27:48,730
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: That is correct. Pero still, for you to be an intelligent witness, expert witness that is, you have to study, analyze, do some research doon sa ipinipresenta sa iyo na dokumento na work. Wherein you were asked to give your expert opinion. So how can you give a proper expert opinion to a certain degree in a certain report or document of you not having full knowledge of it by way of having at least reviewed it, having at least analyzed it? Yan lang sa akin.

1409
06:27:48,990 --> 06:27:56,810
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Correct, Your Honor. I agree po that if you will be doing a full-blown analysis, it takes time.

1410
06:27:57,020 --> 06:27:57,800
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: It takes time.

1411
06:27:57,840 --> 06:27:58,700
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Kanina ho kasi guided.

1412
06:27:58,940 --> 06:28:00,560
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Hindi lang segundo, tama?

1413
06:28:00,620 --> 06:28:15,020
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Opo, guided ho kasi kanina yung naging analysis, tinuro ho sa akin yung mga items. So guided din ho yung aking, I'm not discounting the entire report, just the portion shown to me.

1414
06:28:15,240 --> 06:28:26,300
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Right. Yung sa portion na yun, like you said, isang tingin mo lang agad-agad, alam mo na kung saan, kung ano yung mali doon. Because of your being an expert Bank Officer Two sa AMLC.

1415
06:28:26,460 --> 06:28:35,360
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: I'm not saying that I'm an expert, your honor. I'm again applying as an AML practitioner, my experience.

1416
06:28:35,500 --> 06:29:13,280
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Kasi sir, nirefute mo, binabangga mo ang isang expert witness na si Atty. Cabrera na katulad mo, or I'm sorry, hindi naman kita masyado kilala, na napakalawak yung credentials din. At ikaw sabi mo na respeto mo si Attorney Cabrera, na isang tao na ginagalang mo yung kanyang credentials, kilala mo. Eh, siyempre, hindi mo basta-basta i-refute yung mga binigay niyang report unless kung talagang sure ka na pag-aralan mo siya, na pag-aralan mo yung mga report na binigay niya, at gumawa ka ng malalim na saliksik at research, then only then makapagbigay ka ng expert opinion, siguro, I suppose.

1417
06:29:13,580 --> 06:29:28,210
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: If I may explain, Your Honor, kanina ko kasi, nung pinakita yung mga sa ating PowerPoint presentation, hypothetical po yung mga questions. Again, I mentioned I have no personal knowledge about the report. I cannot give a definite analysis or conclusion.

1418
06:29:29,550 --> 06:29:31,210
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: You cannot give indefinite analysis.

1419
06:29:31,850 --> 06:29:40,370
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: As to his methodology, as to paano po yun. So ang tinanong mo sa akin kanina, hypothetical. So I answered also on hypothetical trials. So

1420
06:29:40,370 --> 06:29:43,070
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: hypothetical yung binigay mo answer because the question was hypothetical.

1421
06:29:43,510 --> 06:29:43,870
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, sir.

1422
06:29:44,010 --> 06:29:54,090
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: So hindi ka talaga very much aware or well knowledgeable doon sa report at hand na pinakita.

1423
06:29:54,250 --> 06:29:56,270
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Kung ano lang po yung napakita, yun lang po.

1424
06:29:56,290 --> 06:29:58,690
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Kung ano lang pinakita, agad-agad nagbigay ka ng iyong opinion.

1425
06:29:59,010 --> 06:30:17,090
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: And there is a high... As much as possible, again, I haven't read the full text. I avoid making conclusions contradicting whatever he did. So kung ano po yung nandoon at ginawang hypothetical yun, again, without discounting other documents, yun lang po ang limitado.

1426
06:30:17,270 --> 06:30:18,550
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Kindly wind up, Senator Judge Raffy.

1427
06:30:18,550 --> 06:30:23,670
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Maraming salamat po sa iyong pasensya, Mr. Witness. Thank you. Thank you po, Mr. Presiding Officer.

1428
06:30:23,950 --> 06:30:28,390
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you, Senator Judge Raffy. Senator Judge Kiko is recognized. You may proceed, sir. You have two minutes when you're ready.

1429
06:30:33,070 --> 06:30:35,130
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Magandang hapon, Mr. Witness.

1430
06:30:35,450 --> 06:30:36,170
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Good afternoon, Your Honor.

1431
06:30:36,490 --> 06:30:41,620
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Kanina nabanggit mo na wala kang political affiliation. Tama?

1432
06:30:42,620 --> 06:30:43,440
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: None, Your Honor.

1433
06:30:43,580 --> 06:30:49,140
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: In fact, sabi mo the last time hindi ka bumoto nga since 2019. Tama?

1434
06:30:49,420 --> 06:30:54,540
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Hindi po. Mga sirkomstansya po hindi ako pinayagang makaboto.

1435
06:30:54,840 --> 06:31:00,360
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Pero si Atty. Edward Gialogo is your law firm partner.

1436
06:31:01,100 --> 06:31:07,580
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: When I left the service, 2018 up to 2021.

1437
06:31:08,640 --> 06:31:10,400
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: So, he was your law firm partner?

1438
06:31:10,840 --> 06:31:11,420
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor.

1439
06:31:11,620 --> 06:31:14,600
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: So, you are aware? So, ngayon hindi na?

1440
06:31:15,520 --> 06:31:19,600
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Starting 2021 po. When I started the consulting firm, hindi na po.

1441
06:31:19,800 --> 06:31:31,150
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Okay. So, are you aware na si Atty. Gialogo, a lawyer for the Duterte Youth Party List?

1442
06:31:31,790 --> 06:31:46,970
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Well, I have no personal knowledge but could be. Because ang naging practice ho niya, election practice, after ho naming mag-part ways, medyo hindi ho kami nag-uusap for years. Ngayon lang ho kami nag-uusap.

1443
06:31:47,130 --> 06:31:48,430
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: So hindi mo alam?

1444
06:31:48,630 --> 06:31:50,590
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Hindi ko po alam kung ano man yung...

1445
06:31:50,590 --> 06:31:53,570
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Na naging counsel siya ng Duterte Youth.

1446
06:31:53,810 --> 06:31:56,450
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Opo. Possible po kasi ang practice talaga niya is election.

1447
06:31:56,690 --> 06:31:58,490
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Pero hindi mo nga alam. Possible lang.

1448
06:32:01,230 --> 06:32:06,770
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: May information from legal circles. How long have you known Atty. Gialogo?

1449
06:32:07,010 --> 06:32:11,410
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Kami po ay magkaibigan from law school days pa sa San Beda College.

1450
06:32:12,410 --> 06:32:24,500
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: May information from legal circles and pati na rin sa Facebook na si Atty. Gialogo supported the campaign of the previous president. Are you aware?

1451
06:32:25,380 --> 06:32:29,000
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Again, after 2021, Your Honor, wala na kaming communication.

1452
06:32:30,000 --> 06:32:41,020
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Yes, pero we're talking about 2016. 2016. Sabi niyo matagal na kayong magkakilala. So hindi mo alam kung sinuportahan niya?

1453
06:32:41,180 --> 06:32:45,040
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, your honor. It's his personal matters na po.

1454
06:32:47,280 --> 06:32:55,740
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Curious. Sabi mo 2019 hindi ka bumoto. Since 2019. Sino binoto mo noong 2016 sa presidential election?

1455
06:32:57,270 --> 06:32:58,930
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: 2016. I

1456
06:32:58,930 --> 06:32:59,670
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: mean, you're under oath.

1457
06:33:02,510 --> 06:33:03,070
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: 2016.

1458
06:33:06,140 --> 06:33:07,280
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Nakaboto pa ba ako noon?

1459
06:33:07,440 --> 06:33:08,200
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Presidential election.

1460
06:33:08,700 --> 06:33:10,940
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: I'm just recalling your honor if I voted.

1461
06:33:12,540 --> 06:33:14,640
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Okay. So you cannot recall?

1462
06:33:17,250 --> 06:33:18,270
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Long time ago.

1463
06:33:18,790 --> 06:33:26,450
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: It's okay. Kung hindi mo alam, hindi mo alam. Okay. I'll go to another point.

1464
06:33:30,170 --> 06:33:44,580
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Sabi niyo na kanina nung tinatanong ka sa direct examination, sabi mo, mahirap. Pero kaya gumawa ng forensic report sa loob ng two weeks. You said that, no?

1465
06:33:44,720 --> 06:33:45,120
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, po.

1466
06:33:45,640 --> 06:33:53,460
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Okay, so two weeks na pag-aaral o pagbabuo ng forensic report, mahirap pero kaya. Pero dalawang linggo, tama?

1467
06:33:54,170 --> 06:33:54,850
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, sir.

1468
06:33:54,970 --> 06:34:00,090
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Okay. Pero kanina rin sinabi mo, nakita mo ka agad, alam mo na.

1469
06:34:01,900 --> 06:34:11,460
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: So, parang... Mahirap gumawa ng forensic report, pero pagka nakita mo yung portion ng forensic report, agad-agad alam mo na. Tama?

1470
06:34:12,560 --> 06:34:20,940
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Kanina po, may mga tanong lang na hypothetical. It's not about the full report po.

1471
06:34:21,550 --> 06:34:25,110
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Yes. And therefore, pag hypothetical, kaya mong sagutin.

1472
06:34:25,290 --> 06:34:27,290
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Kasi po, themed lang. Limited ang scope.

1473
06:34:27,290 --> 06:34:48,310
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: So what is the probative value of your testimony if you answer hypothetically? In an impeachment trial wherein we look at the evidence and we determine the law necessary or applicable based on the evidence. What is the probative value of your testimony?

1474
06:34:48,810 --> 06:34:56,730
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: I was called upon, Your Honor, to testify on AML standards, how financial investigation is usually conducted. So dun lang po.

1475
06:34:56,950 --> 06:35:13,710
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Okay. You also said in your commentary kanina na... You are able to provide legal opinion or you can analyze whether or not an act is within the bounds of the law. Tama? Sabi mo kanina?

1476
06:35:14,190 --> 06:35:16,410
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, I just rely po on the law.

1477
06:35:17,030 --> 06:35:21,690
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: But how will you know if it is within the bounds of the law if you don't know the facts?

1478
06:35:27,890 --> 06:35:30,290
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Well, the question, Your Honor?

1479
06:35:30,290 --> 06:35:30,630
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Yes.

1480
06:35:30,790 --> 06:35:37,090
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Again, the question propounded ay limited lang po doon sa mga hypothetical questions.

1481
06:35:37,090 --> 06:36:16,580
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: I hope you understand, ikaw eh nag law school, pareho tayo nag law school, sanay tayo sa recitation, hindi ba? Di ba pag nagre-recite tayo, kailangan we apply the law based on the facts, hindi ba? Pag sinabi ng ating professor, tinawag tayo sa recitation at sinabi sa atin, what is the law, recite the case of people versus etc. Pwede mo bang sabihin dun sa professor? Professor, hindi ko po nabasa yung case, yung decision, pero I can give my comments. Pagdaganon, anong grade mo?

1482
06:36:18,390 --> 06:36:19,130
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Bagsak po.

1483
06:36:19,250 --> 06:36:33,710
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Well, again, in fairness to the witness, he's admitted that his manifestations are all hypothetical. And therefore, we should be guided accordingly. No other questions?

1484
06:36:34,520 --> 06:36:36,640
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you. Senator Judge Erwin Tulfo is recognized.

1485
06:36:43,480 --> 06:36:47,140
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Ah, palit talaga. Senator Riza is recognized then.

1486
06:36:50,370 --> 06:36:51,910
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: You may proceed, ma'am. You have two minutes.

1487
06:37:01,480 --> 06:37:05,940
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Salamat, Mr. Presiding Officer. At magandang hapon muli, Atty. Dela Fuente. Good

1488
06:37:05,940 --> 06:37:07,520
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: afternoon, ma'am. Good afternoon, sir.

1489
06:37:08,920 --> 06:37:12,740
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Napanggit niyo po kanina na consultant kayo ng CESA.

1490
06:37:14,450 --> 06:37:24,140
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Nakatawag pansin yun po sa akin dahil marami po nagsasabi na... Doon sa CESA, unang ipinanganak ang POGO.

1491
06:37:26,190 --> 06:37:30,710
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Tapos trainer din po kayo sa PAGCOR para sa casino sector.

1492
06:37:33,580 --> 06:37:52,670
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Regulatory compliance po ang expertise nyo. So tama po ba na ibig sabihin tinuturuan nyo po yung mga kumpanya ang mga dapat nilang gawin para makaiwas sa investigasyon at makaiwas din sa liability. Tama po ba yun?

1493
06:37:52,910 --> 06:38:16,920
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Hindi. Mag-cooperate with the investigation. At yun po ang natin. These are law-abiding entities. We only deal with registered covered persons po. Kasi sila na din po ang mga ngailangan ng ganitong suporta. So, again, hindi para makaligtas sa investigation. Mag-comply if there is an investigation.

1494
06:38:19,690 --> 06:38:21,590
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Be aware of their AML obligations.

1495
06:38:22,580 --> 06:38:53,820
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Sige po, pag-usapan natin ng konti pa itong mga registered covered persons, itong mga law-abiding entities. At any point po ba, nagkaroon po ba kayo ng kliyente na gambling firms? o POGO. Hindi nyo po kailangan banggitin kung sino po ah, kung nagkaroon. Para lang mas malinawan po tayo in relation sa inyong work experience. Nagkaroon po ba ng POGO or online gambling firms na mga kliyente? Sa

1496
06:38:53,820 --> 06:39:06,220
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: PAGCORP po, yes po. Yung mga covered persons po nila because may AML requirements po sila. So, training kasama po yun at saka paggawa po ng mga manuals, risk assessment.

1497
06:39:07,610 --> 06:39:12,510
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Okay. So sa PAGCOR, nagkaroon po kayo ng POGO na kliyente?

1498
06:39:13,640 --> 06:39:15,460
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: During those times, yes, Your Honor.

1499
06:39:15,540 --> 06:39:22,980
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: And nagkaroon din ba kayo sa PAGCOR ng gambling firms na kliyente? Online gambling firms na kliyente?

1500
06:39:23,700 --> 06:39:26,940
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: If they are covered by AMS, yes, Your Honor.

1501
06:39:31,100 --> 06:39:43,060
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Sabi niyo rin po kanina, ang AMLAC lamang ang pwedeng mag-imbestiga ng money laundering. Pero tama po ba na sa ngayon, hindi na po kayo parte ng AMLAC?

1502
06:39:43,260 --> 06:39:43,760
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Correct, Your Honor.

1503
06:39:45,020 --> 06:39:56,720
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: And then, so, ibig sabihin, hindi nyo na po masasabi ngayon kung nagkaroon o hindi nagkaroon ng mga krimen sa kasong pinag-uusapan dito?

1504
06:39:56,940 --> 06:39:58,600
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Correct, Your Honor. I am in the private sector.

1505
06:39:58,920 --> 06:40:01,020
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Yes, nasa private sector na po kayo.

1506
06:40:03,840 --> 06:40:20,840
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Alam nyo po ba kung meron na pong naibigay na lehitimong paliwanag ang Cale88 dun sa mga covered transaction reports at suspicious transaction reports na ipinadala sa AMLOC. Would you know?

1507
06:40:21,100 --> 06:40:22,100
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Know, Your Honor.

1508
06:40:23,970 --> 06:40:56,620
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Pero, sige, medyo may pagka-hypothetical din. Pero, kumpara sa ibang kumpanya na medyo parehong size ng Cale88. Masasabi niyo po bang unusual itong total of wrapping up Mr. Presiding Officer? Masasabi niyo po bang unusual itong total of 757 CTRs at STRs na may halagang 1,254,736,297 pesos and 8 centavos?

1509
06:40:56,820 --> 06:40:58,880
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Kung ito po ay suspicious or unusual?

1510
06:40:59,220 --> 06:41:08,930
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Kung unusual po ba yung ganyang karaming 757 na CTRs? CTRs at STRs total. Sa kasing laking kumpanya tulad ng Cale88.

1511
06:41:09,410 --> 06:41:27,970
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Well, ang makakapag-determine po niya ay ang AML sila kung ito ay suspicious. Again, pag sinabi ko kasing suspicious, it doesn't mean that directly merong unlawful activity agad. This is still subject to further checking or further validation. It invites scrutiny.

1512
06:41:28,950 --> 06:41:50,970
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Pero kumpara dun sa... Walumpu o siyam na pong kasong hinawakan nyo dati nung panahon nyo sa AMLOC. I'm sure meron din kasing laki na kumpanya tulad sa Cale88. Usual po ba na more than 700 plus yung CTRs at STRs? Or usually mas kaunti sa kasing laking kumpanya tulad ng Cale88?

1513
06:41:50,970 --> 06:41:54,310
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Nakakita na po ako na mas marami pa. Kumpanyang mas marami pa,

1514
06:41:54,350 --> 06:41:56,070
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: 'Di hamak, ang kanilang combined

1515
06:41:56,070 --> 06:41:57,630
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: CTRs and STRs.

1516
06:41:57,980 --> 06:42:02,200
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Okay. Mga ilan dun sa 80 or 90 cases yung may mas marami pa?

1517
06:42:02,480 --> 06:42:03,360
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Libo po. Libo po yung iba.

1518
06:42:03,600 --> 06:42:08,520
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Ah, hindi po. Dun sa 80 or 90 cases na hinawakan nyo nung panahon nyo sa AMLOC?

1519
06:42:08,560 --> 06:42:09,780
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Ah, hindi ko na malaman.

1520
06:42:09,780 --> 06:42:13,980
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Ilan sa kanila may mas marami sa 700 plus CTRs at STRs?

1521
06:42:14,720 --> 06:42:21,730
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Pag mga corporations po kasi normally ganyan. Kasi... Very malikot ho ang kanilang financial transactions.

1522
06:42:22,370 --> 06:42:23,570
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Lahat nung 80 at 90 na yun?

1523
06:42:23,570 --> 06:42:25,030
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Hindi po. Not 100%.

1524
06:42:25,030 --> 06:42:27,270
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Or mga 8 or 9 nila? Or ilan?

1525
06:42:27,390 --> 06:42:30,390
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Safe po siguro. We can say 30% of that.

1526
06:42:30,810 --> 06:42:44,750
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: 30%. So, ibig sabihin, ang Cale88 ay nagkaroon ng mas maraming CTRs at STRs total ng mga 70%. At least dun sa mga kasong hinawakan nyo nung panahon nyo sa anglap.

1527
06:42:44,770 --> 06:42:50,990
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Baligtad po. May mas mga korporasyon pa pong mas marami doon sa nabanggit na numero.

1528
06:42:51,070 --> 06:42:55,570
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: So 30% ay mas konti ang number?

1529
06:42:56,790 --> 06:42:58,470
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Libo po. Iyon sinabi ko, libo.

1530
06:42:59,110 --> 06:43:04,190
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Ilan po ang may mas marami sa 700 plus? 30% o 70%?

1531
06:43:04,450 --> 06:43:07,270
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Sa akin pong mga nahawakan, umabot hanggang libo.

1532
06:43:08,860 --> 06:43:10,100
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Mga 30% po siguro.

1533
06:43:10,180 --> 06:43:14,880
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Kaya nga po. So 30% ang mas marami na CTRs at STRs.

1534
06:43:14,880 --> 06:43:17,820
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Opo, ang benchmark po natin si yung company po na yun.

1535
06:43:17,820 --> 06:43:22,240
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: So mas maraming CTRs at STRs ang Cale88 sa 70% na hinawakan.

1536
06:43:22,260 --> 06:43:26,720
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Kasi kung pag korporasyon po, napakadami po talagang in and out transactions. That's normal.

1537
06:43:26,900 --> 06:43:36,440
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: And lastly po, sa official records din ng Cale88, taon-taon itong diumanong lugi, dalawa lang diumanong empleyado.

1538
06:43:36,440 --> 06:44:12,490
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: At 208 million pesos lamang di umano ang idineklarang benta. Pero ayon sa AMLAC, halos 776 million pesos ang flagged as covered or suspicious sa nagpumasok na pera at 319 million pesos dyan galing sa China. So sa mga bank account nitong ipinakita sa Korte, Wala pang 400,000 pesos ang natitira sa katapusan ng bawat taon. Lastly po, Atty. Dela Fuente, hindi po ba yan posibleng mga red flags?

1539
06:44:13,090 --> 06:44:23,490
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, these are red flags po that merit maimbestigahan po, scrutiny review. But again, red flags po are not direct evidence of wrongdoing.

1540
06:44:24,570 --> 06:44:28,330
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Marami salamat, Atty. Dela Fuente. Salamat po, Mr. Presiding Officer. Thank

1541
06:44:28,330 --> 06:44:30,990
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: you. For the third time, Sen. Judge Erwin Tulfo.

1542
06:44:43,760 --> 06:44:46,600
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Maraming salamat po, Ginoong Presiding Officer.

1543
06:44:48,620 --> 06:44:58,810
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Mr. Witness, kanina po natanong kayo tungkol sa Constitution natin at ang inyong mga pananawhingil dito. Ano po? At sinagot nyo naman.

1544
06:45:01,010 --> 06:45:08,430
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Tutal, natanong po kayo dyan, ano po ang interpretasyon ninyo sa Article 7, Section 13 ng Constitution?

1545
06:45:12,360 --> 06:45:24,700
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Ito po yung Pangulo at Vice Presidente, hindi paaring kumuha ng ibang trabaho o mag-aari ng mga negosyo. Ano po ang interpretation niyo po dyan?

1546
06:45:25,040 --> 06:45:41,060
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Well, we apply verbal legis, the plain meaning of the law, Your Honor. Kung ano po ang nakasulat doon, kung may pagbabawal, yun po. But again, it's up to the impeachment court. Leave it to the wisdom of the impeachment court, how they will interpret.

1547
06:45:42,180 --> 06:45:48,760
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: No, I'm asking you as a lawyer, sir, and as an accountant, how do you interpret this?

1548
06:45:48,760 --> 06:45:52,180
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Well, we apply po verbally the plain meaning of the law.

1549
06:45:52,260 --> 06:45:59,940
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: So, hindi pwede po silang dalawa at kanilang mga cabinet secretaries and assistants na mag-ari ng negosyo. Tama po ba?

1550
06:46:00,120 --> 06:46:03,320
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yan po ay aking humble personal opinion.

1551
06:46:03,560 --> 06:46:35,860
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: That's your personal opinion. Very good. So, sa SEC po, hindi inamin ni VP Sara Ang negosyo niya, ito pong Cale88, o part owner siya. Sa SAL-N niya, nilagay niya po ito. So, anong dokumento po ang paniniwalaan natin kayo ho bilang investigador? Hindi mo ba tinicheck niyo rin ang SEC at saka SAL-N ng isang government official?

1552
06:46:36,480 --> 06:46:39,820
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Correct, Your Honor. If there's an ongoing investigation, lahat ho yan.

1553
06:46:40,100 --> 06:47:00,150
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Okay. I-check SEC, SALN. Kung magkaiba po, sino ang paniniwalaan niyo? Meron dito, sabi sa SEC, hindi siya bahagi ng kumpanya na yan. Pero sa SALEN po sabi niya, hindi, meron akong hold dyan sa company na yan. Sino ang paniniwalaan mo bilang investigador?

1554
06:47:00,390 --> 06:47:06,630
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Bilang investigador, dapat neutral muna ang iyong pananaw. Ihintayin mo kung saan ka dadalhin ng ebidensya.

1555
06:47:07,250 --> 06:47:07,810
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: So

1556
06:47:07,810 --> 06:47:29,670
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: you don't take sides. Para walang prejudice, walang bias. So you gather as much evidence as possible. Kaya sa ating AMLA may compulsive process. Bank inquiry. You interview the witnesses. You do on-sites. And then you prepare your report. So magtitilt ho ang report whether for or against the accused kung ano ho ang mas mabigat na ebidensya.

1557
06:47:29,970 --> 06:47:53,320
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Okay, panghuling katanungan na lamang ginaong witness. Doon po sa nabanggit ho ninyo, sa inyong pananaw, Yung interpretation po ninyo sa Article 7, Section 13, bawal po ang mga matataas na opisyal natin, ang Pangulo, Vice Presidente, Cabinet Secretaries, etc., na mag-ari o maging bahagi ng isang negosyo. Tama po?

1558
06:47:53,800 --> 06:47:54,560
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor.

1559
06:47:54,920 --> 06:48:07,800
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Okay. So, hingin ko lang po ang inyong pananaw din at this point. Totale, natanong mo kayo ilang beses kanina at magaling po kayo sumagot. Sa tingin mo ba may nalabag na sa konstitusyon ang Vice Presidente?

1560
06:48:08,540 --> 06:48:16,620
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Ito, Your Honor, is a question of law. Again, I leave it to the wisdom of the Honorable Impeachment Court to decide if meron o wala.

1561
06:48:17,440 --> 06:48:21,420
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Maraming salamat po ginoong testigo. Mr. Presiding Officer. Thank you.

1562
06:48:21,420 --> 06:48:25,380
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Senator Judge Erwin. Senator Judge Joel Villanueva is recognized. You may proceed, sir. You have two minutes.

1563
06:48:28,842 --> 06:48:36,760
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Thank you, sir, Presiding Officer. Thank you, Mr. President. Just a few questions to Attorney Rainer.

1564
06:48:38,810 --> 06:49:05,870
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Chair din po ako ng Committee on Banks dito sa Senado and we look at how MLC uses financial records to understand the purpose of a transaction. From your experience po as an AMLC investigator, when bank records show that a company paid an individual, what can you verify from the check and the bank entries and what other records would you examine to determine why the company made the payment?

1565
06:49:07,990 --> 06:49:20,450
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Number one po, ang question, is it out of the profile ng company that would merit scrutiny? Misan po kasi it is explainable, there is a contractual obligation, etc.

1566
06:49:21,350 --> 06:49:36,850
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Halimbawa po, para mas klaro, halimbawa po a company says it was returning an earlier investment, how would you verify the original contribution, the amount still owed, and whether the payment was actually applied against that balance?

1567
06:49:37,960 --> 06:49:59,660
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Well, number one, you check po yung kanilang SEC records. You request for certified copies ng kanilang GIS to determine the holdings. So, i-compile niyo po yan. SEC records, if there is a private contract between the company and that individual, you compile them if there is legal basis for that returned money.

1568
06:50:00,000 --> 06:50:06,920
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Pag-return po ng money, pwede po ba niyo i-differentiate sa akin return on capital versus return of capital?

1569
06:50:08,280 --> 06:50:20,370
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Return of capital, binabalik ang puhunan. Ito ay hindi considered income. Return on capital, ito ay tubo, kita.

1570
06:50:20,890 --> 06:50:37,570
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Ngayon kung ang return of capital na sinasabi niyo binalik yung puhunan, let's say 48,000 lang ang puhunan, pero ang binalik ay 2,142,000, masasabi niyo na po ba ito ngayon na return on capital?

1571
06:50:38,730 --> 06:50:43,090
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Again, this is, again, limited, this is hypothetical based on that.

1572
06:50:43,090 --> 06:50:45,770
Sen. Joel Villanueva: I'm trying to find out.

1573
06:50:45,990 --> 06:50:53,130
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: 48 po ang capital pero ang binalik ay more than 2 .1 million.

1574
06:50:54,980 --> 06:50:57,540
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Ang tanong po ay is it a return of?

1575
06:50:57,920 --> 06:51:16,690
Sen. Joel Villanueva: That's why I'm asking the difference between return of capital and return on capital because you mentioned a while ago if it is return of capital. Return of capital, it only means binabalik yung puhunan. Pero ang puhunan ay 48,000 lang. So, di ba naging return on capital na po ito?

1576
06:51:16,890 --> 06:51:26,870
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: So, ang tanong po, this can be explained. Possibly po itong nag-accrue na dividendo, hindi niya kiniklaim ang kanyang dividendo. Again, we are...

1577
06:51:26,870 --> 06:51:30,550
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Ang claim po kasi walang dividendo na nilabas.

1578
06:51:30,590 --> 06:51:33,190
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: So, it merits scrutiny po.

1579
06:51:34,730 --> 06:51:38,550
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yung aking nabigay na teorya ay isa lamang but again we have to test this.

1580
06:51:38,690 --> 06:51:57,350
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Thank you. And just to be more, to be clarified on this, if payments continue after the recorded capital balance has been fully paid or fully repaid, what records would you look for to determine the basis for the later payments if it is return of capital?

1581
06:51:57,810 --> 06:52:13,310
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Now, based on that hypothetical scenario, Your Honor, I will check if this is a sort of compensation. Compensation po. Baka sweldo po ito. Hindi na in the capacity of a shareholder but capacity of an employee or officer. Isa po yan.

1582
06:52:13,410 --> 06:52:14,930
Sen. Joel Villanueva: And it becomes an income?

1583
06:52:16,840 --> 06:52:25,880
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Yeah. Thank you for that. Attorney, gusto kong tanungin itong... So

1584
06:52:33,270 --> 06:53:05,380
Sen. Joel Villanueva: suppose a company explains that credits to its bank accounts came from... It's regular export business. From an investigator standpoint, paano po ninyo biniverify yun? And what would you compare in the bank records and the company's records, company's books, para po ma-establish who made the payment, which sale or shipment it covered, and whether the company had already recorded the sale before the money came in?

1585
06:53:05,620 --> 06:53:27,920
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Number one, sir, yung invoices. Suppliers' invoices, contractual agreements, bill of lading, warehouse receipts. So that would verify if there's really an economic transaction that transpired. So ito kasi ay dokumentong pang-komersyo. So ito ay dokumentado.

1586
06:53:28,630 --> 06:54:00,820
Sen. Joel Villanueva: At kung yung kumpanya po nag-presenta ng BOI or FDA registrations and evidence of participation in trade fairs, What further records would you look for to connect a particular remittance to an actual sale? Kasi nga po diba sabi ng Section 3 B.1.1 concerns the purpose of or economic justification of the particular transaction. I'm sure you are very much aware of that.

1587
06:54:01,360 --> 06:54:07,440
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor. So normally yung kontrata po behind the transaction should be intact.

1588
06:54:09,380 --> 06:54:18,420
Sen. Joel Villanueva: At para humalaman kung bayad po talaga, for example, sa export sale, aling shipment at aling invoice ang tinutukoy.

1589
06:54:18,540 --> 06:54:19,180
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes po.

1590
06:54:19,240 --> 06:54:19,860
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Tama po ba?

1591
06:54:19,960 --> 06:54:30,020
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: It can be verified. Lalo na kung ito ay may export or import, meron hong record yan ng ating gobyerno for the goods that really went in and out.

1592
06:54:30,280 --> 06:54:35,140
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Sige po. Salamat, Mr. Witness. I'll just do the round two, Mr. President. Thank you.

1593
06:54:35,460 --> 06:54:40,180
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: The Senate President is recognized. You have two minutes, sir. You may proceed when you're ready. Thank you,

1594
06:54:40,220 --> 06:54:42,900
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Mr. Presiding Officer. Good afternoon, Atty. De La Fuente.

1595
06:54:43,180 --> 06:54:44,340
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Good afternoon, Your Honor.

1596
06:54:44,500 --> 06:54:48,480
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Dahil kayo ay expert witness sa AMLOC, I'll focus on AMLOC.

1597
06:54:50,080 --> 06:55:31,850
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Tinitignan ko itong report ng AMLOC na sinamit dito sa impeachment. At between 2009, ito yung mga transactions ni VP Sara. So nagsubmit sila sa amin per year yung volume at yung value ng transactions from 2007 all the way to 2025. So nakita ko dito from 2009 to 2013, 2.7 billion pesos ang naging transaction out of the 3.9 billion pesos.

1598
06:55:34,380 --> 06:56:01,720
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Just a few years. 2009, 700 million. 2010, 648 million. 2011, 597 million. Ngayon, pinasubmit rin sa amin yung taxable income or net taxable income net of tax ng BIR. At lumalabas sa 2009, 600,000. 2010, 700,000. 2011.

1599
06:56:03,330 --> 06:56:17,840
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: 1 million. So malayong malayo. Malayong malayo. So ganitong mga data na sinabit sa amin, hindi ko inimbento ito, sinabit ito sa amin. Ano ang analysis nyo dito?

1600
06:56:18,480 --> 06:56:55,350
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Well, yan po ay, it would merit further investigation, Your Honor. Iyan po mag-trigger ng other compulsory processes like freeze order, bank inquiry. So that we can dig into the details. Makita sa statement of accounts the actual deposit slips, withdrawal slips. Yung conclusion natin ay magkakaroon tayo ng conclusion if we get those documents. We gather those documents. As much as possible, no conclusion is being made. We only make the conclusions after exhausting all the legal remedies.

1601
06:56:56,100 --> 06:57:03,200
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: So in other words, based on your experience, kailangan ito further investigation and application of a freeze order kaagad?

1602
06:57:04,040 --> 06:57:06,920
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yan po sa normal case and bank inquiry.

1603
06:57:08,020 --> 06:57:27,600
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Okay. And base sa sinabi nyo, ito bang mga ganito ay tingin nyo highly unusual, malaking red flag? Ano ang personal assessment nyo dito sa ganitong data?

1604
06:57:28,420 --> 06:57:37,370
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Again, sinubmit ito sa amin. Hindi ko inimbento ito. So based on your analysis, how can you describe these differences?

1605
06:57:37,890 --> 06:58:15,890
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Ang nagde-determine, Your Honor, kung yan ay suspicious or irregular ay yung mga covered persons po natin. Ibabato nila yan sa AMLC for further checking. Si AMLC naman, sila po kasi nakakakita. They can scan. Other STRs, CTRs submitted by other covered persons. So sila ho yung magdidikit-dikit, bubuuin ho nila yung puzzle and check if they can make a picture out of it. Doon naman ho malalaman kung meron talagang, it merits further investigation or kung wala naman, move on to other cases.

1606
06:58:15,890 --> 06:58:36,280
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Ano pa bang kailangan dokumentong hingin? Dahil meron ng, from the BIR, net, income net of tax. What else ang kailangan pa? Dahil may income side ka na, andun na lahat yun. Compensation income, business income. So ano pa bang information ang kailangan para for the investigation?

1607
06:58:36,720 --> 06:58:41,100
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: I think, Your Honor, the bank records. The source documents.

1608
06:58:43,150 --> 06:59:06,570
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Dun yung malalaman, sino ang pinuntahan, kaninong nagpunta ang pera, ano ang transaction codes. Kasi ang CTRs and STRs, these are just snapshots. Hindi nyo nakikita talaga yung in-between na mga nangyayari. So makikita nyo yan, if you dig deeper, makita nyo yan sa bank inquiry. Doon nyo makikita ngayon ang buong picture. Mabubuo na ang kwento.

1609
06:59:07,390 --> 06:59:15,990
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Base rin sa mga bank information, meron rin mga amounts outside of SAL-N.

1610
06:59:17,880 --> 06:59:40,820
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Ang aking focus dito kasi yung source which is yung income. Diyan naman manggagaling yung source. So base, again, nababalik ako dito, my last question is, base dito sa mga information na binigay sa amin ng AMLAC and BIR, do you think itong discrepancy is an impeachable offense?

1611
06:59:42,800 --> 06:59:52,880
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: That, Your Honor, is a question of law and I would defer again to the Honorable Impeachment Court if it is or if it is not an impeachable offense.

1612
06:59:53,260 --> 06:59:54,820
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Thank you, Mr. Presiding Officer.

1613
06:59:57,580 --> 06:59:59,560
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Senator Judge Marcos is recognized.

1614
07:00:03,820 --> 07:00:39,750
Sen. Imee Marcos: Yes, maraming salamat, presiding judge. Pagod na yung witness natin, konting tanong na lang. Okay, so unang-una, what is the evidentiary value of AMLOC reports? Ano ba yung timbang nito? Ano ba yung bigat nito? Yung financial intelligence report tungkol kay VP Sara, talagang ginagamit natin, sabi mo kanina, analytical ang ginamit, analytical judgment. At bahagi pa lamang ito ng case build-up at fact-finding. So hindi pa ito yung kompleto. Tama po ba?

1615
07:00:39,890 --> 07:00:55,400
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor. Under our law, yung susunod hung steps to, yung section 10, 11, and 12, please order bank inquiry. Yun ho yung mas mabusisi na talaga. Evidence gathering and there is a compulsory process. Kaya ho dadaan ito sa Korte.

1616
07:00:55,540 --> 07:01:05,100
Sen. Imee Marcos: Sorry. Kapag financial intel report pa lamang, hindi pa ito ebidensya, kumbaga? Hindi pa napreba ito? Wala pa siyang bigat, kumbaga?

1617
07:01:05,710 --> 07:01:12,750
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: May bigat na po ito but hindi pa siya yung ebidensya. Ito ay clues pa lang. Ituturo ho tayo sa ebidensya.

1618
07:01:12,830 --> 07:01:38,330
Sen. Imee Marcos: Tama. Kasi may direksyon na siyang sinasabi. It expressly advises the recipients to verify information and states that its analytical judgment may be based on only incomplete or fragmentary information. At bilang abogado, would you agree na yung mga media, news articles, mga report na lumalabas sa dyaryo ay hearsay lamang?

1619
07:01:40,130 --> 07:01:47,590
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: It's second-hand information, Your Honor. Kaya dapat maingat din sila sa paglalabas ng information.

1620
07:01:47,730 --> 07:01:51,110
Sen. Imee Marcos: Maingat yung amla, o yung nagbabasa, o yung dyaryo?

1621
07:01:51,150 --> 07:01:52,010
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yung dyaryo po.

1622
07:01:53,490 --> 07:02:43,520
Sen. Imee Marcos: Tama. Maraming palsipikadong report ngayon. Uso yun. Isa pa, napansin ko at nabanggit kanina yung tungkol sa dalawang insurance company na STR na flinag ng AMLA bilang suspicious transaction. Yung isa, July 2019. Yung isa naman, November 2019. Ngayon, ang dahilan na binibigay na flinag ito bilang suspicious ay dahil lumabas daw sa media na naman na ang mga individual at korporasyon may kinalaman sa flood control investigation sa DPWH. Kaya nagkaroon ng suspicious transaction report. Ngayon, pinagtatakahan ko, 2019 to, kailan ba yung flood control issue? Meron na bang flood control noon? Sa pagkaalam mo, wala pa yan.

1623
07:02:44,600 --> 07:02:48,140
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Ang pagkaalam

1624
07:02:48,140 --> 07:03:22,300
Sen. Imee Marcos: ko, hindi ba lumabas lang yan sa zona noong nakaraang taon? So bago-bago pa lang siya. At isa pa, ang tinatanong ko, kung sakasakali lumitaw yung issue ng flood control ng 2025, alimbawa, tapos 2019 ang tinutukoy, meron bang retroactive flagging? May ganun ba? Legal nung panahon na nangyari, baka tapos five years down the line, pinagbawal na. Pwede pong sabihin na suspicious yung nangyari five years ago?

1625
07:03:22,880 --> 07:03:38,020
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Posible, Your Honor. During that time, kasi clueless pa ang ating mga bangko. Wala pa silang kaalaman. From the time they learn of this information, they can backtrack. They can check the records.

1626
07:03:38,910 --> 07:03:44,410
Sen. Imee Marcos: So, it can keep going back? Hanggang 10 years, 15 years, 20 years? Pwede bang ganon?

1627
07:03:44,950 --> 07:03:50,190
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Normally po ang retention, well, yes, yes, Your Honor. Yes, Your Honor.

1628
07:03:50,250 --> 07:03:54,110
Sen. Imee Marcos: So, mayroon retroactive flagging. So, pwede ganon?

1629
07:03:54,230 --> 07:03:59,790
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes po. At dahil ito po ay red flags lang, this is subject to further checking, further scrutiny.

1630
07:04:00,570 --> 07:04:22,530
Sen. Imee Marcos: E paano kung bibili ka ng insurance ngayon na hindi naman na illegal, lihiti mo, pagkatapos five years down the line, sasabihin na bawal na to, hindi ba unfair na sabihin bigla na suspicious transaction yung ginawa mo? Na legal naman sa pagkaalam mo at sa pagkaalam ng lahat, at nasa batas naman at sa regulasyon na wala namang pinagbabawal, biglang magiging illegitimate.

1631
07:04:23,230 --> 07:04:40,770
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Okay lang po yun. Hindi ho siya magmimerit ng agad freezing. Again, suspicious from the word itself. Hindi ho siya criminal transaction report. So, it will only activate checking, verification. Pag sinek at muka naman na... At na-verify, okay na po yun.

1632
07:04:40,850 --> 07:04:41,550
Sen. Imee Marcos: Okay na yan.

1633
07:04:42,750 --> 07:04:49,930
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Kahit retroactive. Yes po, hindi na ho siya magpo-proceed sa ibang mga proseso. Freeze order, bank inquiry for future.

1634
07:04:50,360 --> 07:05:20,060
Sen. Imee Marcos: Isang huling tanong na lang. May in-identify na 4.4 billion labas-pasok sa iba't ibang mga account. Yung aggregate amount, yung suma total nun lahat, pwede bang sabihin na income or accumulated wealth ng tao na may-ari nung account? Yung labas-pasok kahit repeated rollover ng iba't-ibang amount, tapos ito-total mo, yun na ba talaga yung pag-aari at kayamanan nilang buo?

1635
07:05:20,260 --> 07:05:24,540
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Malalaman po ito, Your Honor, sa full financial investigation.

1636
07:05:24,840 --> 07:05:29,320
Sen. Imee Marcos: Kung nagkaroon ng double counting or at saka yung inflow at outflow.

1637
07:05:30,170 --> 07:05:33,490
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Doon na po malalaman yan sa full financial investigation. Pero

1638
07:05:33,490 --> 07:05:39,050
Sen. Imee Marcos: hindi mo pwedeng isumatotal lamang yung lahat ng pumasok, lahat ng lumabas.

1639
07:05:39,070 --> 07:05:39,730
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Correct your honor.

1640
07:05:40,290 --> 07:05:40,810
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Okay,

1641
07:05:40,950 --> 07:05:43,470
Sen. Imee Marcos: those are all my questions. Maraming salamat, attorney.

1642
07:05:43,810 --> 07:05:48,210
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you, Senator Judge Jaime. Senator Judge Villanueva is recognized. You have two minutes, sir. You may proceed when you're ready.

1643
07:05:55,070 --> 07:05:57,030
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Thank you, Sir Presiding Officer.

1644
07:06:01,290 --> 07:06:29,120
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Attorney, Mr. Witness, kanina po binanggit natin kung walang dividends hindi pasok doon sa kumpanya na nagbibigay ng nabanggit niyo po kanina, maaari itong compensation. Pero anong masasabi niyo? Kasi kung compensation, wala nga pong empleyado actually. In fact, 23 and 24, dalawa po yung employees. Anong masasabi niyo dito? Pwede pa rin bang compensation yun o hindi na pwedeng tawaging compensation?

1645
07:06:30,000 --> 07:06:32,860
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Again, ito po ay theoretical lang po, no? Based on that hypothetical.

1646
07:06:33,200 --> 07:06:50,750
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Hindi po. Lahat po nung tinanong ko sa inyo, nangyari po yun. At in fact, binanggit nyo nga po na ito'y papasok na dun sa income. Gusto ko lang malaman dun sa binanggit nyo na ba ari itong compensation. Eh kung compensation, eh wala naman po empleyado. Pwede ho bang gamitin yun as compensation?

1647
07:06:51,630 --> 07:06:54,490
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Pwede ho ang may-ari mismo ang nag-aakas empleyado.

1648
07:06:54,950 --> 07:06:56,510
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Ah kung may-ari po siya?

1649
07:06:56,840 --> 07:07:00,240
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Kung may-ari. Opo. Kasi sila ang nag-work.

1650
07:07:00,340 --> 07:07:30,230
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Lalo na kung yan po ay bagong kumpanya lang. Attorney, base po dun sa dokumentong na isumiti dito sa Korte, nakatanggap po kasi itong... Kale88 ng malalaking halaga ng salapi mula po sa iba't ibang bansa. Kabilang na China, Russia, Ukraine. At sa ilalim po ng Anti-Money Laundering Act at BSP Regulations, ano po ang mga obligasyon ng bangko para tiyakin na legitimate ito at ang mga transaksyong ito ay tugma din dun sa aktwal at nakadiklarang negosyo ng kumpanya?

1651
07:07:30,490 --> 07:08:10,030
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Number one, Your Honor, they have to ask, yung mga bangko natin, what's the purpose for those transactions? Number two, if it will originate from a high-risk jurisdiction, they have to report it. Yan po yung mga triggers. What's the legitimate business purpose? Tapos ititingnan nila, iscreen nila, saan ba ang pinanggalingan ng pera that would merit reporting. Yan po ipapasok sa client and transaction monitoring system ng ating mga bangko. Part of their KYC. Know your client and customer due diligence, CDD.

1652
07:08:10,210 --> 07:09:05,790
Sen. Joel Villanueva: High risk at purpose. Doon po sa forensic report na sinubmitibo dito sa Korte, may approximately 222.62 million pesos. foreign remittances ang Cale88 mula po 2023 to 2025. Ang gusto po natin kasing malinawan eh kung anong verification ang dapat gawin ng mga bangko para matukoy po na consistent ang remittance sa declared business activities ng isang kumpanya. In fact, yung legal basis and I'm sure you know about this section 9 letter A ng RA 9160. Sabi po doon, it provides that covered persons shall establish and record the true identity of their clients. Ang tanong ko po, if a company claims that these are export payments, is that declaration sufficient or should additional verification be required depending on the risks identified and why?

1653
07:09:06,150 --> 07:09:06,890
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Again,

1654
07:09:07,010 --> 07:09:08,010
Sen. Joel Villanueva: self-serving

1655
07:09:08,010 --> 07:09:26,300
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: po yung verbal declarations. Normally po, it is backed by documents. Kung ganun kalalaki ang pera, Ito po ay dapat may dokumento, may paper trail. So, normally po, kontrata to support the remittance in or out of the bank.

1656
07:09:26,760 --> 07:10:12,430
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Maraming pong salamat. Last na po, Atty. Dela Puente. Noong din pong hearing natin dito, October 9, nabanggit po na ang Artmen LLC, isa pong kumpanya sa Ukraine na nagpapadala po ng salapi sa KL88. ay naiugnay umano sa isang investigasyon sa ibang bansa tungkol po sa panluloko at money laundering. Sa ilalim po ng mga regulasyon ng AMLC, kapag may ganito pong informasyon, kayo po yung isang eksperto dito tungkol sa isang foreign company na nagpapadala ng salapik, ano po ang karagdagang pagsusuri at karagdagang pagbabantay na dapat gawin ng mga bangko po na tumatanggap ng remittance?

1657
07:10:12,860 --> 07:10:16,520
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Well, number one po, private obligation for them is to report it as suspicious.

1658
07:10:18,880 --> 07:10:52,820
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yun po ang isang immediate obligation ng mga bangko. Number two, ask the client for justifications regarding the transaction. So, depende na po yan sa internal policy ng mga bangko if they will accept the explanation or not. Kasi may mga covered persons po tayo na hindi nila ina-accept, nagkakaroon po ng de-risking, kinuklose nila yung account. Kapag hindi na nila, they can no longer accommodate the risk with that particular client.

1659
07:10:53,060 --> 07:11:09,970
Sen. Joel Villanueva: At kahit po wala pang final conviction, can credible information concerning a foreign criminal... Investigation. Justify enhanced due diligence or suspicious transaction reporting.

1660
07:11:10,470 --> 07:11:12,950
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor. So, it invites scrutiny.

1661
07:11:13,530 --> 07:11:14,470
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Para po?

1662
07:11:14,770 --> 07:11:34,330
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Enhanced due diligence, ibig sabihin, mas maraming dokumentong hihingin, more paperwork. They could delay the transaction, subject to verification. Yun po yung ginagawa natin sa EDD. Bago mag-transact, maraming kailangang senior management approval. Ito po yung mga safeguards na meron ang ating mga bangko bago nila payagamot.

1663
07:11:34,330 --> 07:11:52,210
Sen. Joel Villanueva: When you talk about safeguards, ang legal basis po nito, yung Section 3, B1, 5, and 6 ng AMLA law that provides the transactions deviating from the client's profile for past transactions or related to unlawful activities may be considered suspicious transactions. Is that correct?

1664
07:11:52,210 --> 07:12:01,530
Atty. Rainer P. Dela Fuente: Yes, Your Honor. So doon po natatapos ngayon ang obligasyon ng covered person sa STR. Ang bola po naman ngayon ay napapasa na sa AMLAC. para mag-investiga.

1665
07:12:01,770 --> 07:12:04,830
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Okay. Maraming salamat po for that clarification. Thank you, Mr. Vice President.

1666
07:12:04,830 --> 07:12:06,030
